e skin a protein is secreted from the Endothelial Cells of blood vessels.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:33:22',16,'2026-03-28 01:36:32'),(15852,26,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Adhaerere</em></strong> (L. v.), to cling to, attach to</p><p><strong><em>Adhaesum </em></strong>(past part.), attached<strong> </strong></p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:33:36',16,'2025-01-17 12:59:53'),(15853,26,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Adhaesion</em></strong></p><p>Literally, platelets “attaching together”</p><p><br></p><p><em>comp</em><strong><em>., <u>Adhaes- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ion</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Adhaesum</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>-ion</em> </strong>(suffix), forms noun of action</li></ul>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:33:47',16,'2026-03-28 01:38:10'),(15854,27,15,NULL,'<p>Adrenal</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:34:49',16,'2025-04-26 07:15:04'),(15855,27,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Glands</strong></p><p>Endocrine glands</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:34:57',16,'2026-03-28 01:40:55'),(15856,27,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Suprarenal Glands;</strong> glands superimposed on the kidney; excretes several hormones influencing water homeostasis and the Autonomic Nervous System.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:35:06',16,'2026-03-28 01:41:52'),(15857,27,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards</p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:35:15',NULL,NULL),(15858,27,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenal,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“above the kidney”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp</em><strong><em>., <u>Ad</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>Ren</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-al</u> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ren</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:35:47',16,'2026-03-28 01:43:06'),(15859,28,15,NULL,'<p><strong>&nbsp;Adrenal</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:38:10',16,'2025-04-26 07:14:42'),(15860,28,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Medullary Mechanism,&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Production of Adrenaline, noreadrenaline, neuro-stimuli.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:38:27',16,'2026-03-15 02:41:45'),(15861,28,13,NULL,'<p>Functionally, Adrenal Medulla releases Epinephrine and Norepinephrine during high Sympathetic stimulation to the heart and blood vessels.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:38:36',NULL,NULL),(15862,28,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:38:44',NULL,NULL),(15863,28,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenal,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“above the kidney”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp</em><strong><em>., Ad</em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>Ren</u></em><u> </u></strong><u>+</u><strong><u> </u><em><u>-al</u> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em>Ren</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:38:52',16,'2026-03-28 02:04:02'),(15864,29,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Epinephrine</strong>;  Adrenergic Hormone produced in the Adrenal Gland influence the Sympathetic Autonomic Nervous System; exerts Sympathetic influence to heart rate.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:40:05',16,'2026-03-15 02:38:30'),(15865,29,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:40:13',NULL,NULL),(15866,29,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenaline</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>hormone from the gland at the kidney</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ad</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>Ren</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-al </u></em></strong><em><u>+ </u></em><strong><em><u>-ine</u> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ren</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p><p><strong><em>· -ine </em></strong>(suffix), denotes basic chemical substance</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:40:35',16,'2026-03-28 01:45:19'),(15867,30,15,NULL,'<p>&nbsp;<strong>Adrenergic&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:41:47',44,'2025-03-31 02:36:14'),(15868,30,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Hormones</strong></p><p>Endocrine secretions that prompt organs and other endocrine glands to secrete or act.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:41:54',16,'2026-03-15 02:46:56'),(15869,30,13,NULL,'<p>Collective term for Epinephrine and Norepinephrine, stimulant hormones from Medullary Adrenal Gland that influence Sympathetic, \"fight or flight modes\'\' of the Autonomic Nervous System; Sympathetic influence to the heart rate.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:42:02',16,'2026-03-28 01:53:08'),(15870,30,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney </p><p><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong> (L. n.), work</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:42:11',NULL,NULL),(15871,30,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenergic</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>the work of the Adrenal Gland</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ad</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>Ren</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-erg-</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ren</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erg- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Ergon</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:42:24',44,'2025-03-31 02:40:25'),(15879,32,13,NULL,'<p>The process of blood clotting:<em> </em>when platelets are stimulated by an injury, they form attachments to each other that cause clumping (clotting) of the blood in the site of injury.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:50:53',16,'2025-04-26 07:14:01'),(15880,32,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agglutinare</em></strong> (L. v.), to glue<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Agglutinatum</em></strong> (past part.), glued together;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:51:03',NULL,NULL),(15881,32,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agglutination</em></strong></p><p>metaphorically, “<em>binding together</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em> <u>Agglutinat- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Agglutinatum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em> </strong>(suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:51:13',16,'2026-03-15 03:02:35'),(15882,33,13,NULL,'<p>During the first and subsequent exposure to a <em>“clot-causing antigen protein” s</em>pecific Antibodies are produced in the Plasma, called Agglutinin.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:51:51',NULL,NULL),(15883,33,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agglutinare</em></strong> (L. v.), to glue<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Agglutinatum</em></strong> (past part.), glued together;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:52:00',NULL,NULL),(15884,33,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agglutinin</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “clotting protein”</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>comp., <u>Agglutin- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Agglutinatum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:52:10',44,'2025-03-31 03:07:17'),(15885,34,13,NULL,'<p>Antigens in the RBC plasma that triggers production of <strong><em>Agglutininogen </em></strong>that generates <strong><em>Agglutinin</em></strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:54:08',NULL,NULL),(15887,34,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agglutinare</em></strong> (L. v.), to glue<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Agglutinatum</em></strong> (past part.), glued together</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Genitor</em></strong> (L.&nbsp;n.), father, begetter, producer</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:54:42',44,'2025-03-31 03:10:36'),(15888,34,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agglutininogen</em> </strong></p><p><em>metaphorically,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>production of</em> <em>clotting protein</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Agglutin- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-in </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-gen</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Agglutinatum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., insulin)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-gen</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Genitor</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:54:53',44,'2025-03-31 03:13:20'),(15889,36,13,NULL,'<p>Under magnification Monocytes and Lymphocytes are WBC that appear without granulations, i.e. clear plasma.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:57:13',16,'2025-04-26 07:13:36'),(15890,36,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>An </em></strong>(L. prep.), without</p><p><strong><em>Granulus</em></strong> (L. n.), fine grain, small seed&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Cytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:57:20',NULL,NULL),(15891,36,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Agranulocyte,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>cells without grain</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>A- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Granulo </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-cyte</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A- </em></strong><em>derived from </em><strong><em>An</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Granulus</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-cyte</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:57:30',44,'2025-03-31 03:17:19'),(15892,37,13,NULL,'<p>Albumin is 58% of the suspended plasma protein responsible for Colloid property of the blood necessary for H2O homeostasis between the interstitia and the blood stream.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:58:14',NULL,NULL),(15893,37,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Albus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), white <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:58:23',NULL,NULL),(15894,37,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Albumin</em></strong></p><p>literally, “<em>white protein in plasma</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Album </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Album </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., insulin)<strong> </strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:58:33',44,'2025-03-31 03:21:39'),(15895,38,13,NULL,'<p>Product of the Adrenal Cortex and Zona Glomerulosa that is necessary for H2O / Na- / K+ / H+ homeostasis of blood in circulation</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:59:18',NULL,NULL),(15896,38,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Aldo-</em></strong> (Chem. prefix), dehydrogenated alcohol</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Ester- </em></strong>(Chem. prefix), ethelacetate or dimethylacetate</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:59:25',44,'2025-03-31 03:24:11'),(15897,38,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AldoEsterone</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, Hormone for homeostasis of blood</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp</em><strong><em>., <u>Aldo- </u></em></strong><u>+</u><strong><u> </u><em><u>Ester- </u></em></strong><u>+</u><strong><u> </u><em><u>-one</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Aldo-</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ester-</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-one</em></strong> (Chem. suffix), denotes Ketone</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 01:59:35',16,'2026-03-21 23:44:41'),(15898,39,15,NULL,'<p>&nbsp;<strong>Ameboid&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:00:24',16,'2025-04-26 07:13:11'),(15899,39,13,NULL,'<p>WBC equipped with Cilia, fine hair-like processes, that enable the cells to paddle around like <strong><em>Amoebae</em></strong> to where they are needed during immune defenses.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:00:34',NULL,NULL),(15900,39,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Amoeba</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Amoebae</em></strong>), ciliated, pseudopod single-celled organism</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:00:42',16,'2025-08-09 02:03:02'),(15901,39,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Amoeboid,</em></strong></p><p><em>simile, </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>resembling amoeba</em>”</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>comp., <u>Amoeba + -oid</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Amoeba </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-oid</em></strong> (suffix), forms simile; <em>“resembling”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:00:54',44,'2025-03-31 03:30:26'),(15902,41,13,NULL,'<p>Deficiency in RBC count per 100ml of blood volume; below normal count: 14-18g for men, 12-16g for women</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:03:17',NULL,NULL),(15903,41,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>An</em></strong> (L. prep.), negative sense, against, without</p><p><strong><em>Heme / Haima </em></strong>(Gr. n.), blood</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:03:24',NULL,NULL),(15904,41,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Anemia,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>a condition without blood</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>An </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-em </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;An </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-em </em></strong><em>derived from </em><strong><em>Haima</em></strong>&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ia </em></strong>(suffix), denotes condition, state (ex., Absentia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:03:32',44,'2025-03-31 03:32:47'),(15905,42,13,NULL,'<p>Literally, focal dilation or ballooning of an artery, commonly, in brain and Aorta; a high risk for stroke and internal bleeding&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:04:18',16,'2025-04-26 07:12:44'),(15906,42,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Aneurysma</em></strong> (Gr. n.), dilation, ballooning</p><p>Metaphor for focal swelling of blood vessels</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:04:24',NULL,NULL),(15907,43,9,NULL,'<p><strong>&nbsp;Angina&nbsp;</strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:05:26',44,'2025-03-31 03:36:03'),(15908,43,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pectoris</strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em>“</strong>of the chest”</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:05:34',NULL,NULL),(15909,43,13,NULL,'<p>Acute pain in the chest, with sensation of choking and suffocating caused by stenosis or vasospasm of the Coronary Arteries, compromising blood supply to the myocardia.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:05:42',NULL,NULL),(15910,43,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Angina</em> </strong>(L. n.), choking, strangulation</p><p>metaphorically, <em>“choking pain of the chest”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:05:50',NULL,NULL),(15911,332,13,NULL,'<p>Hormones derived from Angiotensinogen + Renin + Angiotensin Converting Enzyme =&gt; Angiotensin II, a potent vasoconstrictor; constricts veins causing higher peripheral resistance and elevated blood pressure.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:07:19',NULL,NULL),(15912,332,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Angius </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Angii</em></strong>), blood vessel</p><p><strong><em>Tendere </em></strong>(L. v.), to expand, to stretch;</p><p><strong><em>Tensum </em></strong>(past part.), stretched out</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:07:29',NULL,NULL),(15913,332,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AngioTensin,</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>metaphorically, “</em></strong><em>hormone that constricts blood vessels</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Angio- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Tens- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Angius </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tens- </em></strong><em>derived from </em><strong><em>Tensum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:07:40',NULL,NULL),(15914,45,15,NULL,'<p><strong>&nbsp;Angiotensin&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:09:34',44,'2025-03-31 03:45:02'),(15915,45,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Enzyme</strong></p><p>EnZymos, “leaven”, metaphor for the action of yeast, a catalyst</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:09:44',NULL,NULL),(15916,45,13,NULL,'<p>Angio-, pertaining to blood vessels; Enzyme affecting small blood vessels in the lungs to influence blood pressure by Vasoconstriction&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:09:53',44,'2025-03-31 03:46:36'),(15917,45,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Angius </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Angii</em></strong>), blood vessel<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Tendere </em></strong>(L. v.), to expand, to stretch;</p><p><strong><em>Tensum </em></strong>(past part.), stretched out</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:10:03',44,'2025-03-31 03:47:27'),(15918,45,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AngioTensin,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>hormone that constricts blood vessels</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Angio- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Tens- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Angius </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tens- </em></strong><em>derived from </em><strong><em>Tensum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:10:14',44,'2025-03-31 03:48:10'),(15920,46,13,NULL,'<p>Precursor Plasma protein of Angiotensin produced in the liver and activated by the Renin from the kidney.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 02:11:22',NULL,NULL),(15921,46,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Angius </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Angii</em></strong>), blood vessel</p><p><br></p><p><stro