sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bios </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trans</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Forma</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ation </em></strong>(suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:18:04',44,'2025-04-01 02:55:35'),(16088,105,13,NULL,'<p>Heart-beat count below normal, 55-60 BPM</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:18:46',NULL,NULL),(16089,105,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Bradys </em></strong>(Gr. adj.),<strong><em> </em></strong>slow, delayed, tardy</p><p><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), heart</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:18:54',NULL,NULL),(16090,105,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>BradyCardia,</em></strong></p><p><em>literally</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“slow heart”</em></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>comp., <u>Brady- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Cardia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bradys </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cardia</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:19:03',44,'2025-04-01 02:57:20'),(16091,106,13,NULL,'<p>The whitish-translucent part of the plasma after the Formed Elements are spun to the bottom of the test tube.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:19:39',NULL,NULL),(16092,106,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Buffy Coat</strong> (Eng.), white liquid between</p><p>the RBC and the Plasma that seems to act as a “buffer” between the two blood elements</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:19:48',44,'2025-04-01 02:58:30'),(16093,108,13,NULL,'<p>A small tube in the blood pressure cuff of Sphygmomanometer that is attached to the arm against the Brachial Artery for reading blood pressure with a stethoscope.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:20:54',NULL,NULL),(16094,108,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cannula </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Cannulae</em>)</strong>, literally a <em>“small tube”</em></p><p>diminutive form, <strong><em>Canna</em></strong> (L. n.), tube</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:21:00',NULL,NULL),(16095,109,13,NULL,'<p>The thinnest of all blood vessels that function as O2/nutrients - CO2/waste exchange between the circulatory system and the interstitial environment.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:21:44',16,'2025-04-26 06:32:11'),(16096,109,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Capilla</em></strong>), classically, <em>strand of hair</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:21:53',NULL,NULL),(16097,109,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillary,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>hair-thin</em>” blood vessels;</p><p>functions like hair</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Capill- + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Capilla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:22:01',44,'2025-04-01 03:00:05'),(16098,110,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Capillary&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:24:11',16,'2025-04-26 06:31:46'),(16099,110,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Action</strong></p><p>Observe how water behave in wet hair</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:24:19',NULL,NULL),(16100,110,13,NULL,'<p>The O2, CO2, H2O, and nutrient gradient difference between the interstice and the bed of Arterioles and Venioles drives Capillary Action between the 2 compartments.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:24:26',NULL,NULL),(16101,110,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Capilla</em></strong>), classically, “<em>strand of hair”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:24:33',NULL,NULL),(16102,110,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillary,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, functions like</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>hair-thin</em>” blood vessels</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Capill- + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Capilla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:24:43',44,'2025-04-01 03:01:02'),(16103,111,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Capillary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:26:03',44,'2025-04-01 03:01:28'),(16104,111,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Exchange </strong></p><p>O2 for CO2; cellular nutrients for cellular waste</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:26:10',NULL,NULL),(16105,111,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., DIFFUSION; Exchange of chemical substances between the inside and outside environment of Capillary vessels is driven by osmotic pressure and concentration gradient between the external and internal membrane.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:26:17',NULL,NULL),(16106,111,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Capilla</em></strong>), classically,<em> hair</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:26:26',NULL,NULL),(16107,111,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillary,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, functions like “hair-thin</em>” blood vessels</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Capill- + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Capilla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:26:34',44,'2025-04-01 03:01:55'),(16108,112,13,NULL,'<p>Transports of CO2 by the Globin part of the Hemoglobin during Venous Return of deoxygenated blood for exchange with Oxygen in the lungs.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:27:06',NULL,NULL),(16109,112,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Carbo</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Carbones</em></strong>), charcoal,</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Carbon in basic form</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><br></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Amino </em></strong>(Biochemistry), 20 Amino Acids</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">building blocks of protein; nitrogen groups</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:27:17',44,'2025-04-01 03:03:24'),(16110,112,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Carb- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Amino </u></em></strong><u>+ HEMOGLOBIN</u></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Carbo</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;   <strong><em>Amino&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:27:36',NULL,NULL),(16111,113,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cardiac&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:28:45',16,'2025-04-26 06:31:18'),(16112,113,7,NULL,'<p><strong> Apex </strong></p><p>The peak of the heart is at the bottom of an inverted triangle</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:28:55',44,'2025-04-01 03:07:09'),(16113,113,13,NULL,'<p>The Apex of the heart is the inferiorly directed conical part; the base is rounded and positioned superiorly.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:29:04',NULL,NULL),(16114,113,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cardia </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-akos</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-akos</em></strong> (Gr. adj. suffix), pertaining to . . .&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:29:14',NULL,NULL),(16115,114,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cardiac&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:30:35',16,'2025-04-26 06:30:50'),(16116,114,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Auricles</strong></p><p>The atria resemble the Outer ears</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:30:43',44,'2025-04-01 03:09:18'),(16117,114,13,NULL,'<p>Literally, “<em>small ear</em>” of the heart; Atria were once termed Auricles due to the ear-like projections from the heart.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:30:50',NULL,NULL),(16118,114,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cardia </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-akos</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-akos</em></strong> (Gr. adj. suffix), pertaining to . . .&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:30:59',NULL,NULL),(16119,115,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cardiac</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:32:14',16,'2025-04-26 06:30:25'),(16120,115,13,NULL,'<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Like an inverted pyramid, the base of the heart is the wide, rounded superior end.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:32:23',NULL,NULL),(16121,115,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p><strong><em>-akos</em></strong> (Gr. adj. suffix), pertaining to. .&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:32:30',NULL,NULL),(16122,116,15,NULL,'<p>Cardiac&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:33:07',NULL,NULL),(16123,116,13,NULL,'<p>Cyclical pumping of the heart starts with the onset of Ventricular Systole (contraction-ejection) and ends with Diastole (relaxation-refilling), allowing the Ventricles to be Refilled from the Atria for the next systole.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:33:14',NULL,NULL),(16124,116,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p><strong><em>-akos</em></strong> (Gr. adj. suffix), pertaining to. . .</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:33:22',NULL,NULL),(16125,118,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cardiac&nbsp;</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:37:21',44,'2025-04-01 03:11:34'),(16126,118,13,NULL,'<p>Specialized heart muscles (Myocardia) have innate, self-generated Action Potential originating from the SA Node; they are, however, influenced by Sympathetic Autonomic Nervous System during increased demand for oxygen</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:37:29',NULL,NULL),(16127,118,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p><strong><em>-akos</em></strong> (Gr. adj. suffix), pertaining to. . .</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:37:37',NULL,NULL),(16128,119,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cardiac</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:38:10',16,'2025-04-26 06:30:01'),(16129,119,13,NULL,'<p>Venous Return of de-oxygenated blood from the Heart Muscles are collected in the Coronary Sinus and the Vena Cava, then <em>“poured”</em> into the right Atria</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:38:18',NULL,NULL),(16130,119,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p><strong><em>-akos</em></strong> (Gr. adj. suffix), pertaining to. . .</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:38:25',NULL,NULL),(16131,120,13,NULL,'<p>Baroreceptors located in the Medulla Oblongata contains CARDIO ACCELERATORY CENTER via Sensory neurons of Glossopharygeal Nerve (CN IX) and Vagus Nerve (CN X); they are influenced by Sympathetic A.N.S. and CARDIO INHIBITORY CENTER, where Sensory stimuli are integrated for<span style=\"color: red;\"> </span>systemic control.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:38:55',NULL,NULL),(16132,120,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), the heart</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Regulatus</em></strong> (L. adj.), ruled</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:39:01',NULL,NULL),(16133,120,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>CardioRegulatory</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“ruling the heart”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">&nbsp;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cardio- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Regulat- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ory</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cardia</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Regulatus</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ory</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:39:09',44,'2025-04-01 03:13:49'),(16134,121,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cardiovascular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:41:21',44,'2025-04-01 03:21:43'),(16135,121,13,NULL,'<p>The closed system of blood Circulation: comprised of heart, Arteries and veins. - Arteries for distribution of oxygenated blood to the interstice; Venous Return of de-oxygenated blood from the interstice back to the Right Atrium ànd Right Ventricle, to the lungs for oxygenation; back to the Left Atrium ànd Left Ventricle, and pumped to the Aorta; now the blood is oxygenated again for recirculation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:41:28',44,'2025-04-01 03:24:34'),(16136,121,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cardia </em></strong>(Gr. n.), heart</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Vasculus </em></strong>(L. n.), small vessel; </p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Diminutive form, <strong><em>Vasum</em></strong> (L. n.), vessel</p><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:41:37',NULL,NULL),(16137,121,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>CardioVascular</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><em>Literally</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>heart-blood vessels”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>comp., <u>Cardio- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Vascul- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ar</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cardia </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Vasculus</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:41:45',44,'2025-04-01 03:24:59'),(16138,123,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Carotid&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:44:54',16,'2025-04-26 06:29:15'),(16139,123,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Artery</strong></p><p>A-, “<em>Away from the heart</em>”</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:45:01',44,'2025-04-01 03:26:37'),(16140,123,13,NULL,'<p>Carotid Arteries originate from the Aortic Arch to the neck and head; the junction where common carotid divides into internal and external carotid arteries contain baroreceptors that monitor blood pressure to the brain.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:45:10',NULL,NULL),(16141,123,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Carotikos / Karotikos</em></strong> (Gr. n. coined by Galen), </p><p>metaphorically, “<em>soporific stupor</em>”</p><p>(compression of both arteries causes fainting)</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:45:18',NULL,NULL),(16142,124,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Carotid</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:46:16',16,'2025-04-26 06:28:48'),(16143,124,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Sinus Reflex</strong></p><p>Baroceptor-feedback within the carotid sinus</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:46:26',NULL,NULL),(16144,124,13,NULL,'<p>Blood Pressure in the Carotid Arteries activate the Baroreceptors in the Carotid Sinus at a dangerous level; located in the junction of the Aortic Arch and Carotid Artery.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:46:33',44,'2025-04-01 03:29:36'),(16145,124,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Carotikos / Karotikos</em></strong> (Gr. n. coined by Galen), </p><p>metaphorically, “<em>soporific stupor</em>”</p><p>(compression of both arteries causes fainting)</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:46:45',NULL,NULL),(16146,126,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Celiac</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:47:31',16,'2025-04-26 06:28:23'),(16147,126,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Trunk</strong></p><p>Arterial Trunk gives rise to arterial branches</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:47:42',NULL,NULL),(16148,126,13,NULL,'<p>Arteries originating from the Abdominal Aorta, directly distribute blood into the liver and stomach and spleen</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:47:49',NULL,NULL),(16149,126,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Coeliacus </em></strong>/ <strong><em>Koiliakos</em></strong> (Gr. adj.), pertaining to the bowel; </p><p><strong><em>Coelia </em></strong>/ <strong><em>Koilia</em></strong> (Gr. n), bowel&nbsp;</p><p>literally, “<em>arterial trunk</em> branches <em>to the bowels, liver, spleen</em>”.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:47:58',NULL,NULL),(16150,127,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Central&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:48:27',16,'2025-04-26 06:28:00'),(16151,127,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Veins</strong></p><p>V-, for <em>“<u>Ven</u> aqui”, </em>Come here.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:48:35',44,'2025-04-01 03:31:38'),(16152,127,13,NULL,'<p>The venous network of the Liver Sinusoids collects blood into Central Veins and empty into Hepatic Veins, finally, into the Inferior Vena Cava.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:48:52',NULL,NULL),(16153,127,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Centrus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Centri</em></strong>), center</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:48:58',NULL,NULL),(16154,128,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cephalic&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:52:11',16,'2025-04-26 06:27:36'),(16155,128,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Veins</strong></p><p>V-, for <em>“Ven aqui.”, </em>Come here</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:52:17',44,'2025-04-01 03:33:01'),(16156,128,13,NULL,'<p>Cephalic Veins originate from the upper extremities, conjoin with Axillary Veins to become Subclavian veins, finally, connect to the Superior Vena Cava.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:52:25',NULL,NULL),(16157,128,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cephalus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Cephali</em></strong>), the head, brain&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:52:31',NULL,NULL),(16158,129,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cerebral&nbsp;</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:53:27',16,'2025-04-26 06:27:10'),(16159,129,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Arteries</strong></p><p>A-, <em>“Adios, sangre</em>”, says the heart.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:53:43',44,'2025-04-01 03:34:46'),(16160,129,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cerebrum</em></strong> (L. n.)), brain&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:53:50',NULL,NULL),(16161,130,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cervical</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:54:21',44,'2025-04-01 03:35:19'),(16162,130,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Sympathetic Chain Ganglia,</strong></p><p>Exerts Sympathetic Autonomic influence on the heart</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:54:32',NULL,NULL),(16163,130,13,NULL,'<p>Pre-ganglionic Sympathetic neurons originate from the Spinothoracic region, projecting to the heart as cardiac nerves.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:54:40',NULL,NULL),(16164,130,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cervix</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cervices</em></strong>), neck, or back of the neck</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:54:51',NULL,NULL),(16166,130,12,NULL,'<p>CERVIX – REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM</p><p>CERVICIS</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:56:43',NULL,NULL),(16167,131,13,NULL,'<p>Sensory cells that are stimulated by presence of chemicals; i.e., taste receptors, olfactory receptors, carotid bodies&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:57:07',NULL,NULL),(16168,131,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chemia </em></strong>(Gr. n.), Alchemy&nbsp;<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>Recipire </em></strong>(L. v.), to receive;<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Receptum </em></strong>(past part.), taken, received&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 04:57:20',44,'2025-04-01 03:36:53'),(16169,131,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ChemoReceptor</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>literally, “</em></strong><em>chemical sensors</em>”</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">&nbsp;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Chemo- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Recept- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-or</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb