p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Coll- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-oid </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Colla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-oid</em></strong> (suffix), forms simile: <em>“resembling”</em></p><p><strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:08:10',44,'2025-04-01 03:44:13'),(16198,141,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Conducting</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:10:39',44,'2025-04-01 03:44:44'),(16199,141,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Arteries</strong></p><p>A- for <em>“Adios, blood”</em></p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:10:52',NULL,NULL),(16200,141,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., ELASTIC ARTERIES; elastic property of arteries allows for high pressure circulation to channel blood through the smallest arterioles; blood can be channeled even through the narrowest Capillary Arterioles.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:11:00',NULL,NULL),(16201,141,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cum</em></strong> (L. prep), with, along with</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Ducere </em></strong>(L. v.), to lead; <strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ducens </em></strong>(present. part.), leading&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:11:12',44,'2025-04-01 03:45:18'),(16202,141,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ConDucentes,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“leading with”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>comp., <u>Con- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Ducentes</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Con- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Cum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ducens&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:11:21',44,'2025-04-01 03:45:37'),(16203,142,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Conjugated</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:12:07',44,'2025-04-01 03:46:20'),(16204,142,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Bilirubin,</strong></p><p>Bile in circulation, Free Bilirubin</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:12:21',NULL,NULL),(16205,142,13,NULL,'<p>When RBC is recycled, the Heme component is converted into Bili<u>verdin</u> (green due to oxidation), then into Bilir<u>ubin</u> (red); in the blood stream it is called Free Bilirubin, in the liver it is <u>Conjugated</u> with Glucoronic Acid and becomes bile again.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:12:29',NULL,NULL),(16206,142,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Conjungere</em></strong> (L. v.), to join, unite with<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:12:37',NULL,NULL),(16207,142,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em><u>Conjungated</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Literally, </em></strong><em>“joined”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>comp., <u>Conjung- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ated</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><strong><em>Conjungere</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ated</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:12:46',NULL,NULL),(16208,143,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cordae</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:13:21',16,'2025-04-26 06:26:15'),(16209,143,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Tendinae</strong></p><p>Stretchable, tendinous</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:13:35',NULL,NULL),(16210,143,13,NULL,'<p>Metaphorically, “<em>stretchable</em> <em>strings</em>”; tendinous cords that support and strengthen the Atrio-Ventricular valves during snap-close to prevent backflow of the blood&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 05:13:43',NULL,NULL),(16211,143,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Corda</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cordae</em></strong>), strings of string instrument