<em>the peak</em>”&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:22:26',NULL,NULL),(16315,175,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>epi-</em></strong></p><p><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:22:33',44,'2025-04-02 01:16:50'),(16316,176,13,NULL,'<p>Thin Serous outer membrane of the heart; wraps the heart, protects from trauma. (Mid layer- Myocardium; Inner layer- Endocardium)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:23:23',16,'2025-04-26 06:17:08'),(16317,176,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p><p><strong><em>Cardium</em></strong> (Gr. n.), heart<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:23:30',NULL,NULL),(16318,176,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EpiCardium</em></strong></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>above the heart</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Epi- + Cardium</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Epi- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Apices</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cardium</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:23:37',44,'2025-04-02 01:18:32'),(16319,177,13,NULL,'<p>Juvenile RBC from Stem cells become Pro-Erythroblasts, subsequently, become </p><p>Early-Erythroblasts, finally, Erythroblasts.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:27:28',NULL,NULL),(16320,177,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Blastos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), sprout, bud, germinal cells</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:27:36',NULL,NULL),(16321,177,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ErythroBlastos</em></strong></p><p><em>literally</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>germinal red blood cell”</em></p><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + -Blastos + -osis</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erythros </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Blastos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:27:47',44,'2025-04-02 01:20:21'),(16322,178,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Erythroblastosis</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:28:28',44,'2025-04-02 01:21:15'),(16323,178,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Fetalis,</strong></p><p>Translation: <em>“of the fetus”</em></p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:28:43',NULL,NULL),(16324,178,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., Hemolytic Disease of the Newborn; the mother develops Antibodies against an incompatible blood type with the baby; a high risk of system wide coagulation in the mother’s circulation&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:28:51',NULL,NULL),(16325,178,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Blastos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), sprout, bud, germinal cells</p><p><br></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:28:58',NULL,NULL),(16326,178,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ErythroBlastosis ,</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Literally, </em></strong><em>“disorder with the RBC of the young”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">&nbsp;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + -Blastos + -osis</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erythros </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Blastos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-osis</em></strong> (suffix), denotes pathology</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:29:07',NULL,NULL),(16327,179,13,NULL,'<p>Erythroblasts develop into Erythrocytes, mature Red Blood Cells</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:30:05',NULL,NULL),(16328,179,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cytos </em></strong>/ <strong><em>Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:30:11',NULL,NULL),(16329,179,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>ErythroCytes</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><em>Literally, </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>Red Cells”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>comp., <u>Erythro- + -Cytos</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erythros </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Cytos </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-osis</em></strong> (suffix), denotes pathology</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:30:19',44,'2025-04-02 01:22:13'),(16330,180,13,NULL,'<p>Condition of above normal number of RBC causing high blood Viscosity, reduced flow rate, plugged Capillaries, hemolysis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:31:35',NULL,NULL),(16331,180,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cytos </em></strong>/ <strong><em>Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:31:41',NULL,NULL),(16332,180,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Erythrocytosis,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “condition of Red Blood Cells”</em></p><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + -cyto- + -osis</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erythros </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Cytos </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-osis</em></strong> (suffix), denotes pathology</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:31:51',44,'2025-04-02 01:22:42'),(16333,181,13,NULL,'<p>Production of new RBC from Stem cells via action of Erythropoeitin.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:32:40',NULL,NULL),(16334,181,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Poiesis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), production, formation</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:32:47',NULL,NULL),(16335,181,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + Poiesis</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erythros </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Poiesis</em></strong> </p><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:32:56',NULL,NULL),(16336,182,13,NULL,'<p>GlycoProtein produced in the kidney stimulates red bone Marrow to produce pro-erythroblasts when oxygen levels in the blood declines or higher demand for oxygen during athletics or high mountain elevation.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:41:46',44,'2025-04-02 01:24:27'),(16337,182,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Poiesis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), production, formation</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:41:52',NULL,NULL),(16338,182,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ErythroPoietin</em></strong></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>protein for production of RBC</em>”</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">&nbsp;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + Poiet- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Erythros </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Poiet- </em></stron