mpartment.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:47:03',NULL,NULL),(16347,186,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fenestra</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Fenestrae</em></strong>), classically, a window, opening</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:47:10',44,'2025-04-02 01:32:48'),(16348,187,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Fenestrated</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:47:38',16,'2025-04-26 06:16:32'),(16349,187,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Capillaries</strong></p><p>Hair -thin blood vessels</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:47:52',44,'2025-04-02 01:34:20'),(16350,187,13,NULL,'<p>Capillaries with openings for white blood cells to exit from the blood stream into the extra cellular compartment where WBC are needed to fight infection.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:48:00',NULL,NULL),(16351,187,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fenestra</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Fenestrae</em></strong>), classically, a window, opening</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:48:07',44,'2025-04-02 01:35:06'),(16352,187,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fenestratus,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>provided with openings</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Fenestra + -atus</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em> Fenestra</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>&nbsp;-atus</em></strong> (suffix), forms adj.; provided with; Eng., <strong>-ated<em> </em></strong></li></ul>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:48:20',44,'2025-04-02 01:36:28'),(16353,188,13,NULL,'<p>Thread-like protein that form into woven sheets for clotting and sealing the wound from further bleeding.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:49:07',16,'2025-04-26 06:15:53'),(16354,188,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fiber</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Fibri</em></strong>), classically,  filament, thread</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:49:13',44,'2025-04-02 01:37:47'),(16355,188,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fibrin</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>fibrous protein</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Fibri- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fibri</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)<strong> </strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:49:26',44,'2025-04-02 01:38:19'),(16356,189,13,NULL,'<p>Precursor to the production of Fibrin</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:49:59',NULL,NULL),(16357,189,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fiber</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Fibri</em></strong>), classically, a filament, thread</p><p><strong><em>Genitor</em></strong> (L. n.), father, begetter, producer</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:50:06',44,'2025-04-02 01:39:05'),(16358,189,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fibrinogen,</em></strong></p><p>Literally, producer of <strong><em>“</em></strong><em>fibrous protein</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Fibri + -in + -gen</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fibri</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)<strong> </strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-gen </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Genitor</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:50:16',44,'2025-04-02 01:40:18'),(16359,190,13,NULL,'<p>Action that dissolves clots after complete healing has taken place by Hydrolyzing the Fibrin by the action of Plasmin.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:51:18',NULL,NULL),(16360,190,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fiber</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Fibri</em></strong>), classically,  a filament, thread</p><p><strong><em>Lysis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lytes</em></strong>), destruction, dissolution&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:51:29',44,'2025-04-02 01:41:04'),(16361,190,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>FibrinoLysis,</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>breakdown of fibrous protein</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Fibrin + Lysis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fibrin</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Lysis</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:51:36',44,'2025-04-02 01:41:25'),(16362,191,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Fibula</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:52:03',44,'2025-04-02 01:42:09'),(16363,191,13,NULL,'<p>Stabilizing bone of the Tibial Bone, spans the full length of the Tibia, superiorly anchored to the lateral aspect of the tibial plateau, distally, to the lateral Talus</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:52:11',NULL,NULL),(16364,191,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fibula</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, clasp of a belt</p><p>(bone’s semblance to the tongue of a buckle, brooch, or safety pin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:52:17',44,'2025-04-02 01:46:37'),(16365,191,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Fibula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fibula</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:52:26',NULL,NULL),(16366,192,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Fibular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:53:20',44,'2025-04-02 01:44:31'),(16367,192,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., PERONEAL (VEIN / ARTERY); in a downward direction, the Iliac Artery branches into External and Internal Iliac Artery; the external becomes Fibular Artery, becomes Dorsalis Pedis, and finally, turns into medial, lateral Plantar Vein /Artery.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:53:27',NULL,NULL),(16368,192,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fibula</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, clasp of a belt</p><p>(bone’s semblance to the tongue of a buckle, brooch, or safety pin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:53:34',44,'2025-04-02 01:46:01'),(16369,192,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Fibula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fibula</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:53:43',NULL,NULL),(16370,194,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Fluid</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:54:39',44,'2025-04-02 01:47:18'),(16371,194,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Shift Mechanism,</strong></p><p>Water shifts from circulation to the interstitial compartment during dehydration</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:54:51',44,'2025-04-02 01:48:03'),(16372,194,13,NULL,'<p>When dehydration occurs blood pressure on capillary walls increase forcing fluid to exit into the interstice, reducing blood volume.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:54:59',NULL,NULL),(16373,194,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fluere</em></strong> (L. v.), to flow;</p><p><strong><em>Fluitum </em></strong>(past part.), flowed</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:55:17',NULL,NULL),(16374,195,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Foramen</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:55:53',44,'2025-04-02 01:48:44'),(16375,195,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Ovale</strong></p><p>Elongated round, egg-shape</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:56:01',NULL,NULL),(16376,195,13,NULL,'<p>The fetal heart has an opening, \"small over hole\', through the atrial septum between the right and left Atria allowing the mother’s blood circulation to by-pass oxygenation; the fetal Ventricles works in conjunction with the mother’s circulation.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:56:10',44,'2025-04-02 01:51:36'),(16377,195,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Foramen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Foramines</em></strong>), a small opening, hole</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:56:18',44,'2025-04-02 01:52:33'),(16378,196,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Foramen</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:56:51',44,'2025-04-02 01:53:06'),(16379,196,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Magnum</strong></p><p>Great; the biggest foramen of all</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:57:05',NULL,NULL),(16380,196,13,NULL,'<p>The “<em>Great Hole</em>” of the Occiput for exit of the Spinal Cord from the Cranium to the Spinal Canal.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:57:12',NULL,NULL),(16381,196,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Foramen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Foramines</em></strong>), a small opening, hole</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:57:19',NULL,NULL),(16382,197,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Fossa</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:58:10',44,'2025-04-02 01:53:47'),(16383,197,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Ovalis</strong></p><p>Elongated round, egg-shaped</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:58:17',NULL,NULL),(16384,197,13,NULL,'<p>Figuratively, an “<em>oblong depression.</em>” The Fossa Ovalis in the right Atrium is the site of the former <strong><em>Foramen Ovale</em></strong> for the mother’s circulation that sealed up soon after birth.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:58:24',NULL,NULL),(16385,197,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fossa </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Fossae</em></strong>), classically, ditch, trench, hole, or pit in the ground</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:58:34',44,'2025-04-02 01:54:47'),(16386,198,13,NULL,'<p>The Hemoglobin Chemical structure is composed of four Globin (polypeptide) chain, each one tied to one Heme for O2 / CO2 transport.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:59:07',NULL,NULL),(16387,198,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Globus</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, sphere, ball</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:59:14',44,'2025-04-02 01:55:44'),(16388,198,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Globin</em></strong></p><p>figuratively, “<em>spherical protein</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Glob- + -in</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Globus</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)</li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 06:59:28',44,'2025-04-02 01:57:06'),(16389,199,13,NULL,'<p>Comprises 38% of plasma protein, antibodies and complements, as part of the immune system and transport molecules.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-16 07:00:06',NULL,NULL),(16390,199,8,NULL,'<p><st