right Ventricle flow into Left and Right Pulmonary Artery saturated with CO2 and diffuse into the lungs to exchange CO2 for O2 and returns to the Left Atrium via the Left and Right Pulmonary Vein.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:32:06',NULL,NULL),(16754,315,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pulmon + -ary</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Pulmon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pulmones</em></strong>), lung</li><li><strong><em>-ary </em></strong>(suffix), denotes function/site</li></ul>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:32:14',44,'2025-04-07 02:02:39'),(16755,316,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pulmonary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:32:48',44,'2025-04-07 02:04:37'),(16756,316,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Valve</strong></p><p>Metaphor:<strong><em> Valvus</em></strong> (L. n.) classically, <em>“double door”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:32:58',NULL,NULL),(16757,316,13,NULL,'<p>Valve located at the opening of right Ventricle prevents blood from back flowing from the Pulmonary Trunk to the Ventricle</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:33:05',NULL,NULL),(16758,316,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pulmon + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Pulmon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pulmones</em></strong>), lung</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ary </em></strong>(suffix), denotes function/site</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:33:13',NULL,NULL),(16759,317,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pulmonary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:35:49',44,'2025-04-07 02:05:26'),(16760,317,13,NULL,'<p>Oxygenated blood is pumped back to the left Atrium via Left and Right PULMONARY VEINS</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:35:55',NULL,NULL),(16761,317,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pulmon + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Pulmon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pulmones</em></strong>), lung</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ary </em></strong>(ending), denotes function/site</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:36:02',NULL,NULL),(16762,318,13,NULL,'<p>The ejection of blood from the left ventricle into the Aorta produces a pressure wave that travels rapidly, palpable by pulse along the arterial system (Radial, Carotid, Temporal, Brachial, Dorsalis Pedis . . .)&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:36:29',NULL,NULL),(16763,318,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pulsus</em></strong> (L. n.), drumming sound</p><p>metaphorically,<em> “rapid double beat,</em>”</p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\">derived from:</em><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Pellere </em></strong>(L. v.), to beat a drum;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Pulsum </em></strong>(past part.), beaten like a drum&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:36:39',44,'2025-04-07 02:08:19'),(16764,319,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pulse</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:37:02',44,'2025-04-07 02:08:46'),(16765,319,13,NULL,'<p>Difference between systolic and diastolic pressure (BP, 120/80 --&gt; 120 - 80 = pp 40 mm. Hg.)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:37:12',NULL,NULL),(16766,319,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pulsus</em></strong> (L. n.), drumming sound</p><p>metaphorically,<em> “rapid double beat,</em>”</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:37:27',NULL,NULL),(16767,320,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Purkinje</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:38:15',44,'2025-04-07 02:09:51'),(16768,320,13,NULL,'<p>Action Potentials to the myocardia<em> </em>originate from the Sino-Atrial Node, whence Purkinje nerve fibers course along the Cardiac Septum innervating the heart up to the Apex of the heart, then divides into left and right Bundle Branches at the Cardiac Apex.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:38:22',NULL,NULL),(16769,320,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Purkinje</em></strong>, Jan Evangelista, Czech Physiologist, </p><p>discovered the self-initiating, self-regulating </p><p>cardiac nerve fibers</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:38:28',NULL,NULL),(