g>(L. v.), to bend, curve;<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Flexum </em></strong>(past part.), bent, curved&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:46:40',NULL,NULL),(16788,326,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReFlex</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “response back again”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Re- + Flex</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> (prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong>·</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Flexum </em></strong>(past part.), bent, curved; </p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:46:55',NULL,NULL),(16789,328,13,NULL,'<p>having the property to adjust correctly, automatically, to mechanical stimuli, such as, changes in temperature, H2O and chemical homeostasis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:48:38',NULL,NULL),(16790,328,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>Flectere </em></strong>(L. v.), to bend, curve<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Flexum </em></strong>(past part.), bent, curved;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:48:51',NULL,NULL),(16791,328,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReFlex, </em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“response back again”</em> </p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Re- + Flex + -ivus</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Flexum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ive</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; function</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:49:03',NULL,NULL),(16792,330,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Renin</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:50:16',44,'2025-04-07 02:24:58'),(16793,330,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Angiotensin,</strong></p><p>Angiotensin II, a potent vasoconstrictor; constricts veins causing higher peripheral resistance and elevated blood pressure.</p><p><strong>Aldosterone,</strong></p><p>Product of the Adrenal Cortex and Zona Glomerulosa that is necessary for H2O / Na- / K+ / H+ homeostasis.</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:50:31',NULL,NULL),(16794,330,13,NULL,'<p>Regulate kidney function in a system-wide control of blood volume by urine output via Vasodilation and Constriction; the physiological cascade involves a satellite of organs in a series of hormonal influences.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:50:40',NULL,NULL),(16796,330,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:51:23',NULL,NULL),(16797,330,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ren + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ren</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:51:30',44,'2025-04-07 02:25:34'),(16798,331,13,NULL,'<p>produced by Juxtaglomerular apparatus to influence production of Angiotensin for Vasocontrol.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:52:21',NULL,NULL),(16799,331,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:52:26',NULL,NULL),(16800,331,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ren + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ren</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:52:34',NULL,NULL),(16801,334,13,NULL,'<p>Process of re-setting muscle Membrane Resting Membrane Potential level back to --72 / -90 mV. (Think of it as re-cocking your pistol for another fire.)</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:56:24',NULL,NULL),(16802,334,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Polaris </em></strong>(L. adj.), opposite ends of pole (+/-)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:56:31',NULL,NULL),(16803,334,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>RePolarisation</em></strong> </p><p>literally, “<em>resetting negative charge”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Re- + Polaris + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Polaris </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ation</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:56:45',NULL,NULL),(16804,335,13,NULL,'<p>Mathematical expression of flow:&nbsp;P1 – P2/R = stable under outside influence</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:57:15',NULL,NULL),(16805,335,8,NULL,'<p><em style=\"--tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / .5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ;\">Resistare </em><span style=\"background-color: rgb(241 245 249 / var(--tw-bg-opacity)); color: rgb(39 39 42 / var(--tw-text-opacity));\">(L. v.), to withstand oncoming force&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><em>Resistans </em></strong>(present part.), standing up to opposite force;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:57:29',44,'2025-04-07 02:28:36'),(16806,336,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Resting</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:58:19',44,'2025-04-07 02:29:05'),(16807,336,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Membrane Potential,</strong></p><p>Muscle Cell Membrane generates and stores potential electrical energy to drive Action Potential, ultimately, for the purpose of muscle contraction.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:58:33',44,'2025-04-07 02:30:08'),(16808,336,13,NULL,'<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Metaphorically, muscle membrane has stored potential energy “<em>resting</em>” at -70/-90 mV, standing ready for an Action Potential to initiate depolarization, i.e., muscle contraction.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:58:41',NULL,NULL),(16809,336,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Resting</strong> (Eng. v.), sense of waiting for a stimulus for action</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:58:51',NULL,NULL),(16810,337,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Reticulo-</strong>, prefix</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:59:14',NULL,NULL),(16811,337,13,NULL,'<p>Generally, a meshwork of fine fibers, tendinous Tissue, lymphoid tissue that forms a net like Filtration or connective tissue.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:59:21',NULL,NULL),(16812,337,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), classically, <em>small fishing net</em></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Retices</em></strong>), net<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 02:59:34',44,'2025-04-07 02:31:17'),(16813,338,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reticular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:00:03',44,'2025-04-07 02:31:40'),(16814,338,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Fibers,</strong></p><p>Literally,<em> “threads”</em>; add strength to cartilaginous tissue</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:00:12',16,'2024-12-18 03:00:54'),(16815,338,13,NULL,'<p>Generally, a meshwork of fine fibers, tendinous tissue, lymphoid tissue that forms a net like Filtration or connective tissue.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:00:22',NULL,NULL),(16816,338,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), small fishing net</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Retices</em></strong>), net</p><p>metaphor for fibrous screen formed by proteins</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:00:30',NULL,NULL),(16817,338,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Reticula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Reticula</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:00:39',NULL,NULL),(16818,339,13,NULL,'<p>Immature RBC which are directly produced from the bone marrow whose nucleus have been extruded; the remaining network of Reticulum is visible in the cytoplasm.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:01:32',NULL,NULL),(16819,339,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), small fishing net</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Retices</em></strong>), net<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:01:42',NULL,NULL),(16820,339,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulo- + -cytes</em> </strong></p><p><em>figuratively, </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>Reticular Network of cells</em>”</p><p>metaphor for fibrous screen formed by proteins</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Reticulo- + -cytes</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Reticulum </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cytos</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:07:14',NULL,NULL),(16821,340,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reticuloendothelial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:08:38',44,'2025-04-07 02:32:59'),(16822,340,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Fibers,</strong></p><p>Literally, <em>“threads”</em>; add strength to cartilaginous tissue</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:09:00',NULL,NULL),(16823,340,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of Vascular Endothelium and reticular tissue; Serve as a “net” to filter foreign body in the blood stream.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:09:07',44,'2025-04-07 02:33:39'),(16824,340,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), small fishing net</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Retices</em></strong>), net<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Endo</em></strong> (L. prep), in, inside, into&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Thelium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Thelia</em></strong>), teat, buds, nipple</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:09:18',NULL,NULL),(16825,340,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReticuloEndoThelial,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphor for fibrous screen formed by proteins</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Reticulo- + Endo + Thelia + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Reticulum </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Endo</em></strong> </p><p><strong>·&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Thelia</em></strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;        <em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:09:55',NULL,NULL),(16826,343,15,NULL,'<p>RH</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:11:51',NULL,NULL),(16827,343,13,NULL,'<p>Having Rh, D-antigens, on the membranes of RBC</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:11:58',NULL,NULL),(16828,343,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Rhesus monkey</em></strong>, subject of study for blood typing</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:12:04',NULL,NULL),(16829,344,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Saphenous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:12:34',44,'2025-04-07 02:34:33'),(16830,344,13,NULL,'<p>Two principal visible veins at the posterior aspect of the lower limbs, calves</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:12:42',NULL,NULL),(16831,344,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Saphenus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), visible, superficial, demonstrated</p><p>figuratively, “<em>visible spider veins</em>”</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:12:48',44,'2025-04-07 02:35:09'),(16832,345,13,NULL,'<p>Fluid compartment of the muscle cell containing Organelles, surrounding the nucleus.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:13:22',NULL,NULL),(16833,345,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sarx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Sarces</em></strong>), muscle tissue, flesh</p><p><strong><em>Plasma</em> </strong>(Gr. n.), something molded, formed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:13:29',NULL,NULL),(16834,345,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SarcoPlasm</em></strong>	</p><p><em>Intracellular cells fluid + organelles </em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Sarco- + Plasma + -ic </u></em></strong></p><p>			<strong><em>Sarco- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Sarces</em></strong></p><p>			<strong><em>Plasma</em> </strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:13:54',NULL,NULL),(16835,347,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Semilunar</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:14:53',44,'2025-04-07 02:36:01'),(16836,347,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Valve</strong></p><p>Metaphor: <strong>Valvus</strong> (L. n.), Classically, <em>double-door</em></p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:15:09',NULL,NULL),(16837,347,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., MITRAL VALVE; a.k.a., BICUSPID VALVE; “<em>half-moon</em>” shaped valves in the left chambers of the heart</p><p>(Tricuspid is in the right chambers).</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:15:20',44,'2025-04-07 02:36:44'),(16838,347,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Semis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Semises</em></strong>), half</p><p><strong><em>Luna</em></strong> (plu.., <strong><em>Lunae</em></strong>), a moon&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:15:28',NULL,NULL),(16839,347,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SemiLunar</em></strong></p><p>Metaphor for 2 half- moon valve</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Semi- + Luna + -ar</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>&nbsp;Semi- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Semis</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>&nbsp;Luna</em></strong></li><li><strong><em> -ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</li></ul>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:15:45',44,'2025-04-07 02:37:44'),(16840,349,13,NULL,'<p>Plasma from the blood containing the clotting ingredients and processes; extruded during clot Retraction.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:18:10',NULL,NULL),(16841,349,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Serum</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Sera</em></strong>), watery part of milk, whey</p><p>Metaphor for the clear part of the blood</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:18:17',NULL,NULL),(16842,350,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Serous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:18:49',44,'2025-04-07 02:39:21'),(16843,350,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pericardium</strong></p><p>Around the heart</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:18:57',NULL,NULL),(16844,350,13,NULL,'<p>The exterior protective lining of the heart is a thin transparent, mucoid layer of simple squamous epithelium.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:19:07',NULL,NULL),(16845,350,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Serosus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), watery;</p><p><strong><em>Serum</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Sera</em></strong>), watery part of milk, whey</p><p>Metaphor for the clear part of the blood</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:19:17',44,'2025-04-07 02:39:57'),(16846,351,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sinoatrial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:20:09',44,'2025-04-07 02:40:25'),(16847,351,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Node,</strong></p><p>Inconspicuous bead of tissue seated&nbsp;between the Atria; generates impulses for heartbeat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:20:20',44,'2025-04-07 02:41:50'),(16848,351,13,NULL,'<p>Neural Origin of<em> </em>self-initiating, self-generating Action Potential for heart muscles is located at the junction of the Venae Cavae and Atria.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:20:29',NULL,NULL),(16849,351,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sinus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Sini</em></strong>), an empty bowl, curved surface </p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Atrium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Atria</em></strong>), open part of roof to collect rain water</p><p>Metaphor for blood being “<em>poured”</em> into Atrial chambers</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:20:37',NULL,NULL),(16850,351,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SinoAtrial,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“empty space in the Atria”</em></p><p><em>metaphor for two vessels merging, creating larger vessel </em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sino- + Atria + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sinus </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Atria</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:20:55',44,'2025-04-07 02:43:14'),(16851,352,15,NULL,'<p>Sinosoidal</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:21:28',NULL,NULL),(16852,352,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Capillaries,</strong></p><p>Metaphor: <strong>Capillum</strong> (L. n.), hair; Thinnest blood vessel</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:21:44',NULL,NULL),(16853,352,13,NULL,'<p>Have larger Fenestrae than Fenestrated Capillaries; they occur in Endocrine Glands where large molecules need larger Fenestrae for exit.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:21:56',NULL,NULL),(16854,352,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sinus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Sini</em></strong>), an empty bowl, curved surface</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:22:06',NULL,NULL),(16855,352,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sinusoidal</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“like an open space”</em></p><p><em>metaphor two vessels merge creating larger vesse</em><strong><em>l </em></strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sinus + -oid + -al</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;Sinus</em></strong> </li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-oid</em></strong> (suffix), forms simile; resembling</li><li>&nbsp;<strong><em>-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</li></ul>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:22:33',NULL,NULL),(16856,353,13,NULL,'<p>Large diameter Sinusoidal Capillaries in the liver and bone marrow for large molecules and cells to move easily.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:23:00',NULL,NULL),(16857,353,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sinus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Sini</em></strong>), an empty bowl, curved surface</p><p>metaphor for two vessels merging, creating larger vessel&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:23:07',44,'2025-04-07 02:44:36'),(16858,353,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Sinus + -oid</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sinus </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-oid</em></strong> (suffix), forms simile; resembling . . .&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:23:14',NULL,NULL),(16859,356,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sphincter</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:25:33',44,'2025-04-07 02:45:04'),(16860,356,13,NULL,'<p>Circular muscle that closes an orifice, or a blood Vessel; metaphorically, muscle that “grips”</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:25:41',NULL,NULL),(16861,356,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sphingere </em></strong>(L. v.), to grip; <em>hold tight</em></p><p><strong><em>Sphinctum </em></strong>(past part.), held tight, gripped</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>-or</em></strong><em> </em>(suffix), denotes agent of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:25:50',44,'2025-04-07 02:46:07'),(16862,358,13,NULL,'<p>Measures blood pressure in the Brachial Artery with a Stethoscope by tightening the blood pressure cuff around the arm just above the elbow, slowly releasing the cuff to let the blood flow to register a mercury reading.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:26:33',NULL,NULL),(16863,358,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sphygmos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), throbbing, pulsation, pulse</p><p><strong><em>Manos</em></strong> (Gr. adj.), loose, rare, sparse</p><p><strong><em>Metrum </em></strong>(L. n.), measure</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:26:39',NULL,NULL),(16864,358,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SphygmoManoMetrum,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively</em><strong><em>, “</em></strong><em>loose measurement of pulse</em>”</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sphygmo + Mano + Metrum</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sphygmos</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;<strong>&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Manos</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;     <strong><em>Metrum&nbsp;</em></strong></li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:27:11',44,'2025-04-07 02:50:35'),(16865,359,13,NULL,'<p>Changes in the Ventricular load will result in changes in the force of contraction and stroke volume.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:28:32',NULL,NULL),(16866,359,8,NULL,'<p>Original discoverer of the phenomenon: Elias Cyon (1866), Carl Ludwig, University of Leipzig; Otto Frank, <strong><em>Ernest Starling</em></strong> performed subsequent study and conclusion.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:28:42',NULL,NULL),(16867,360,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stem</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:29:17',44,'2025-04-07 02:51:38'),(16868,360,13,NULL,'<p>All formed elements of the blood are derived from Stem Cells produced in the Red Bone Marrow.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:29:25',NULL,NULL),(16869,360,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Stemn</strong> (Old Eng.), to originate, to arise from </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:29:32',NULL,NULL),(16870,361,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Subclavian</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:32:45',44,'2025-04-07 02:52:05'),(16871,361,13,NULL,'<p>Artery and Vein that course under the Clavicle </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:32:53',44,'2025-04-07 02:52:23'),(16872,361,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sub </em></strong>(L. prep.), under, below</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Clavis </em></strong>(L. n.), classically, “<em>door bolt, a key</em><strong><em>”</em></strong></p><p>Metaphor for the clavicle bone</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:33:00',44,'2025-04-07 02:52:50'),(16873,361,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SubClavis</em>, </strong></p><p><em>literally, Artery/Vein </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>under the clavicle</em>”</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sub + Clavis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sub </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Clavis&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:33:12',NULL,NULL),(16874,362,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Subclavius</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:33:53',44,'2025-04-07 02:53:19'),(16875,362,13,NULL,'<p>Muscle located under the clavicle, an accessory muscle for breathing.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:34:03',NULL,NULL),(16876,362,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sub </em></strong>(L. prep.), under, below</p><p><strong><em>Clavis </em></strong>(L. n.), clavicle; classically, door bolt, a key<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>Metaphor for the clavicle bone</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:34:10',NULL,NULL),(16877,362,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SubClavis</em>, </strong></p><p><em>literally, Artery/Vein “under the clavicle</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sub + Clavis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sub </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Clavis</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:34:37',NULL,NULL),(16878,364,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Symphathetic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:41:08',44,'2025-04-07 03:01:09'),(16879,364,13,NULL,'<p>Sympathetic Autonomic Nervous System: The <em>“fight”</em> mode of the <em>“fight or flight’</em> polar forces of Autonomic N. S.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:41:15',16,'2025-04-23 02:37:04'),(16880,364,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sym </em></strong>(Gr. prep.), with</p><p><strong><em>Pathos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), sensitivity, strong feeling</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:41:23',NULL,NULL),(16881,364,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SymPathetic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically. </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>with deep sensitivity”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sym + Pathos + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sym </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pathos</em></strong> </p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:41:40',NULL,NULL),(16882,365,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sympathetic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:42:49',44,'2025-04-07 03:02:51'),(16883,365,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Chain Ganglia</strong></p><p>Group of nuclei of neurons</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:42:58',NULL,NULL),(16884,365,13,NULL,'<p>Bilateral chain of paravertebral Ganglia from the ventral roots of Spinal Nerves T1 to L2 influences increased heart activities and <em>“fight”</em> mode.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:43:05',NULL,NULL),(16885,365,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sym </em></strong>(Gr. prep.), with</p><p><strong><em>Pathos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), sensitivity, strong feeling</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:43:12',NULL,NULL),(16886,365,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SymPathetic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically. </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>with deep sensitivity”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sym + Pathos + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sym </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pathos</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:43:24',NULL,NULL),(16887,366,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Systemic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:44:01',44,'2025-04-07 03:03:42'),(16888,366,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Circulation</strong></p><p><strong>Circulus</strong> (L. n.), small circle; </p><p>figuratively, <em>“going in small circle”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:44:08',44,'2025-04-07 03:04:13'),(16889,366,13,NULL,'<p>Oxygenated blood from the lungs return to the left Atrium and pumped into the left Ventricle, whence the blood is ejected to the Aorta for distribution throughout the circulation composed of muscular arteries, arterioles, transfusive capillaries. Deoxygenated blood returns to the right Atrium by a system of Venous Return network; pumped into right Ventricle, then ejected to the lungs for oxygenation.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:44:16',NULL,NULL),(16890,367,13,NULL,'<p>When the heart muscles contract, internal force pressure build-up within the Atria and Ventricles opening the atrioventricular valves and ejecting blood into the Ventricles, Pulmonary Artery to the lungs and into the Aorta to the circulatory system.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:44:41',NULL,NULL),(16891,367,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Systole </em></strong>(Gr. n.), drawing together, contraction</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:44:47',NULL,NULL),(16892,368,13,NULL,'<p>Fast heart beat count; usually over 100BPM; a response to exercise or stress; maybe pathological caused by arrythmia</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:45:16',NULL,NULL),(16893,368,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tachys </em></strong>(Gr. adj.),<strong><em> </em></strong>fast, rapid</p><p><strong><em>Cardia</em></strong> (Gr. n.), heart</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:45:23',NULL,NULL),(16894,368,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em><u>Tachy- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Cardia</u></em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “fast heart”</em></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Tachy- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Cardia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tachys </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cardia</em></strong> </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:45:38',NULL,NULL),(16895,372,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Thoracic,</strong> adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:46:34',NULL,NULL),(16896,372,13,NULL,'<p>The chest region; also refers to the upper to mid back, encompassing the Thoracic Spine, T1-T12.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:46:40',NULL,NULL),(16897,372,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thorax </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thoraces</em></strong>), classically, chest, breastplate</p><p>Metaphor for the human torso</p><p>Vertebral levels T1 to T12&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:46:48',NULL,NULL),(16898,373,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Thrombo</strong>, prefix</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:47:18',NULL,NULL),(16899,373,13,NULL,'<p>Modern Latin, <em>“blood clot”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:47:24',NULL,NULL),(16900,373,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thrombus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thrombi</em></strong>), classically, <em>“lump/curd of milk”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:47:31',44,'2025-04-07 03:07:05'),(16901,374,13,NULL,'<p>Stage 2 in the activation of clotting protein; generated from Prothrombin compounded with Prothrombinase.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:47:58',NULL,NULL),(16902,374,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thrombus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thrombi</em></strong>), blood clot;</p><p>classically, <em>“lump/curd of milk”</em></p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:48:06',44,'2025-04-07 03:08:11'),(16903,374,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thrombin</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “protein for clotting”</em></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Thrombi + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thrombi</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:48:20',44,'2025-04-07 03:08:44'),(16904,375,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., Platelets; precursor to platelet plugs for clotting material.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:48:57',NULL,NULL),(16906,375,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thrombus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thrombi</em></strong>), blood clot;</p><p>classically, <em>“lump/curd of milk”</em></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:49:26',44,'2025-04-07 03:09:36'),(16907,375,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ThromboCyte</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “clotting cell”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Thrombo- + Cyte</u> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thrombo- </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cytos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:50:23',NULL,NULL),(16908,376,13,NULL,'<p>A condition of less than normal Platelet count (normal count: 250K – 400K), causing blood to escape through small vessels and capillaries.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-18 03:51:02',NULL,NULL),(16910,376,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thrombus </em></strong>(plu., 