1:56'),(17123,3842,13,NULL,'<p>Figuratively, “gap-<em>connections</em>”; gaps between heart muscles that allow adjacent cells to transmit Action Potentials with each other via channels and low electrical resistance.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:46:08',NULL,NULL),(17124,3842,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Jungere </em></strong>(L. v.), to join, unite, connect;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Junctum </em></strong>(past part.), joined, connected&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:46:16',NULL,NULL),(17125,3842,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Junction</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “gap-connections</em>” between cardiac muscles</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Junct- + -ion </u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em><u><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></u>Junctum</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun o<span style=\"background-color: rgb(241 245 249 / var(--tw-bg-opacity)); color: rgb(39 39 42 / var(--tw-text-opacity));\">f action</span></li></ul>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:46:48',44,'2025-04-08 02:43:23'),(17126,3843,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Marginal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:47:46',44,'2025-04-08 02:44:11'),(17127,3843,13,NULL,'<p>Arteries that branch off from the left and right Coronary Artery to the left and right walls (margins) of the Ventricles, respectively.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:47:53',NULL,NULL),(17128,3843,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Margo</strong> (plu., <strong><em>Margines</em></strong>), edge, brink, border</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:48:00',NULL,NULL),(17129,3844,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reflex</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:48:50',44,'2025-04-08 02:45:45'),(17130,3844,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Autorhythmic,</strong></p><p>SinoAtrial node normally regularly generates the action potential for muscle contraction</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:49:04',NULL,NULL),(17131,3844,13,NULL,'<p>The SinoAtrial node is the <em>“fountain-head”</em> of action potentials for heart muscles in auto-rhythmic intervals.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:49:11',NULL,NULL),(17132,3844,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flectere </em></strong>(L. v.), to bend, curve<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Flexum </em></strong>(past part.), bent, curved;&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:49:24',44,'2025-04-08 02:46:24'),(17133,3844,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReFlex, </em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“response back again”</em> </p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Re- + Flex</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Flexum </em></strong>&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:49:41',NULL,NULL),(17134,3845,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Refractory</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:50:24',44,'2025-04-08 02:47:07'),(17135,3845,13,NULL,'<p>Reduced sensitivity of heart muscles to stimulation while an Action Potential is in progress; two types: absolute and relative.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:50:31',NULL,NULL),(17136,3845,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Frangere </em></strong>(L. v.), to break</p><p><strong><em>Fractum </em></strong>(past part.), broken, shattered;&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:50:42',44,'2025-04-08 02:47:26'),(17137,3845,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong> <em><u>Re- + Fract- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Fractum </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ory</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:50:52',NULL,NULL),(17138,3846,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reticulum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:51:42',44,'2025-04-08 02:47:53'),(17139,3846,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Smooth Sarcoplasmic</strong></p><p>No Ribosomes; the plasma part of cell is clear</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:51:50',NULL,NULL),(17140,3846,13,NULL,'<p>Microscopically visible in the Muscle Cell Plasma, a<em> </em>network of flat tubules surrounding the cell nucleus; Cardiac muscles have them but not as abundant and organized as those of Skeletal Muscles.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:51:59',NULL,NULL),(17141,3846,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), small fishing net</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Retices</em></strong>), net<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>metaphor for fibrous network formed by proteins</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:52:07',NULL,NULL),(17142,3847,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spasms</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:53:58',44,'2025-04-08 02:48:33'),(17143,3847,13,NULL,'<p>Metaphorically, vascular “<em>convulsion</em>”;<em> </em>sudden but temporary closure of blood vessels due to the contraction of the smooth muscles within the vascular wall.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:54:07',NULL,NULL),(17144,3847,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spasmus</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Spasmi</em></strong>), convulsion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:54:13',NULL,NULL),(17145,3849,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cava</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 05:59:53',NULL,NULL),(17146,3849,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Vena</strong></p><p>Vein (<em>“Ven aqui”.</em> Come here, blood.)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:00:06',44,'2025-04-08 02:50:43'),(17147,3849,13,NULL,'<p>Inferior and Superior Vena Cava are large collecting Veins prior to the final Venous Return of de-oxygenated blood into the right Atrium.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:00:14',NULL,NULL),(17148,3849,8,NULL,'<p><br></p><p><strong><em>Cavus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), hollow, empty</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:00:27',NULL,NULL),(17149,3850,15,NULL,'<p>Vertebral</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:01:07',NULL,NULL),(17150,3850,13,NULL,'<p>Originate from the Subclavian artery; course upward through the Vertebral Foramen of the Transverse Processes of the Cervical Vertebrae through the Foramen Magnum and unite at the Basilar Artery and merge as the Circle of Willis.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:01:17',NULL,NULL),(17151,3850,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vertere</em></strong> (v.), to twist, bend, turn&nbsp;</p><p>Metaphor for the movements of Vertebral Column</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:01:24',NULL,NULL),(17152,3851,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Willis</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:02:05',44,'2025-04-08 02:51:18'),(17153,3851,7,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Cerebral Arterial Circle</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:02:12',NULL,NULL),(17154,3851,13,NULL,'<p>&nbsp;Located in the Cranial Cavity; the continuum of the right and left Carotid Arteries as they enter the base of the brain. Posteriorly, Basilar Artery formed by the left and right Vertebral arteries forms a circular loop branching off to half a dozen arterial distribution to the brain.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:02:19',NULL,NULL),(17155,3851,9,NULL,'<p>Dr. Willis, Thomas (1621 – 1675), An English physician.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:02:39',44,'2025-04-08 02:51:46'),(17156,3852,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Retraction</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:05:30',44,'2025-04-08 02:52:05'),(17157,3852,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Clot,</strong></p><p>Innate property of blood plasma to form plug against blood loss.</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:05:48',NULL,NULL),(17158,3852,13,NULL,'<p>Withdrawal of blood clot by condensing into compact matter (scab); achieved by spasm of platelets that contain protein Actin and Myosin attached to fibrin.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:05:54',NULL,NULL),(17159,3852,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;<span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Trahere </em></strong>(v.), to draw, pull;<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Tractum </em></strong>(past part.). dragged, drawn</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:06:05',44,'2025-04-08 02:52:37'),(17160,3852,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReTraction</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>withdrawing</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Tract- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tractum </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-19 06:06:16',NULL,NULL),(17294,999,15,NULL,'<p>Accessory</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:00:23',NULL,NULL),(17295,999,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Skin Structures</strong></p><p>Sensory structures, hair, nails, glands;&nbsp;</p><p>functions for protection, sensation, temperature regulation</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:00:33',16,'2025-05-28 01:32:26'),(17296,999,13,NULL,'<p>Accessory skin structures are hair, glands, and nails.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:00:42',NULL,NULL),(17297,999,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Accedere</em></strong> (L. v.), to aid, to add to;</p><p><strong><em>Accessum </em></strong>(past. part.), added to&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:00:49',NULL,NULL),(17298,999,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Accessory</em></strong></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>in addition to”</em> skin</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Access- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Accessum</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location; Eng., -ory</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:01:04',16,'2025-05-28 01:32:39'),(17299,999,12,NULL,'<p><strong>ACCESSORY</strong>&nbsp;NERVE - NERVOUS SYSTEM</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:01:14',NULL,NULL),(17300,1000,13,NULL,'<p>A skin condition characterized by white patches</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:01:35',NULL,NULL),(17301,1000,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Albicare</strong> (L. v.), to whiten, to become white;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Albicans</strong> (present. part.), becoming white;&nbsp;</p><p><em>derived from., </em></p><p><strong>Albus</strong>,<strong> -a</strong>, <strong>-um </strong>(L. adj.)<strong> </strong>, white</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:02:13',16,'2025-05-28 01:34:46'),(17302,1001,13,NULL,'<p>A recessive genetic trait of inability to produce Tyrone; the result is a deficiency or absence of </p><p>pigment in the skin, hair, and eyes; several chromosomes are responsible for skin color but </p><p>a single mutation can prevent the manufacture of melanin</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:02:50',NULL,NULL),(17303,1001,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Albus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), white <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:02:56',NULL,NULL),(17304,1001,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Albinism</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“state of whiteness”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Alb- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ine </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ism</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Albus </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-inus </em></strong>(suffix), forms adjective; Eng., -ine</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ismus</em></strong> (suffix), denotes principle, state; Eng., -ism</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:03:07',16,'2025-05-28 01:35:25'),(17305,1002,13,NULL,'<p>A person with the condition of Albinism</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:03:23',NULL,NULL),(17306,1002,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Albus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), white <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:03:35',NULL,NULL),(17307,1002,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Albinus</em></strong></p><p>Metaphorically, person of “<em>white nature</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Alb- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-inus</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Albus </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-inus </em></strong>(suffix), forms adjective; Eng., -ine</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:03:42',16,'2025-06-02 00:23:22'),(17308,1002,12,NULL,'<p><strong>ALBICANS</strong>, CORPUS – REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:03:55',NULL,NULL),(17309,1003,15,NULL,'<p>Apocrine</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:04:18',NULL,NULL),(17310,1003,13,NULL,'<p>Fragments of certain glandular cell break off to become part of the secretion; ex., Mammary </p><p>glands pinched off large cell portions to become part of the milk</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:04:26',NULL,NULL),(17311,1003,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), change, separation; ex., Apogee, Apology</p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:04:34',NULL,NULL),(17312,1003,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ApoCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“secretion of cell fragments breaking away”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Apos </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Apos </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:04:47',16,'2025-06-02 00:23:54'),(17313,1004,15,NULL,'<p>Apocrine</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:05:17',NULL,NULL),(17314,1004,13,NULL,'<p>Apocrine sweat glands are compound coiled tubular glands that drain into the hair Follicular </p><p>opening of the Sebaceous Glands found in the axilla, genitalia and around the anus; secretions </p><p>is influenced by the sex hormones.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:05:24',NULL,NULL),(17315,1004,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), change, separation; ex., Apogee, Apology</p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:05:31',NULL,NULL),(17316,1004,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ApoCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “secretion of cell fragments breaking away”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Apos </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Apos </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Crinos</em></strong> </p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:05:44',NULL,NULL),(17317,1005,13,NULL,'<p>Skin subjected to friction or pressure over bony prominences increases in number of layers in the Stratum Corneum greatly producing a thickened area.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:06:03',NULL,NULL),(17318,1005,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Callus</em></strong> (n.), tough skin, any hard substance<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Callosus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), thickened; </p><p>Figuratively, <em>“thickened skin”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:06:12',NULL,NULL),(17319,1006,13,NULL,'<p>The yellow pigment found in plants such as carrots and corn; humans normally ingest carotene and use it as a source of vitamin A; lipid soluble and the excess accumulates in the Stratum Corneum and Adipose cells of the dermis and hypodermis causing the skin to develop a yellowish tint</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:06:34',NULL,NULL),(17320,1006,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Carotinus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), reddish-orange;<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Carota </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Carotae</em></strong>), carot</p><p>Metaphor for <em>“reddish hue”</em> of skin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:06:43',NULL,NULL),(17322,1007,13,NULL,'<p>Usually refers to the wax produced in the ear canal</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:08:46',NULL,NULL),(17323,1007,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cerumen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cerumines</em></strong>), wax</p><p><strong><em>Ceruminous </em></strong>(L. adj.), waxy&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:08:53',NULL,NULL),(17324,1008,15,NULL,'<p>Ceruminous</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:09:52',NULL,NULL),(17325,1008,13,NULL,'<p>Modified Merocrine sweat glands located in the ear canal that produce cerumen (earwax), </p><p>combined secretions of Ceruminous Glands and Sebaceous Glands.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:09:59',NULL,NULL),(17326,1008,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ceruminous </em></strong>(L. adj.), waxy </p><p><strong><em>Cerumen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cerumines</em></strong>), wax</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:10:11',NULL,NULL),(17327,1009,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., TENSION LINES;<strong> </strong>Elastin and collagen fibers of the skin are oriented in uniform directions and tension, producing cleavage or tension lines in the skin.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:11:38',NULL,NULL),(17328,1009,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Cleave </strong>(Eng. v.), to divide</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:11:42',NULL,NULL),(17329,1010,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., CALLUS; The skin in the Stratum Corneum develop excess layers and form a cone shaped thickened area due to constant friction or pressure over bony prominence.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:12:04',NULL,NULL),(17330,1010,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cornus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cornus</em></strong>), horn;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Metaphorically,<em> “Cornified skin”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:12:11',16,'2025-06-02 00:24:33'),(17331,1012,15,NULL,'<p>Conified</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:12:50',NULL,NULL),(17332,1012,13,NULL,'<p>Hard protein Keratin cover protects Stratum Corneum dead cells.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:12:56',NULL,NULL),(17333,1012,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cornus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cornus</em></strong>), a horn; </p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Corneus, -ea, -eum</em></strong> (L. adj.), horned</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Metaphorically,<em> “corny” or “horny” </em>(?)</p><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:13:05',NULL,NULL),(17334,1014,13,NULL,'<p>Outer covering of glands; outer part of bones; outer layer of the brain; outer layer of hair shaft; outer layer of kidney</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:13:49',NULL,NULL),(17335,1014,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cortex</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cortices</em></strong>), nutshell, coat of seeds&nbsp;</p><p>Metaphor for “o<em>uter coat, outer layer”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-21 03:14:01',NULL,NULL),(17336,1419,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">ENGLISH TRANSLATION:<em> </em></p><p><em>abductor</em> <em>muscle of the smallest finger </em>(pulls away from middle finger)</p><p>· <u>ABDUCTOR</u>, <em>abductor</em> <em>muscle </em></p><p>· <u>DIGITI</u> <u>M