</strong>), bile</p><p><strong><em>Cystis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cystes</em></strong>), bladder, blister</p><p><strong><em>Kinesis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), movement</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:50:22',NULL,NULL),(17935,476,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>CholeCystokinin</em></strong></p><p>metaphorically, <em>“hormone that moves bile bladder”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Chole- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Cysto- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-kin- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-in</u></em></strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>            Cholus</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Cystis</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong><em>-kin-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Kinesis</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex., Insulin)</li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:50:32',16,'2025-04-30 01:39:33'),(17936,477,13,NULL,'<p>Raw materials for Steroid Hormones and Bile Acids in the liver; 85% in circulation is produced in the cells of the body, mainly in the liver and Intestinal Mucosae as a component of Very Low Density Lipoprotein, stored in Adipose cells as Low Density Lipoprotein.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:50:52',NULL,NULL),(17937,477,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Choline</em></strong>, Quaternary Ammonium Cation, </p><p>Vit. B complex, Lecithin</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Esterol</em></strong>; unsaturated, polycyclic alcohols,</p><p>acid + alcohol ? H2O</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:51:06',NULL,NULL),(17938,477,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Chol- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Esterol</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>            Chol-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Choline</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>            Ester</em></strong>-<em> derived from </em><strong><em>Esterol</em></strong></li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:51:15',16,'2025-04-30 01:40:09'),(17939,479,13,NULL,'<p>Caused principally by Alcoholism leading to breakdown of liver tissue and bile leaks (fatty liver); common sign are malnutrition and skin color turning orange-tawny.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:51:49',NULL,NULL),(17940,479,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cirrhus</em></strong> (L. adj.), orange-tawny color</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:51:57',16,'2025-04-30 01:41:24'),(17941,479,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cirrhosis</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, </em><strong><em>“</em></strong><em>yellow condition”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cirrho </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-osis</u></em></strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>            Cirrhus</em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-align-justify\">            &nbsp;<strong><em>-osis</em></strong> (suffix), denotes pathology</li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:52:06',16,'2025-04-30 01:41:58'),(17942,480,13,NULL,'<p>Fat filled Lymphatic proteins synthesized in the epithelial cells; transported in droplets of Triglycerides, Phospholipids and Cholesterol and circulated in the Lymphatic System.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:52:25',NULL,NULL),(17943,480,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chylus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Chyli</em></strong>), digestive secretion;</p><p>Classic<em>, “raw fruit or animal juice”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Micron</em></strong> (Gr. n.), minute part; crumb; <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>mathematically, 1/1,000,000&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 00:52:34',16,'2025-04-30 01:42:55'),(17944,480,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ChyloMicron</em></strong></p><p><