testinal mucosa to breakdown Polysaccharides to Monosaccharides<span style=\"color: red;\"> </span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:47:20',NULL,NULL),(18062,522,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Di</em></strong><em>- </em>(L. prefix), two-part </p><p><strong><em>Saccharum / Sakkharon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), sugar&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:47:28',NULL,NULL),(18063,522,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DiSaccharidease,</em></strong></p><p><em>Enzyme to breakdown sugar</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Di- + Sacchar- + -ide + -ase</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255);\">·            </span><strong><em>Di</em></strong><em>- </em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255);\">·            </span><strong><em>Sacchar-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Saccharum </em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255);\">·            </span><strong><em>-ide</em></strong>, denotes <em>“family”</em> of simple compounds <strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255);\">·            </span><strong><em>-ase </em></strong>(suffix), denotes enzyme&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:47:44',16,'2025-04-30 02:31:31'),(18064,525,13,NULL,'<p>First segment of the small intestine, approximately 25 cm, <em>“12 finger breaths”</em>; a long tube curving to a near 360degree circular tube that cradles the head of the pancreas, serves as receptacle/outlet of the Hepatopancreatic Ampulla (Vater’s Ampulla).&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:48:36',NULL,NULL),(18065,525,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Duodenum </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Duodena</em></strong>), ancient measure: twelve finger-breaths;</p><p>Figurative for the length of the duodenum</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:48:44',44,'2025-04-08 03:50:41'),(18066,526,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Duodenal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:49:15',NULL,NULL),(18067,526,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Glands,</strong></p><p>Produce digestive secretions</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:49:27',NULL,NULL),(18068,526,13,NULL,'<p>The submucosae of the Duodenum contain coiled tubular mucus glands, Brunner’s Glands, which release more mucus into the floor of the Mucosae and into the base of the intestinal glands.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:49:38',NULL,NULL),(18069,526,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Duodenum </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Duodena</em></strong>), ancient measure: twelve finger-breaths.</p><p>Figurative for the length of the duodenum</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:49:45',NULL,NULL),(18070,529,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Duodenal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:50:42',NULL,NULL),(18071,529,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Ulcer,</strong></p><p>Classically, sore on skin or digestive tract</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:50:54',NULL,NULL),(18072,529,13,NULL,'<p>Chronic stimulation of Sympathetic Autonomic Nerves inhibits Duodenal Gland protective secretions, exposing the intestinal lining to highly acidic chime from the stomach.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:51:01',NULL,NULL),(18073,529,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Duodenum </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Duodena</em></strong>), ancient measure: twelve finger-breaths;</p><p>Figurative for the length of the duodenum</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:51:19',44,'2025-04-08 03:52:17'),(18074,530,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Duodenocolic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:55:02',NULL,NULL),(18075,530,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Reflexes,</strong></p><p>Autonomic action-reaction by sensors</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:55:12',NULL,NULL),(18076,530,13,NULL,'<p>Integrate mass movement of chime originating from the duodenum to the Colon; -COLIC, pertains to large intestine.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:55:18',NULL,NULL),(18078,530,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Duodenum </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Duodena</em></strong>), ancient measure: twelve finger-breaths;</p><p>Figurative for the length of the duodenum</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Colon / Kolon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), large intestine</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:55:43',44,'2025-04-08 03:52:52'),(18079,530,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DuodenoColic</em></strong>,</p><p>Literally, “co-ordination of duodenum-colon”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Duodeno + Col- + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>Duodenum</em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>Col-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Colon </em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:55:53',16,'2025-04-30 02:16:49'),(18080,531,13,NULL,'<p>Excretion of feces from the Colon-Sigmoid Colon via Rectum and Anus; liquefied waste is reabsorbed of water and salts in the Colon turning feces into a semi solid goo.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:56:12',NULL,NULL),(18081,531,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ex </em></strong>(L. prep.), from, out of, off</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><em>Liminatus </em></strong>(L. adj.), provided with a threshold</p><p><strong><em>Limen </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Limines</em></strong>), threshold</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 01:56:22',NULL,NULL),(18082,531,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ELimination</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“action from the threshold”</em> (anus)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>E- + Liminatus + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>E-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Ex </em></str