kle, in the anterior abdominal wall attaches the liver to the diaphragm</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:46:20',NULL,NULL),(18156,555,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Falx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Falces</em></strong>), classically, <em>\"a sickle\"</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:46:27',44,'2025-04-09 01:25:31'),(18157,555,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>FalciForm</em></strong></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“shaped like a sickle”</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Falci- + Forma</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>Falces</em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>Forma</em></strong>, shape, model, mold</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:46:39',16,'2025-04-30 02:51:30'),(18158,555,12,NULL,'<p>FALX CEREBRI / <strong style=\"color: red;\"> </strong>FALX CEREBELLI</p><p><br></p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:46:56',NULL,NULL),(18159,556,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Hypercholesterolemia,</strong></p><p>Condition of High cholesterol in the blood circulation</p><p><br></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:47:38',NULL,NULL),(18160,556,13,NULL,'<p>Inherited disorder in over-production or dysfunction of LDL receptors, resulting in poor clearing of LDL; they develop early atherosclerosis and die of Cardio-vascular disease.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:47:44',NULL,NULL),(18161,556,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Familial </strong>(Eng. adj.), inherited genetic defect</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:47:50',NULL,NULL),(18162,557,13,NULL,'<p>Semi solid, non-absorbable, non-digestible food waste products.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:48:11',NULL,NULL),(18163,557,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Faex</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Faeces</em></strong>), dregs, sediment, excrement</p><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:48:17',NULL,NULL),(18164,558,13,NULL,'<p>State of being bloated with gas accumulating in the large intestine.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:48:42',NULL,NULL),(18165,558,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Flatulus </em></strong>(L. n.), blown air, soft sound of wind instrument</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:48:49',44,'2025-04-09 01:44:38'),(18166,558,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<u> </u><strong><em><u>Flatus + </u></em></strong><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=-ance&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em><u>-enc</u></em></strong></a><strong><em><u>ia</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">·            </span><strong><em>Flatulus</em></strong>, blown air, wind instrument</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255);\">·            </span><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=-ance&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em>-enc</em></strong></a><strong><em>e</em></strong> (suffix), forms abstract noun of condition</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:48:58',16,'2025-04-30 02:52:06'),(18167,559,13,NULL,'<p>Bacteria produce gas and accumulate in the colon escaping through the anus; the amount depends on the food and bacterial population in the colon.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:49:19',NULL,NULL),(18168,559,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Flatus</em></strong><em> </em>(L. n.)<strong>,</strong> soft blown air</p><p>Metaphor for fart</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:49:23',44,'2025-04-09 01:42:02'),(18169,561,13,NULL,'<p>The upper lip, lower lip and the tongue are held down securely by <strong><em>Frenula</em></strong> in the sagittal mid-line</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:50:04',NULL,NULL),(18170,561,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Frenulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Frenula</em></strong>), figuratively,<em> “a small bridle, rein; </em></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Frenum</em></strong>, bridle, rein</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:50:10',NULL,NULL),(18171,562,13,NULL,'<p>Large rounded, dome-like portion of the stomach Superior to the cardiac opening.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:50:28',NULL,NULL),(18172,562,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fundus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Fundi</em></strong>), bottom</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:50:33',NULL,NULL),(18173,563,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Gall</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:50:59',NULL,NULL),(18174,563,13,NULL,'<p>Sac-like bag, about 4X8 cm, lodged on the inferior side of the liver that stores about 40 -70 mL of bile secreted by the liver; releases the bile in the presence of fat/oil in the meal.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:51:06',NULL,NULL),(18175,563,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Galla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Gallae</em></strong>), bag, a bladder</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:51:12',NULL,NULL),(18176,564,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Gall</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:51:41',NULL,NULL),(18177,564,13,NULL,'<p>Cholesterol in the gallbladder can solidify into stones; the stones may get dislodged and flow into the pancreatic duct causing Pancreatitis.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:51:47',NULL,NULL),(18178,564,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Galla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Gallae</em></strong>), bag, a bladder</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:51:54',NULL,NULL),(18179,565,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Gastric</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:52:38',NULL,NULL),(18180,565,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Glands,</strong></p><p>Secretory accessories along digestive system</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:52:47',NULL,NULL),(18181,565,13,NULL,'<p>Surface Mucous Cells, Mucous Neck Cells, Parietal Cells (deeper part of the gastric pits), Chief Cells and Endocrine Cells are imbedded beneath the surface of the mucosal digestive lining, each one producing its own secretions.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 02:52:53',44,'2025-04-09 01:47:14'),(18182,565,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Gaster</em> </strong>(plu., 