:52:41',NULL,NULL),(18389,628,13,NULL,'<p>Pancreatic endocrine cells in clusters distributed within the Pancreas Gland (islets) that produce insulin and glucagon, hormones that enable the trillion of cells in the body absorb and convert glucose to energy; glucagon recalls stored glucose into circulation; insulin enable cells to absorb glucose.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:52:48',NULL,NULL),(18390,628,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Islet</strong> (Eng. n.), diminutive of island</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:53:02',NULL,NULL),(18391,629,13,NULL,'<p>Enzyme that splits Isomaltose into 2 glucose molecules&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:53:28',NULL,NULL),(18392,629,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Isos</em></strong> (Gr. adj.), equal</p><p><strong><em>Malt / Melt</em></strong> (Old Eng.), sugar from dissolved starch</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:53:38',NULL,NULL),(18393,629,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Iso- + Malt + -ase</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;Isos</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>&nbsp;Malt / Melt</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;<strong><em>-ase </em></strong>(suffix), denotes enzyme</li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:53:46',44,'2025-04-09 03:03:47'),(18394,630,13,NULL,'<p>Isomer of sugars derived from carbohydrates and starch.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:54:12',NULL,NULL),(18395,630,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Isos</em></strong> (Gr. adj.), equal</p><p><strong><em>Malt / Melt</em></strong> (Old Eng.), sugar from dissolved starch</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:54:20',NULL,NULL),(18396,630,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Iso- + Malt + -ose</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Isos</em></strong> </p><p><strong>·&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Malt </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ose </em></strong>(suffix), sugar, glucose</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:54:42',NULL,NULL),(18397,631,13,NULL,'<p>A section of Small Intestine, average length 3.5 meters, histologically continuous with the duodenum but smaller in diameter, less thickness of the wall, less microvilli and less <strong><em>Plica Circulares</em></strong>; like the duodenum it is a major site of absorption, specialized Lymphatic Nodules (PEYER’S PATCHES) are imbedded in the mucosae and submucosae for protection and fat absorption.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:55:06',NULL,NULL),(18398,631,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Jejunus, -a, -um </em></strong>(adj.), empty</p><p>always empty during dissection</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:55:10',NULL,NULL),(18399,633,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Labia</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:55:45',NULL,NULL),(18400,633,13,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Labia</em></strong>, lips, formed by the Orbicularis Oris Muscle, and cheeks, the lateral wall of the oral cavity; lined with stratified squamous epithelial cells.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:55:52',NULL,NULL),(18401,633,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Labium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Labia</em></strong>), lip</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:55:58',NULL,NULL),(18402,634,13,NULL,'<p>Translation<em>: “of the lips”</em> (possessive form, <strong><em>Labium</em></strong>, lip)</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:56:30',NULL,NULL),(18403,635,13,NULL,'<p>Enzyme that breaks down milk fat.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:56:51',NULL,NULL),(18404,635,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lactis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lactes</em></strong>), milk</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:56:56',NULL,NULL),(18405,635,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lactase</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “milk digestive enzyme”</em></p><p><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Lact- + -ase</u></em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Lactis</em></strong></li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ase </em></strong>(suffix), denotes enzyme</li></ul>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03:57:09',44,'2025-04-09 03:07:26'),(18406,636,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lactase</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 03: