L),(18643,722,13,NULL,'<p>Over-secretion of Gastric acids and pepsin encroaches the stomach lining around the Pylorus on the Duodenal side and progresses to get infected by Helicobacter Pylori; literally, ulcer <em>“caused by Pepsin”</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:06:36',NULL,NULL),(18644,722,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pepsis </em></strong>(Gr. n.), digestion of protein</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:06:55',NULL,NULL),(18645,722,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Pept- + -icus</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pept-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Pepsis </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ic </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:07:12',NULL,NULL),(18646,723,13,NULL,'<p>Digestive enzyme of intestinal mucosa bind to Absorptive Microvilli Cells and Hydrolyze peptide bonds between amino acid chains.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:07:33',NULL,NULL),(18647,723,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pepsis </em></strong>(Gr. n.), digestion of protein</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:07:39',NULL,NULL),(18648,723,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peptidase</em></strong>,</p><p>Literally, <em>“enzyme for amino acid chains”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Pept- + -id + -ase</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pept-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Pepsis</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ide</em></strong> (suffix), “family” of simple compounds</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ase </em></strong>(suffix), denotes enzyme&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:07:56',NULL,NULL),(18649,724,13,NULL,'<p>Digested Protein</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:08:22',NULL,NULL),(18650,724,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pepsis </em></strong>(Gr. n.), digestion of protein</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:08:28',NULL,NULL),(18651,724,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peptide</em></strong>,</p><p>Literally, <em>“broken down amino acid chains”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Pept- + -id + -ase</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pept-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Pepsis</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ide</em></strong> (suffix), “family” of simple compounds</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:08:52',NULL,NULL),(18652,725,13,NULL,'<p>Surrounding the Anus; around the anus.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:10:17',NULL,NULL),(18653,725,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peri-</em></strong> (L. prep.), around</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Anus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Ani</em></strong>), ring (classically, “<em>the gold one”</em>)</p><p>Metaphor for the External Anal Sphincter</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:10:24',NULL,NULL),(18654,725,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Peri-</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-neum</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peri-</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-neum</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Anus</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:10:32',NULL,NULL),(18655,728,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Periodontal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:11:16',NULL,NULL),(18656,728,13,NULL,'<p>Gingivitis, pyorrhea, halitosis; affecting the gums, alveoli, and surrounding teeth.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:11:23',NULL,NULL),(18657,728,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peri </em></strong>(L. prep.), around, surrounding</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Odons</em></strong>, (Gr. n.; plu., <strong><em>Odontes</em>)</strong>, tooth</p><p>variant of <strong><em>Dens</em></strong> (L. n.), tooth</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:11:28',NULL,NULL),(18658,728,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>PeriOdontal,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “around the teeth”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Peri + Odont- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peri </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Odontes</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:11:39',NULL,NULL),(18659,729,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Periodontal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:12:13',NULL,NULL),(18660,729,13,NULL,'<p>Numerous ligamentous ties securing the teeth inside the Alveolar sockets; literally, ligaments <em>“surrounding the teeth”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:12:20',NULL,NULL),(18661,729,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peri </em></strong>(L. prep.), around, surrounding</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Odons</em></strong>, (Gr. n.; plu., <strong><em>Odontes</em>)</strong>, tooth</p><p>variant of <strong><em>Dens</em></strong> (L. n.), tooth</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:12:26',NULL,NULL),(18662,729,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>PeriOdontal,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “around the teeth”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Peri + Odont- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peri </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Odontes</em></strong>;</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:12:39',NULL,NULL),(18663,730,13,NULL,'<p>Circular smooth muscles lined up throughout the digestive tract contract in sequential waves; autonomically controlled movements throughout the digestive tract, from the Oropharynx to the Anal Canal.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:01',NULL,NULL),(18664,730,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peri </em></strong>(L. prep.), around, surrounding </p><p><strong><em>Stalsis </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Stalses</em></strong>), jumping, skipping</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:06',NULL,NULL),(18665,730,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>PeriStalsis,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “jumping around” </em></p><p><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Peri + Stalsis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peri </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Stalsis&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:15',NULL,NULL),(18666,731,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Peristaltic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:36',NULL,NULL),(18667,731,13,NULL,'<p>Continuous segmental motion throughout the digestive tract begins at the Oropharynx, ends at the Anus; the stomach mix, churn, and push chime to the Pyloric region; the digestive tract is equipped with powerful circular muscle; contractions occur in sequential relaxation and contraction causing distention and constriction that propel intestinal contents for mass movement.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:43',NULL,NULL),(18668,731,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peri </em></strong>(L. prep.), around, surrounding </p><p><strong><em>Stalsis </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Stalses</em></strong>), jumping, skipping</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:49',NULL,NULL),(18669,731,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>PeriStaltic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “jumping around”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Peri + Stalsis + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peri </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Stalsis </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:13:59',NULL,NULL),(18670,732,13,NULL,'<p>Membranes that cover the abdominal wall (Parietal) and the organs (Visceral); protect the organs from each other and trauma within the abdomen as they are shaken, and bumped within the cavity</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:14:28',NULL,NULL),(18671,732,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peritoneus, -ea, -eum</em></strong> (L. adj.), stretched around </p><p>inside the abdominal cavity</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:14:33',NULL,NULL),(18672,735,13,NULL,'<p>Inflammation of the Peritoneum due to digestive contents escaping into the Peritoneum.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:15:26',NULL,NULL),(18673,735,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peritoneum</em></strong> (adj.), stretched around</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:15:32',NULL,NULL),(18674,735,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Periton- + -itis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peritoneum</em></strong> </p><p><strong>·&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-itis </em></strong>(suffix), denotes inflammation</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:15:51',NULL,NULL),(18675,736,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., SECONDARY TEETH replace Deciduous Teeth completely by age 11; 32 permanent teeth, 8 on each quadrant mirroring each other in the upper and lower jaws</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:16:10',NULL,NULL),(18676,737,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphoid tissues imbedded in the distal half of the Duodenum and Jejunum, and in the Appendix.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:16:47',NULL,NULL),(18677,737,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peyer</em></strong>, Johann Conrad<em> </em><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(1653 – 1712), Swiss&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anatomist\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: white; color: black;\">anatomist</a><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white;\">described lymphoid tissue in the peritoneum</span> </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:16:53',NULL,NULL),(18678,738,13,NULL,'<p>Composed of Nasopharynx, Oropharynx, Laryngopharynx; the OROPHARYNX and LARYNGOPHARYNX, lined with moist Stratified Squamous Epithelium, are involved in voluntary swallowing of food.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:17:11',NULL,NULL),(18679,738,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pharynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pharynges</em></strong>), the throat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:17:18',NULL,NULL),(18680,739,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pharyngeal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:17:37',NULL,NULL),(18681,739,13,NULL,'<p>During initial swallowing the bolus of food in the mouth is pushed by the tongue to the back of the mouth against the hard palate, then to the oropharynx; the Pharyngeal Constrictor Muscles pushes the food through the pharynx and closes to prevent back flow.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:17:44',NULL,NULL),(18682,739,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pharynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pharynges</em></strong>), the throat</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:17:51',NULL,NULL),(18683,739,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pharynges + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pharynges</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:17:58',NULL,NULL),(18684,740,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pharyngeal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:18:33',NULL,NULL),(18685,740,13,NULL,'<p>Comprised of superior, middle, inferior; Pharyngeal Constrictors in the posterior Walls are arranged like a stack of 3 drinking glasses.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:18:40',NULL,NULL),(18686,740,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pharynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pharynges</em></strong>), the throat</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:18:46',NULL,NULL),(18687,740,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pharynges + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pharynges</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:18:52',NULL,NULL),(18688,741,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Phrayngeal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:19:15',NULL,NULL),(18689,741,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Phase,</strong></p><p>Classically, Phasis (L. n.), passing the stage of the moon</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:19:24',NULL,NULL),(18690,741,13,NULL,'<p>After the Voluntary Phase of swallowing as a response to Deglutition Reflex food bolus crosses the Oral Cavity to Oropharynx, a touch sensor triggers the swallowing center in the Medulla Oblongata via CN V- Trigeminal N. and CN IX - Glossopharyngeal N.; involuntary phase of ingestion takes over; only the OROPHARYNX and LARYNGXOPHARYNX are involved in voluntary swallowing.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:19:34',NULL,NULL),(18691,741,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pharynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pharynges</em></strong>), the throat</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:19:41',NULL,NULL),(18692,741,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pharynges + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pharynges</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:19:48',NULL,NULL),(18693,747,13,NULL,'<p>Braiding and interlacing of adjacent spinal nerves or blood vessel network for communication and interaction.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:21:17',NULL,NULL),(18694,747,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Plexus </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Plexi</em></strong>), bend, fold</p><p>Metaphor for the inter-braiding of nerve roots</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:21:25',NULL,NULL),(18695,751,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Plicae</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:22:25',NULL,NULL),(18696,751,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., CIRCULAR FOLDS; Deep creases and circular pits in the mucosae and submucosae throughout the length of the digestive tract enhance the absorptive surface and efficiency of the mucosae.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:22:31',NULL,NULL),(18697,751,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Plica</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Plicae</em></strong>), fold</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:22:37',NULL,NULL),(18698,753,13,NULL,'<p>Teeth anterior to the Molars&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:23:15',NULL,NULL),(18699,753,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pre </em></strong>(L. prep.) before, front </p><p><strong><em>Mola </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Molae</em></strong>), millstone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:23:21',NULL,NULL),(18700,753,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>PreMolar</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “before the Molar”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Pre- + Mola + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pre </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Mola </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-aris</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:23:37',NULL,NULL),(18701,755,13,NULL,'<p>Movement of food in digestive tract from swallowing to excretion is achieved by Peristalsis and mixing motion from action of involuntary muscles; the movement is not flowing but rhythmically intermittent of double motion, mixing and pushing.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:24:09',NULL,NULL),(18702,755,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pro </em></strong>(L. prep), for, in behalf of, forward<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><em>Pellere </em></strong>(L. v.), to beat a drum;</p><p><strong><em>Pulsum </em></strong>(past part.), beaten like a drum&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:24:18',NULL,NULL),(18703,755,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ProPulsion</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “moving forward by double beat action”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Pro + Puls- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pro</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pulsum </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:24:30',NULL,NULL),(18704,756,13,NULL,'<p>Composed of carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen are bound together by covalent bonds; protein regulates body processes, cell reproduction, transportation system, protection, muscle contraction, raw material for structures, and energy.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:24:49',NULL,NULL),(18705,756,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Protos </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), first, origin <strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:24:53',NULL,NULL),(18706,756,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Protein</em></strong> </p><p>metaphorically,<em> “the original”</em> substance</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Prot- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Protos </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:25:01',NULL,NULL),(18707,757,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pterygoid</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:25:24',NULL,NULL),(18708,757,13,NULL,'<p>Facial bone for attachment of Medial Pterygoid Muscle, opens the mouth before chewing muscle.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:25:31',NULL,NULL),(18709,757,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pterygus</em></strong> (Gr. n.), little<strong><em> </em></strong>wing<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:25:37',NULL,NULL),(18710,757,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pterygoid</em></strong> </p><p>Simile, <em>“resembling a wing”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Pteryg- + -oid</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pterygus</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-oid</em></strong> (suffix), forms simile: <em>“resembling”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:25:49',NULL,NULL),(18711,759,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pulp</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:26:22',NULL,NULL),(18712,759,13,NULL,'<p>Inner center of the teeth lined with blood vessels, nerves and connective tissue.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:26:29',NULL,NULL),(18713,759,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Pulpa</strong> (plu., <strong>Pulpae</strong>), pulp, flesh of the fruit</p><p>Metaphor for the soft inner core of teeth</p><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:26:50',NULL,NULL),(18714,759,12,NULL,'<p><strong>PULPOSUS</strong>, NUCLEUS – JOINT SYSTEM</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:27:03',NULL,NULL),(18715,761,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pyloric</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:27:38',NULL,NULL),(18716,761,13,NULL,'<p>The narrow part of the stomach ends at the Pyloric opening that empties chyme into the small intestine</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:27:45',NULL,NULL),(18717,761,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pylorus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Pylori</em></strong>), gatekeeper, porter</p><p><strong><em>Pyle </em></strong>(Gr. n.), gate</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:27:52',NULL,NULL),(18718,761,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyloric,</em></strong> ability to guard</p><p>Metaphor for the function of the valve</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pylori + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pylori</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:27:59',NULL,NULL),(18719,762,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pyloric</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:28:27',NULL,NULL),(18720,762,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pump,</strong></p><p>By the force of peristalsis of circular muscles of the stomach</p><p><br></p>',2,