sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:29:42',NULL,NULL),(18728,764,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pyloric</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:30:10',NULL,NULL),(18729,764,13,NULL,'<p>Thick ring of smooth muscle controls the opening from the stomach to the small intestine.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:30:16',NULL,NULL),(18730,764,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pylorus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Pylori</em></strong>), gatekeeper, porter</p><p><strong><em>Pyle </em></strong>(Gr. n.), gate</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:30:22',NULL,NULL),(18731,764,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyloric,</em></strong> ability to guard</p><p>Metaphor for the function of the valve</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pylori + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pylori</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:30:30',NULL,NULL),(18732,765,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pyloric</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:32:21',NULL,NULL),(18733,765,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Valve,</strong></p><p>Valvus (L. n.), classically, <em>“double door”</em></p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:32:31',NULL,NULL),(18734,765,13,NULL,'<p>The inferior opening of the stomach; opens to the Duodenum equipped with a valve that prevents back flow of chyme to the stomach&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:32:40',NULL,NULL),(18735,765,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pylorus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Pylori</em></strong>), gatekeeper, porter</p><p><strong><em>Pyle </em></strong>(Gr. n.), gate</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:32:48',NULL,NULL),(18736,765,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyloric,</em></strong> ability to guard</p><p>Metaphor for the function of the valve</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pylori + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pylori</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:33:10',NULL,NULL),(18737,766,13,NULL,'<p>Infection of the gum, with pus production</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:33:59',NULL,NULL),(18738,766,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), pus</p><p><strong><em>Rrhea</em></strong> (Gr. n.), profuse flow, discharge</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:34:04',NULL,NULL),(18739,766,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>PyoRrhea</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “pus discharge”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Pyo- + Rrhea</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pyo-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Pyon</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Rrhea</em></strong> </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:34:15',NULL,NULL),(18740,767,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a, HEARTBURN; Symptom of GastroEsophageal Reflux Disease; Heartburn caused by backflow of low pH chime from the stomach back to the lower Esophagus due to weakness of inferior Esophageal Sphincter. Possibly, a prelude to CardioVascular Accident.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:34:45',NULL,NULL),(18741,767,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyre</em></strong> (Gr. n.), fire, fever, funeral fire;</p><p>poetically, “fire-blazing\" \"symbolic of terrible things, rages”</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:34:51',NULL,NULL),(18742,767,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyrosis</em> </strong></p><p><em>metaphorically</em><strong><em>,</em></strong><em> “burning condition</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pyro- + -osis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pyro-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Pyre</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-osis</em></strong> (suffix), denotes pathology</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:35:05',NULL,NULL),(18743,768,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Quandrate</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:35:31',NULL,NULL),(18744,768,13,NULL,'<p>A Minor Lobar Divisions of the liver: Quadrate Lobe, large squarish. Major Lobar Division: Left and Right; Caudate Lobe, visible on the inferior view having a stubby tail.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:35:38',NULL,NULL),(18745,768,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Quadrus, -a, -um</em> </strong>(L. adj.), square&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:35:42',NULL,NULL),(18746,768,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Quadrate</em></strong>, </p><p>figuratively, <em>“squarish”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Quadra- + -ate</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Quadrus</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ate</em></strong> (suffix), forms adj; provided with</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:35:57',NULL,NULL),(18747,769,13,NULL,'<p>Straight thick muscular tube 5-7cm long immediately inferior to the Sigmoid Colon; ends at the Anal Canal.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:36:15',NULL,NULL),(18748,769,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Rectus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), upright, straight up</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:36:22',NULL,NULL),(18749,770,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Reflexive,&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Adj., characteristic of autonomic response and feedback</p><p><br></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:36:45',NULL,NULL),(18750,770,13,NULL,'<p>Autonomic response for homeostasis to a stimulus that occurs without conscious volition; an involuntary nervous, or hormonal/chemical response.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:36:52',NULL,NULL),(18751,770,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), back again, repeatedly</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flectere </em></strong>(L. v.), to bend, curve;<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Flexum </em></strong>(past part.), bent, curved&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:37:01',NULL,NULL),(18752,770,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReFlex,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “response back”<span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Re- + Flex-</u></em><u> + </u></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Flexum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:37:20',NULL,NULL),(18753,776,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Regulation</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:38:31',NULL,NULL),(18754,776,13,NULL,'<p>Involves nervous, mechanical, and chemical influences regulating the movement of chyme in the alimentary canal, secretion of gastric glands, absorption by the mucosae and elimination.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:38:37',NULL,NULL),(18755,776,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Regulus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reguli</em></strong>), small ruler; </p><p>diminutive of<strong><em> Rex</em></strong> (plu.,<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong><strong><em>Reges</em></strong>), king&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:38:45',NULL,NULL),(18756,776,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Regulation,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “small rule”</em> of digestion</p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Regul- + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Regulus </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ation </em></strong>(suffix), forms noun of action</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:38:56',NULL,NULL),(18757,777,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Regulation</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:39:17',NULL,NULL),(18758,777,13,NULL,'<p>Pyloric peristalsis pumps and pushes the chyme through the partially closed Pyloric Valve into the duodenum.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:39:24',NULL,NULL),(18759,777,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Regulus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reguli</em></strong>), small ruler; </p><p>diminutive of<strong><em> Rex</em></strong> (plu.,<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong><strong><em>Reges</em></strong>), king&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:39:33',NULL,NULL),(18760,777,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Regulation,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “small rule” </em>of stomach</p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Regul- + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Regulus </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ation </em></strong>(suffix), forms noun of action</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:39:48',NULL,NULL),(18761,778,13,NULL,'<p>Organs attached to the posterior abdominal wall: Duodenum, Pancreas, Kidneys, Adrenal Glands, Urinary Bladder have no Mesenteries but are secured by Omental connective tissue (peritoneal tissue).</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:40:11',NULL,NULL),(18762,778,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Retros </em></strong>(Gr. prep.), behind, backward </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Peritoneus, -ea, -eum</em></strong> (L. adj.), stretched around </p><p>inside the abdominal cavity</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:40:17',NULL,NULL),(18763,778,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>RetroPeritoneum</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “stretched around the back”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Retro- + Peritoneum</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Retros</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Peritoneum</em></strong> </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:40:28',NULL,NULL),(18764,779,13,NULL,'<p>Large folds visible when the stomach is empty, allowing the stomach mucosa and submucosal layers to stretch out when filled with food.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:40:54',NULL,NULL),(18765,779,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ruga</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Rugae</em></strong>), fold, ridge, wrinkle</p><p>Metaphor for the circular folds (deep transverse creases) </p><p>throughout the digestive tube,</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:41:00',NULL,NULL),(18766,780,13,NULL,'<p>Thin fluid produced by the Salivary Glands.</p><p>Secreted from Parotid and Submandibular Salivary Glands, moistens food, and lubricates food for effortless passage through the Esophageal protective lining; contains digestive enzyme, Amylase, for initial digestion of starch; contains oral and dental antibacterial properties;&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:41:25',NULL,NULL),(18767,781,13,NULL,'<p>Second molar has more mineral deposits from the saliva due to the proximity to the exit duct of Parotid Gland.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:41:51',NULL,NULL),(18768,782,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Salivary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:42:25',NULL,NULL),(18769,782,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Amylase,</strong></p><p>Enzyme that lowers digestion CHO to sugar</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:42:33',NULL,NULL),(18770,782,13,NULL,'<p>Breaks down covalent bonds of Polysaccharides; convert them into disaccharides, monosaccharides, maltose and isomaltose sugars.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:42:46',NULL,NULL),(18771,782,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Saliva </em></strong>(L. n.), thin fluid produced</p><p>by the Salivary Glands</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:42:51',NULL,NULL),(18772,782,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Salivary,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “Function for saliva production”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Saliva + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Saliva </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-arium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ary</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:43:15',NULL,NULL),(18773,783,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Salivary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:43:36',NULL,NULL),(18774,783,13,NULL,'<p>Parotid, Submandibular, and Sublingual Salivary Glands, Lingual Glands, Palatine Glands, Buccal glands, Labial glands are coiled tubular glands that secrete Saliva, first stage digestive juice, Amylase for carbohydrate digestion.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:43:49',NULL,NULL),(18775,783,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Saliva </em></strong>(L. n.), thin fluid produced</p><p>by the Salivary Glands</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:43:56',NULL,NULL),(18776,783,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Salivary,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “Function for saliva production”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Saliva + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Saliva </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-arium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ary</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 06:44:07',NULL,NULL),(18777,784,13,NULL,'<p>When acidic chyme enters the duodenum there is a profusion of pancreatic secretions<strong>: </strong>liver bile, intestinal secretions, mucus secretion;<strong> </strong>subsequently,<strong> Secretin</strong> is released by the Duodenum to inhibit Gastric Glands, Parietal and Chief Cells; fatty acids and hypertonic solutions stimulate GASTRIC INHIBITORY POLYPEPTIDE in the Duodenum to inhibit gastric secretions.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:34:27',NULL,NULL),(18778,784,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Secernere </em></strong>(L. v.), set apart, to release;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Secretum </em></strong>(past part.)<em>, </em>separated, released </p><p><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:34:38',NULL,NULL),(18779,784,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Secretin,</em></strong><em> “Hormone for secretion of </em>GIP<em>”</em></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>\"set apart,</em> <em>released\"</em>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Secret- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Secretum</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:34:56',NULL,NULL),(18780,786,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Secretions</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:35:52',NULL,NULL),(18781,786,13,NULL,'<p>Mucus, electrolytes, water, enzymes, Secretin, Cholecystokinin from the mucosae, liver bile and pancreatic juices, insulin.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:35:59',NULL,NULL),(18782,786,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Secernere </em></strong>(L. v.), set apart, to release;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Secretum </em></strong>(past part.)<em>, </em>separated, released&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:36:12',NULL,NULL),(18783,786,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Secretion,</em></strong><em> </em></p><p><em>literally, \"set apart,</em> <em>released,\"</em>&nbsp;</p><p><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Secret- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Secretum</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:36:25',NULL,NULL),(18784,787,13,NULL,'<p>Having the function to produce and release enzyme, hormone, juices; usually the property of glands</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:36:59',NULL,NULL),(18785,787,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Secernere </em></strong>(L. v.), set apart, to release;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Secretum </em></strong>(past part.)<em>, </em>separated, released&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:37:08',NULL,NULL),(18786,787,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Secretory,</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “function to produce and release enzyme, hormone, fluid”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Secret- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Secret- </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>o&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ory</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:37:22',NULL,NULL),(18787,788,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Segmental</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:39:23',NULL,NULL),(18788,788,13,NULL,'<p>Contractions of Involuntary muscles propagated in the Small Intestine in sequential short sections providing mixing and propulsion movements.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:39:31',NULL,NULL),(18789,788,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Segmentum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Segmenta</em></strong>), section, portion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:39:39',NULL,NULL),(18790,789,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Serosa</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:40:06',NULL,NULL),(18791,789,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Adventitia,</strong></p><p>Literally, “Tissue coming from the outside”</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:40:18',NULL,NULL),(18792,789,13,NULL,'<p>Visceral Peritoneum, the 4th and outer most layer of digestive tract is exposed to the Peritoneal Cavity; histologically derived from the abdominal Peritoneal connective tissue and squamous epithelium.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:40:28',NULL,NULL),(18793,789,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Serosus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), watery; </p><p><strong><em>Serum</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Sera</em></strong>), watery part of milk, whey</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:40:36',NULL,NULL),(18794,790,13,NULL,'<p>Kills bacteria with Lysozyme&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:41:02',NULL,NULL),(18795,790,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Serosus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), watery; </p><p><strong><em>Serum</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Sera</em></strong>), watery part of milk, whey</p><p>literally, “<em>fluid</em>”</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:41:10',NULL,NULL),(18796,791,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Serous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:41:30',NULL,NULL),(18797,791,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Membrane,</strong></p><p>Thin layer covering</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:41:42',NULL,NULL),(18798,791,13,NULL,'<p>Lining of the abdominal cavity providing serous fluid for lubrication and protection against the wall and other organs; literally, <em>“watery membrane”&nbsp;</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-28 12:41:51',NULL,NULL),(18799,791,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Serosus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), watery; </p><p><str