&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sur-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Super </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Facies&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:27:44',NULL,NULL),(18836,808,13,NULL,'<p>An agent acting on the surface of covalently bonded elements of H2O.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:28:11',NULL,NULL),(18838,808,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. prep), above, high</p><p><strong><em>Facies </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Faciei</em></strong>), face<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><em>Agere</em></strong> (L. v.), to do, act, perform;</p><p><strong><em>Actum </em></strong>(past part.), acted on, done&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:28:36',NULL,NULL),(18839,808,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SurFactActant</em></strong></p><p>Metaphorically, <em>“acting above the surface”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Sur- + Fact- + Actant</u></em></strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Sur-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Super </em></strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Fact-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Facies </em></strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Actant-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Actum</em></strong> </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:28:55',NULL,NULL),(18840,809,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Swallowing</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:29:20',NULL,NULL),(18841,809,13,NULL,'<p>Located in the Medulla Oblongata; receives stimuli from the <u>Sensory</u> part of CN V - Trigeminal Nerve and CN IX - Glossopharyngeal Nerve; initiates swallowing reflex to <u>Motor</u> part of CN V and CN IX.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:29:29',NULL,NULL),(18842,809,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Swallow, </strong>(Eng. v.), the last voluntary action throughout the </p><p>Digestive System until the act of defecation</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:29:35',NULL,NULL),(18843,811,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Temporalis</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:31:47',NULL,NULL),(18844,811,13,NULL,'<p>Muscle relating to the Temporal bone; Synergist with Medial Pterygoid and Masseter in closing the Mandible for chewing.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:31:54',NULL,NULL),(18845,811,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tempus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tempores</em></strong>), time</p><p>Metaphor for the origination of the muscle where hair turns grey with time</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:32:04',NULL,NULL),(18846,812,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Temporomandibular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:32:44',NULL,NULL),(18847,812,13,NULL,'<p>The Mandibular condyle articulates with the Mandibular Fossa of the Temporal Bone forming the TMJ, </p><p>a major apparatus of mastication; a modified Synovial Joint with limited movement, plane, Ellipsoid joint, and hinge motion; also capable of medio-lateral deviation.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:32:51',NULL,NULL),(18848,812,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tempus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tempores</em></strong>), time</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Mandibulum</em></strong>, small griding tool, the lower jaw</p><p>Metaphor for the chewing bone.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:33:00',NULL,NULL),(18849,812,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Temporo- + Mandibula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tempores</em></strong> </p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Mandibulum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:36:51',NULL,NULL),(18850,813,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Teniae</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:37:16',NULL,NULL),(18851,813,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Coli,</strong></p><p>“Of the colon”</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:37:26',NULL,NULL),(18852,813,13,NULL,'<p>3 longitudinal Bands that runs along the length of the Colon that forms the Haustration of the Colon when not stretched by digestive contents.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:37:33',NULL,NULL),(18853,813,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tenia </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Teniae</em></strong>), band, ribbon</p><p>Figuratively, <em>“longitudinal band of the colon”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:37:41',NULL,NULL),(18854,814,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Terminal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:38:04',NULL,NULL),(18855,814,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Sulcus,</strong></p><p>Depression, dip</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:38:11',NULL,NULL),(18856,814,13,NULL,'<p>A “<em>dip boundary”</em> dividing the tongue to anterior 2/3rd lined with papillae taste buds and posterior 1/3rd lined with small glands and large lymphoid tissue, Lingual Tonsil.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:38:19',NULL,NULL),(18857,814,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Terminus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Termini</em></strong>), limit, end, boundary&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:38:28',NULL,NULL),(18858,815,13,NULL,'<p><em>“. . . of the tonsils”</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:38:51',NULL,NULL),(18859,815,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tonsillarum</em></strong></p><p><em>(plu. Possessive form),</em></p><p><strong><em>Tonsilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tonsillae</em></strong>), glands of the throat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:38:56',NULL,NULL),(18860,819,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Transverse</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:39:48',NULL,NULL),(18861,819,13,NULL,'<p>Part of the large Intestine that crosses from right to left flexures (other parts of the Colon: Ascending, Descending, Sigmoid, Flexures).</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:39:58',NULL,NULL),(18862,819,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trans</em></strong> (L. prep.), across, cross section<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Vertere </em></strong>(L. v.), to twist, bend, turn;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Versum </em></strong>(past part.), turned, bent&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:40:06',NULL,NULL),(18863,819,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>TransVersum,</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “turned cross-wise”</em></p><p><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Trans + Versum</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trans</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Versum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:40:17',NULL,NULL),(18864,820,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Transverse</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:40:37',NULL,NULL),(18865,820,13,NULL,'<p>Mesenteries of the Transverse Colon are attached to the posterior wall of the abdomen&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:40:44',NULL,NULL),(18866,820,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trans</em></strong> (L. prep.), across, crossection<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Vertere </em></strong>(L. v.), to twist, bend;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Versum </em></strong>(past part.), turned, bent&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:40:52',NULL,NULL),(18867,820,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>TransVersum,</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “turned across”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Trans + Versum</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trans</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Versum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:41:05',NULL,NULL),(18868,821,13,NULL,'<p>Commonly known as Triglycerides consisting of three fatty acids and one glycerol molecule covalently bound together.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:41:28',NULL,NULL),(18869,821,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tres </em></strong>(number), three</p><p><strong><em>Glucose </em></strong>(organic comp.), sugar, starch</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:41:34',NULL,NULL),(18870,821,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>TriGlyceride</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “three fatty acids and one glycerol molecule”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Tri- + Glycer- + -ide</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Tri-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Tres </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Glycer-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Glucose </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-ide</em></strong> (chemistry suffix), denotes “family of” simple compounds</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:41:49',NULL,NULL),(18871,822,13,NULL,'<p>1 of 3, Pancreatic Proteolytic enzyme (Chymotrypsin and Caboxypeptidase) released as Trypsinogen to be activated only when needed to digest due to its high acidity.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:42:09',NULL,NULL),(18872,822,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trypsis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), rubbing, crushing, breaking</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:42:15',NULL,NULL),(18873,822,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trypsin</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “protein for crushing”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Tryps- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tryps-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Trypsis</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:42:26',NULL,NULL),(18874,823,13,NULL,'<p>Inactive form of Trypsin at time of production by the Pancreas</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:42:47',NULL,NULL),(18875,823,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trypsis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), rubbing, crushing, breaking</p><p><strong><em>Genitor</em></strong>, father, begetter, producer</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:42:54',NULL,NULL),(18876,823,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trypsinogen</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, producer of “protein for breaking”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Tryps- + -in + -gen</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tryps-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Trypsis</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-gen</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Genitor&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:43:04',NULL,NULL),(18877,824,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Ulcerative</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:43:23',NULL,NULL),(18878,824,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Colitis,</strong></p><p>Inflammation of the Colon</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:43:34',NULL,NULL),(18879,824,13,NULL,'<p>Occurs in the Colon due to inflamed mucosae, brush border</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:43:41',NULL,NULL),(18880,824,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ulcus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Ulceres</em></strong>), sore on skin or on intestinal membrane</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:43:48',NULL,NULL),(18881,824,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em><u>Ulcer- + -ative</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ulceres</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ative</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; characteristic</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:43:56',NULL,NULL),(18882,825,13,NULL,'<p>Located inferior to the Oropharynx; Voluntary muscle that prevents reflux of Bolus and fluids to the Oropharynx&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:44:17',NULL,NULL),(18883,826,13,NULL,'<p>Located superior to the stomach, opens to the esophagus; regulates the movements of food material from the Esophagus into the stomach.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:44:38',NULL,NULL),(18884,827,13,NULL,'<p>A grape-like appendage hanging at the posterior edge of the soft palate; receives stimulus during swallowing to close the Pharynx.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:44:55',NULL,NULL),(18886,827,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Uvula </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Uvulae</em></strong>), figuratively, a small grape; </p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Uva</em></strong>, grape</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:45:27',NULL,NULL),(18887,828,13,NULL,'<p>Short for MUSCULUS UVULAE: Muscle “<em>of the Uvula”;</em></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:45:45',NULL,NULL),(18888,828,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Uvulae</em></strong>, <em>“of the Uvula”</em><strong> </strong></p><p>possessive form of<strong> <em>Uvula </em></strong>(L. n.), a small grape</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:45:51',NULL,NULL),(18889,829,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Vagal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:46:11',NULL,NULL),(18890,829,13,NULL,'<p>Taste, smell, sight, imaginings of food stimulate the Medulla Oblongata Digestive Centers and responds by sending action potentials through CN X – Vagus Nerve Parasympathetic fibers, to the Enteric </p><p>Plexus and stimulates secretory activities in the Gastric Pits producing Gastrin, Hormone, and stimulate the Parietal Cells in the Gastric Glands.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:46:17',NULL,NULL),(18891,829,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vagus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), wondering, undetermined</p><p>Metaphor for the undefined pattern of the C.N. X</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:46:24',NULL,NULL),(18892,829,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vagal</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“vague</em>”, having multiple roles</p><p>Too many to enumerate.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Vaga + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Vaga</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:46:37',NULL,NULL),(18893,830,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Vagus</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:46:56',NULL,NULL),(18894,830,13,NULL,'<p>CN X; Named for its multiple function of sensory, motor, sympathetic and parasympathetic influences in the large region of the neck, throat and chest with a variable <em>“wandering” </em>pattern.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:47:04',NULL,NULL),(18895,830,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vagus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), wondering, undetermined</p><p>Metaphor for the undefined pattern of the C.N. X</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:47:10',NULL,NULL),(18896,830,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vagal</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “vague</em>”, having multiple roles</p><p>Too many to enumerate.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Vaga + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Vaga</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:47:20',NULL,NULL),(18897,832,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Vermiform</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:50:23',NULL,NULL),(18898,832,13,NULL,'<p>“<em>worm-like</em>” lymphoid tissues, a lymphoid appendage at the proximal end of the ascending Colon, <strong><em>Caecum .</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:50:31',NULL,NULL),(18899,832,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vermis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Vermes</em></strong>), worm</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:50:38',NULL,NULL),(18900,832,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Vermi- + -formis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Vermis</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-formis</em></strong> (suffix), shaped, looks like, molded&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:50:45',NULL,NULL),(18901,832,12,NULL,'<p>VERMIS – NEUROLOGY</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:50:55',NULL,NULL),(18902,833,13,NULL,'<p>In general, any front entry: opening to the nostril; also, entry chamber between the Semi-circular Canals (Round Window) and the Cochlea (Oval Window), Vaginal Cleft, etc.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:51:16',NULL,NULL),(18903,833,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vestibulum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Vestibula</em></strong>), front entrance court&nbsp;</p><p>metaphorically, <em>“front opening”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:51:22',NULL,NULL),(18904,835,13,NULL,'<p>The strands of mucosae are lined with simple columnar epithelium projecting like Microvilli of Villi, (like short strands of a shaggy carpet) and contains protective and absorptive brush border composed of artery, vein and Lacteals, lymphoid capillary.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:51:53',NULL,NULL),(18905,835,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Villus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Villi</em></strong>), fine hair, vellus hair</p><p>Metaphor for the brush border of absorptive segment of digestive system</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:51:59',NULL,NULL),(18906,836,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Voluntary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:52:18',NULL,NULL),(18907,836,13,NULL,'<p>Chewing and Swallowing is the Voluntary Phase of Digestive System (including defecation, to some extent). After the bolus is pushed by the tongue to the back of the mouth then Involuntary Phase takes over all the way through to the Internal Anal Sphincter (External Anal Sphincter is a voluntary muscle)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:52:26',NULL,NULL),(18908,836,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Velle </em></strong>(L. v.),<strong><em> </em></strong>to will, to intend</p><p><strong><em>Voluntum </em></strong>(past part.), willed, intended<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:52:34',NULL,NULL),(18909,836,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Volunt- + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Voluntum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-arium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ary</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:52:42',NULL,NULL),(18910,836,12,NULL,'<p><strong>VOLUNTARY</strong> MUSCLE – MUSCULAR SYSTEM</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:52:51',NULL,NULL),(18911,837,13,NULL,'<p>Vomiting center in the Medulla Oblongata is stimulated by irritation, by bacterial infection, over-distention, and over stimulation by unwelcome chemical (ex., MSG).</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:53:16',NULL,NULL),(18912,837,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vomere </em></strong>(L. v.),<strong><em> </em></strong>to discharge;</p><p><strong><em>Vomitum </em></strong>(past part.), digestive discharged</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:53:24',NULL,NULL),(18913,838,13,NULL,'<p>Digestive Secretions have H2O components to liquefy the bolus for passage, digestion and absorption; easily reabsorbed in the small and large intestines.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:55:02',NULL,NULL),(18914,839,13,NULL,'<p>Protein Catalyst that increases the rate of chemical reaction by lowering the threshold of activation energy without denaturation.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:55:22',NULL,NULL),(18915,839,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Zymos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), leaven, yeast;</p><p>metaphor for action of yeast&nbsp;</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:55:27',16,'2025-08-11 03:53:41'),(18916,840,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Zymogen</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:55:50',NULL,NULL),(18917,840,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Zymogenic,</strong></p><p>Adj., metaphorically, “actions of leaven”</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:56:03',NULL,NULL),(18918,840,13,NULL,'<p>Precursor to Pepsin, granules are excreted from the Chief Cells by exocytosis.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:56:11',NULL,NULL),(18919,843,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sigmoid</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 10:59:54',NULL,NULL),(18920,843,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Mesecolon,</strong></p><p>Peritoneum that secures the Sigmoid Colon to the pelvic wall</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 11:00:09',NULL,NULL),(18921,843,13,NULL,'<p>Mesentery of the Sigmoid Colon attached to the posterior abdominal wall.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 11:00:16',NULL,NULL),(18922,843,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sigma</em></strong> (18th letter Gr. alphabet; akin to letter S),<strong><em> </em></strong>Σ</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 11:00:22',NULL,NULL),(18923,843,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sigmoid</em></strong> </p><p>Simile, <em>“resembling an</em> S”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Sigma + -oid</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp