15,NULL,'<p><strong>Perinei</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:43:05',NULL,NULL),(18992,3889,13,NULL,'<p>Part of the pelvic floor musculature; Stretches from the inferior rami of the Iscium across the tendinous Raphe of other pelvic floor muscles.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:43:12',NULL,NULL),(18993,3889,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peri-</em></strong> (L. prep.), around</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Anus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Ani</em></strong>), ring (classically, “<em>gold ring”</em>)</p><p>Metaphor for the External Anal Sphincter</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:43:19',NULL,NULL),(18994,3889,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Perinei</em></strong>, </p><p>possessive form of <strong><em>Perineum</em></strong>,</p><p>Figuratively, <em>“surroundings the anus”</em> </p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Peri-</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-nei</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Peri-</em></strong>, around</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-neum</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Anus</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:43:27',NULL,NULL),(18995,3890,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Peritoneum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:45:28',NULL,NULL),(18996,3890,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Visceral,</strong></p><p>Soft fleshy tissue around organs</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:45:35',NULL,NULL),(18997,3890,13,NULL,'<p>Outer, soft fleshy coverings and connective tissue of the organs within the abdominal cavity.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:45:46',NULL,NULL),(18998,3890,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peritoneum</em></strong> (adj.), stretched around</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:45:53',NULL,NULL),(18999,3891,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Propria</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:49:53',NULL,NULL),(19000,3891,13,NULL,'<p>The 2nd layer, Lamina Propria; the three innermost lining of loose connective tissue of the digestive tract are: 1st layer, Mucous Epithelium; 2nd layer, Lamina Propria, 3rd layer, the Mucosae Muscularis is outer thin smooth muscle.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:50:00',NULL,NULL),(19001,3891,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Proprius, -ia, -ium</em></strong> (L. adj), self, one’s own self (?)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:50:04',NULL,NULL),(19002,3892,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reflex</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:53:06',NULL,NULL),(19003,3892,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Gastrocolic,</strong></p><p>Stomach-colon interaction</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:53:15',NULL,NULL),(19004,3892,13,NULL,'<p>Integrate mass movement of chyme in the intestines beginning from the stomach to the entire digestive system.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:53:23',NULL,NULL),(19005,3892,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), back again, repeatedly</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Flectere </em></strong>(v.), to bend, curve;<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Flexum </em></strong>(past part.), bent, curved&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:53:33',NULL,NULL),(19006,3892,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReFlex,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “response back”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Re- + Flex-</u></em><u> + </u><em><u>-ive</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Flexum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 13:53:45',NULL,NULL),(19007,3894,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Tonsils</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 14:03:00',NULL,NULL),(19008,3894,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphoid tissues in the posterior edges of the soft palate</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 14:03:09',NULL,NULL),(19009,3894,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tonsilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tonsillae</em></strong>), glands of the throat</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 14:03:15',NULL,NULL),(19010,3895,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Vestibule</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 14:04:27',NULL,NULL),(19011,3895,13,NULL,'<p>Space between lips and gum / space between cheeks and gum</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 14:04:34',NULL,NULL),(19012,3895,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vestibulum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Vestibula</em></strong>), front entrance court&nbsp;</p><p>metaphorically, <em>“front opening”</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-29 14:04:42',NULL,NULL),(19013,418,12,NULL,'<p><strong>ACCESSORY</strong>&nbsp;NERVE (CN XI) – NERVOUS SYSTEM<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>ACCESORY</strong>&nbsp;(HEMI-AZYGOUS VEIN) - CARDIOVASCULAR</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:19:11',NULL,NULL),(19014,845,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Active</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:43:40',NULL,NULL),(19015,845,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Immunity</strong></p><p>Established ability to defend against pathogens</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:43:49',NULL,NULL),(19016,845,13,NULL,'<p>Active immunity takes place when an individual is naturally or artificially exposed to an antigen, and Adaptive Immunity System mounts a response by producing antibodies. Responses become more robust with every exposure.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:43:56',NULL,NULL),(19017,845,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>A</em>gere</strong> (L. v.), to do, act, perform</p><p><strong><em>Actum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), acted;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:44:07',16,'2025-05-14 00:04:44'),(19018,845,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Active</em></strong></p><p><em>Currently, “deployable, when needed”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Act- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ive</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Actum</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>-ive </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:44:21',16,'2025-05-14 00:08:36'),(19019,846,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Active</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:44:40',NULL,NULL),(19020,846,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Natural Immunity</strong></p><p>Exposure to antigen from environment</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:44:50',NULL,NULL),(19021,846,13,NULL,'<p>Initial Natural exposure to a Pathogen triggers the individual’s immune system to mount an Adaptive Immune System against the antigen and acquire Active Natural Immunity.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:44:58',NULL,NULL),(19022,846,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>A</em>gere</strong> (L. v.), to do, act, perform;</p><p><strong><em>Actum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), acted</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:45:08',16,'2025-05-14 00:10:01'),(19023,846,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Active</em></strong></p><p><em>Currently, “deployable when needed”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Act- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ive</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>Actum</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>-ive </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj., ability</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:45:17',16,'2025-05-14 00:11:09'),(19024,847,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Acute</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:46:15',NULL,NULL),(19025,847,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Rejection</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Incompatible tissue/blood type</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:46:31',16,'2025-05-14 00:11:42'),(19026,847,13,NULL,'<p>Incompatible tissue graft or transplant are attacked by Lymphocytes and Macrophages; a severe inflammatory response takes over and the tissue is destroyed.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:46:39',NULL,NULL),(19027,847,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Acutus, -a, -um </em></strong>(L. adj.), sharp</p><p>Figurative for sudden onset.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:47:02',NULL,NULL),(19028,848,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Adaptive</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:47:29',NULL,NULL),(19029,848,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Immunity</strong></p><p>Established ability to defend against pathogens</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:47:37',16,'2025-05-14 00:12:10'),(19030,848,13,NULL,'<p>Also called Specific Immunity; the body recognizes and destroys foreign substances from memory of past exposure and has developed specific Cellular and Humoral defenses; responses improve rapidly and effectively with repeated exposure; bacteria are destroyed before any symptoms develop and the person is said to be immune.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:47:45',NULL,NULL),(19031,848,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Adaptare</em></strong> (L. v.), to fit, adjust;</p><p><strong><em>Adaptum</em></strong> (past part.), adjusted&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:47:58',16,'2025-05-14 00:12:35'),(19032,848,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Adaptive</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “adapt-ability”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Adapt- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ive</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>Adaptum</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>-ivus </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj.; denotes ability; Eng., -ive</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:48:10',16,'2025-05-14 00:13:00'),(19033,849,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Afferent</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:48:31',NULL,NULL),(19034,849,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Lymphatic Vessels</strong></p><p>Nodes, ducts and ductules of Lymphatic System</p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:48:41',16,'2025-05-14 00:15:35'),(19035,849,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic vessels that carry Lymph Fluid to the Lymph Nodes for filtration; enters the Subcortical Sinus and filters through the Cortex, then through the Medulla, then through the Cortical Sinuses and its Lymphatic Tissue and exit through the Efferent Lymphatic Vessels&nbsp;<strong><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:48:49',NULL,NULL),(19036,849,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, at, towards<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ferre</em></strong> (L. v.), to carry</p><p><strong><em>Ferren</em></strong> (present part.), carrying</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:49:00',16,'2025-05-14 00:15:18'),(19037,849,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AfFerrens</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “carrying towards”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Af- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Ferrens</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>Af-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Ad</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>Ferrens</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:49:14',16,'2025-05-14 00:16:04'),(19038,849,12,NULL,'<p><strong>AFFERENT</strong> ARTERIOLE – URINARY SYSTEM</p><p><strong>AFFERENT</strong> NERVE FIBERS – NEUROLOGY</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:49:38',NULL,NULL),(19039,850,13,NULL,'<p>The immune system may over-react to foreign antigens such as components of bacteria, viruses, and other microorganisms: pollen, animal dander, scales, dried skin, pieces of house dust, mites, foods, drugs.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:50:02',16,'2025-05-14 00:17:06'),(19040,850,8,NULL,'<p><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=allergy&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em>Allos</em> </strong></a>(Gr.&nbsp;adj.), other, different, strange</p><p><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ergones</em></strong>), work</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:50:08',NULL,NULL),(19041,850,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Allergy</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, immune system’s “different work”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em><u>comp.</u></em><strong><em><u>, </u></em></strong><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=allergy&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em><u>&nbsp;All- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ergy</u></em></strong></a></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All- </em></strong><em style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">derived from</em><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em> Allos</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>-ergy</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:50:25',16,'2025-05-14 00:19:51'),(19042,851,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Allergic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:50:50',NULL,NULL),(19043,851,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Reaction</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Swelling, pain, redness</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:50:58',16,'2025-05-14 00:20:46'),(19044,851,13,NULL,'<p>Lipids produced by mast cells, cause smooth muscle relaxation and vasodilation, thus increasing vascular permeability, stimulating pain receptors and inflammation; Histamine, Kinins, Prostaglandins, Leukotrienes, and other cell mediators induce dilation of blood vessels, some trigger IgE mediation of Mast </p><p>Cells and Basophils.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:51:04',NULL,NULL),(19045,851,8,NULL,'<p><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=allergy&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em>Allos</em> </strong></a>(Gr.&nbsp;adj.), other, different, strange</p><p><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ergones</em></strong>), work</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:51:11',NULL,NULL),(19046,851,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Allergy</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, immune system’s “different work”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp., </em><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=allergy&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em><u>&nbsp;All- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-erg- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ic</u></em></strong></a></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong>All-</strong> derived from <strong>Allos</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>-erg-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  &nbsp; &nbsp;  </em></strong><strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; denotes ability</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:51:25',16,'2025-05-14 00:22:32'),(19047,852,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Alternative</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:51:49',NULL,NULL),(19048,852,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Pathways,</strong></p><p>Predetermined course of action by Innate Immunity</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:51:57',16,'2025-05-14 00:23:49'),(19049,852,13,NULL,'<p>A form of Innate Immunity; initiated when the complement protein C3 becomes activated and combines with foreign substances like bacteria or virus, marking them for lysis.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:52:04',NULL,NULL),(19050,852,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Alterare</em></strong> (L. v.), to change;</p><p><strong><em>Alternatum</em></strong> (past part.), changed&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:52:13',NULL,NULL),(19052,852,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Alternatum </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ive</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Alternatum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ivus </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj., denotes function; Eng., -ive</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:52:46',16,'2025-05-14 00:23:32'),(19053,853,13,NULL,'<p>Sudden onset; commonly caused by errant Medication, allergy, and bee stings which trigger IgE mediation of Mast Cells and Basophils producing massive systemic vasodilation causing a dangerously sudden drop in blood pressure, shock; an E.R event.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:53:06',16,'2025-05-14 00:25:07'),(19054,853,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>An</em></strong> (L. prep), negative sense, against, without</p><p><strong><em>Phylaxis </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Phylaxes</em></strong>), precaution,&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:53:14',NULL,NULL),(19055,853,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AnaPhylaxis</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “without warning”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Ana- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Phylaxis</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ana- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> An</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Phylaxis</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:53:24',16,'2025-05-14 00:25:40'),(19056,854,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Anaphylactic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:53:50',NULL,NULL),(19057,854,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Shock</strong></p><p>Sudden drop of blood pressure</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:53:59',16,'2025-05-14 00:26:03'),(19058,854,13,NULL,'<p>Describes a systemic allergic re-action that suddenly drops blood pressure (shock) caused by systemic vasodilation that could be fatal; an ER event.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:54:10',NULL,NULL),(19059,854,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>An</em></strong> (L. prep), negative sense, against, without</p><p><strong><em>Phylaxis </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Phylaxes</em></strong>), precaution,&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:54:20',NULL,NULL),(19060,854,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AnaPhylactic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically</em><strong><em>,</em></strong><em> “condition without warning</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Ana- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Phylaxis</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ana-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> An</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Phylaxis</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; denotes ability</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:54:30',16,'2025-05-14 00:26:15'),(19061,855,13,NULL,'<p>Blocking, altering, or deleting an antigen receptor prevent activation of B- or T-cells from responding to an antigen; when the antigen complex binds to the receptor no co-stimulation occurs.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:54:50',16,'2025-05-14 00:26:42'),(19062,855,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>An</em></strong> (L. prep.), negative sense, against, without</p><p><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ergones</em></strong>), work</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:54:57',NULL,NULL),(19063,855,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AnErgon,&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “absence of work”</em></p><p><em><u>&nbsp;</u></em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>An </u></em><u>+ </u><em><u>Ergon</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>An</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ergon</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:55:08',16,'2025-05-14 00:26:53'),(19064,856,13,NULL,'<p>Against</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:55:26',NULL,NULL),(19065,856,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Anti</em></strong> (L. prep.), opposite, against</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:55:32',NULL,NULL),(19066,857,13,NULL,'<p>T-cells give rise to cells that produce proteins called Antibodies, which inhabit the plasma; this </p><p>process embodies Antibody Mediated Immunity</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:56:08',NULL,NULL),(19067,857,13,NULL,'<p>Produced in response to antigenic pathogen; large amounts occur in plasma; also known as Gammaglobulins and Immunoglobulins: IgA, IgD, IgE, IgG, IgM.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:56:15',NULL,NULL),(19068,857,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Anti</em></strong> (prep.), opposite, against</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:56:20',NULL,NULL),(19069,858,13,NULL,'<p>Substances that enter (infect) the body, or part of the host body, stimulate production of antibodies, any foreign body, organism, or host cell that triggers Adaptive Immune defense to mount a defensive response; they usually are molecules with a molecular weight of 10,000 or more</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:56:39',NULL,NULL),(19070,858,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Anti</em></strong> (L. prep.), opposite, against</p><p><strong><em>Genitor</em></strong> (L. n.), father, begetter<strong><em>,</em></strong> producer</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:56:45',NULL,NULL),(19071,858,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Antigen,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “triggers antibody production”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Anti </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-gen </u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Anti</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-gen</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Genitor</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:56:56',NULL,NULL),(19072,859,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Antigenic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:57:25',NULL,NULL),(19073,859,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Determinants</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Markers that triggers for immune response</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:57:33',16,'2025-05-14 00:28:08'),(19074,859,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., EPITOPES; the specific part of Antigen that binds to receptors on the surface of lymphocytes initiating the immune system response.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:57:43',NULL,NULL),(19075,859,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Anti</em></strong> (L. prep.), opposite, against</p><p><strong><em>Genitor</em></strong> (L. n.), father, begetter<strong><em>,</em></strong> producer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:57:52',NULL,NULL),(19076,859,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Antigenic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “generation of antibodies”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Anti </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-gen </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><u>-</u><em><u>icus</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Anti</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-gen</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Genitor</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ic</em></strong> (suffix), forms adj.; denotes ability<strong> </strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:58:02',16,'2025-05-14 00:27:53'),(19077,860,13,NULL,'<p>Plasma extracted from clotting factors that contain antibodies are responsible for artificial immunity; used as vaccine against common childhood diseases.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:58:22',NULL,NULL),(19078,860,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Anti</em></strong> (L. prep.), opposite, against</p><p><strong><em>Serum</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Sera</em></strong>), watery part of milk, whey</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:58:28',NULL,NULL),(19079,860,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Anti </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Serum</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Anti</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Serum</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 01:58:45',16,'2025-05-14 00:28:41'),(19080,861,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Arthus</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:01:06',NULL,NULL),(19081,861,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Reaction</strong></p><p>Allergic reaction</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:01:16',16,'2025-05-14 00:29:20'),(19082,861,13,NULL,'<p>Localized immune reaction characterized by localized inflammation caused by repeated dermal vaccine application; Neutrophil infiltration, and tissue Necrosis.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:01:35',NULL,NULL),(19083,861,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Arthus</em></strong>, Nicholas Maurice, described localized skin reaction due to repeated vaccination of tetanus toxoid</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:01:41',16,'2025-05-14 00:29:03'),(19084,862,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Artificial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:02:06',NULL,NULL),(19085,862,13,NULL,'<p>An antigen is introduced into the body by Vaccination to stimulate production of the specific Antibodies against specific Antigen. Passive Artificial Immunity begins with vaccinating an animal such as a horse with the intended antigen; the animals’ immune system responds to the antigen and produce antibodies; serum is extracted from the animal and injected into humans for artificial preventive immunity.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:02:13',NULL,NULL),(19086,862,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Artificium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Artificia</em></strong>), craftsmanship, trickery</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:02:20',NULL,NULL),(19087,862,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Artificia </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Artificia</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:02:29',16,'2025-05-14 00:29:48'),(19088,863,13,NULL,'<p>Localized IgE mediated hypersensitivity reaction; pollens are allergens that cause hay fever resulting in localize upper respiratory mucosal inflammation; allergens can stimulate the release of Histamines to the</p><p>Bronchi causing constriction of Bronchioles (Asthma).</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:02:52',NULL,NULL),(19089,863,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>An </em></strong>(L. prep.), against, without, negative sense </p><p><strong><em>Topos </em></strong>(Gr.<strong><em> </em></strong>n.), place</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:02:57',NULL,NULL),(19090,863,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ATopia</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>off-site”</em> condition</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>A- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Topos </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ia</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>A-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> An </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Topos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ia </em></strong>(suffix), denotes condition, state (Absentia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:03:09',16,'2025-05-14 00:30:54'),(19091,864,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Autoimmune</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:03:31',NULL,NULL),(19092,864,13,NULL,'<p>Hyperactive immune reaction caused by Self-antigens that stimulate unwanted tissue destruction (ex, inflammatory Arthritis); a pathology akin to allergic reaction or Hypersensitivity.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:03:37',16,'2025-05-14 00:32:20'),(19093,864,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Auto</em></strong> (L. prep.), self</p><p><strong><em>Im- </em></strong>(L. prefix), negative sense (Immature, Insane)</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(L. n.), classically, </span><em style=\"background-color: white;\">civic duties</em><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> </span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:03:43',NULL,NULL),(19094,864,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis</em></strong></p><p><em>classical sense: \"exempt from common civic duty”</em></p><p><em>Metaphor for exception from</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“plague”</em></p><p><em>Imagine the plague. Lots of history behind this term.</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>comp., <u>Auto- + Im- + </u></em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em><u>Mūnis</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Auto- </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Im- </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:04:02',16,'2025-05-14 00:33:07'),(19095,865,13,NULL,'<p>(Microbiology), One-celled organism, spherical, spiral, or rod shaped and appearing singly or in chains, comprising of Schizomycota, a Phylum of the Kingdom Monera; involved in fermentation, putrefaction, infectious diseases, or nitrogen fixation.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:04:59',16,'2025-05-14 00:34:22'),(19096,865,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Bakterion </em></strong>(Gr. n.; plu., <strong><em>Bakteria</em></strong>), staff, stick</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:05:06',NULL,NULL),(19097,866,13,NULL,'<p>Motile cells that leave the blood stream, enter the area of injured tissues and release chemicals that promote inflammation; in microscopy, attracted to basic dye.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:06:00',NULL,NULL),(19098,866,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Basis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Bases</em></strong>), bottom support, foundation </p><p><strong><em>Philos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), affinity, attraction, liking</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:06:07',NULL,NULL),(19099,866,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Basophilic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “attracted to basic dye”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Baso- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-phil </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Basis</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-phil</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Philos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em></strong> (suffix), forms adj.; denotes ability<strong> </strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:06:38',16,'2025-05-14 00:35:21'),(19100,867,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Basophilic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:07:12',NULL,NULL),(19101,867,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Early Erythroblasts</strong></p><p>Immature RBC</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:07:22',NULL,NULL),(19102,867,13,NULL,'<p>Proliferating immature White blood cells with granules that stain with basic dyes for microscopy; promotes inflammatory reaction.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:07:28',16,'2025-05-14 00:35:46'),(19103,867,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Basis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Bases</em></strong>), bottom support, foundation </p><p><strong><em>Philos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), affinity, attraction, liking</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:07:35',NULL,NULL),(19104,867,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Basophilic</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “loves basic dye”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Baso- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-phil </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Basis</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-phil</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Philos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em></strong> (suffix), forms adj.; denotes ability<strong> </strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:07:55',16,'2025-05-14 00:36:08'),(19105,868,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Bronchomediastinal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:08:16',NULL,NULL),(19106,868,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Trunks</strong></p><p>Bundled group of lymphatic vessels</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:08:24',16,'2025-05-14 00:36:32'),(19107,868,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic Bronchomediastinal Trunks drain lymph from the thoracic organs and the deep thoracic wall.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:08:31',NULL,NULL),(19108,868,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Bronchus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Bronchi</em></strong>), windpipe</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Mediastinum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Mediastina), </em></strong>mid-sternum</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:08:37',16,'2025-05-14 00:36:41'),(19109,868,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>BronchoMediastinal</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “middle of the breastbone”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Broncho- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Mediastin-</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Bronchus</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Mediastinum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:08:55',16,'2025-05-14 00:36:54'),(19110,869,13,NULL,'<p>Outer coat of Lymph Nodes composed of dense connective tissue.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:09:14',NULL,NULL),(19111,869,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capsulus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Capsuli</em></strong>), Classically, small tube for storage;</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Capsa, </em></strong>tubes for storage of written scrolls;</p><p>metaphor for hard outer coat.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:09:19',16,'2025-05-14 00:37:39'),(19112,869,12,NULL,'<p><strong>CAPSULE</strong>, JOINT – JOINT SYSTEM</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:09:36',NULL,NULL),(19113,871,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cell</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:11:56',NULL,NULL),(19114,871,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Mediated Immunity</strong></p><p>Promoting or inhibiting immunity</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:12:08',16,'2025-05-14 00:38:16'),(19115,871,13,NULL,'<p>A series of T-cells, regulatory T-helper cells, T-suppressor cells either promote or inhibit the activities of both Antibody Mediated Immunity and Cell Mediated Immunity becoming Effector, Cytotoxic, and </p><p>Delayed Hypersensitivity.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:12:14',NULL,NULL),(19116,871,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cella </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Cellae</em></strong>), room</p><p><strong><em>Cytos</em></strong> (Gr. n), cell</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:12:21',NULL,NULL),(19117,872,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Chemical</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:12:47',NULL,NULL),(19118,872,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Mediators,</strong></p><p>trigger other inflammatory factors to join in</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:12:55',16,'2025-05-14 00:39:27'),(19119,872,13,NULL,'<p>Lysozyme found in the skin and mucus linings kill microorganisms or prevent their entry; chemicals such as Histamine promote inflammation by causing vasodilation; increasing vascular permeability, attracting white blood cells, stimulating phagocytes; Interferons kill viruses.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:13:06',NULL,NULL),(19120,872,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chemia </em></strong>(Gr. n.), Alchemy</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:13:22',NULL,NULL),(19121,872,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Chemic- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Chemic-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Chemia</em></strong></p><p><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:13:30',16,'2025-05-14 00:53:40'),(19122,873,13,NULL,'<p>A mode of WBC movement for phagocytosis when attracted by chemical stimulus from foreign body, </p><p>infectious foreign material, bacterial particles, dead cells, dirt, dust, pollen, etc.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:13:46',NULL,NULL),(19123,873,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chemia </em></strong>(Gr. n.), Alchemy <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Taxis </em></strong>(Gr. n.), arrangement, in order;</p><p><strong><em>Tassein </em></strong>(Gr. v.), to set in order</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:13:56',NULL,NULL),(19124,873,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ChemoTaxis</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “to put the infection to rest”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Chemo- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Taxis</u></em> </strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Chemo-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Chemia </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Taxis</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:14:06',16,'2025-05-14 00:54:32'),(19125,874,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Chemotactic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:18:39',NULL,NULL),(19126,874,13,NULL,'<p>Parcels of microbes or chemicals released by dead tissue cells serve as chemical signals to attract white </p><p>blood cells and cause them to move towards the source of the chemical signals; they diffuse out from area where they are released.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:18:45',NULL,NULL),(19127,874,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chemia </em></strong>(Gr. n.), Alchemy <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Taxis </em></strong>(Gr. n.), arrangement, in order;</p><p><strong><em>Tassein </em></strong>(Gr. v.), to set in order</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:19:05',NULL,NULL),(19128,874,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ChemoTaxis</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “to put the infection in order”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Chemo- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>Taxis</u></em> </strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Chemo-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Chemia </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Taxis</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:19:18',16,'2025-05-14 00:54:56'),(19129,876,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Chronic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:20:44',NULL,NULL),(19130,876,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Condition</strong></p><p>Disease/illness</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:20:52',16,'2025-05-14 00:56:22'),(19131,876,13,NULL,'<p>A pathology of long duration with frequent re-occurrence-remission. Repeated <em>“ebb and flow”</em> of relapse, and recovery.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:21:01',NULL,NULL),(19132,876,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chronos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), time</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:21:13',NULL,NULL),(19133,876,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chronic</em></strong></p><p>literally, <em>“time” </em>and again</p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Chronos </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Chronos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; property</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:21:21',16,'2025-05-14 00:56:32'),(19134,877,13,NULL,'<p>The lymphatic fluid passing through lymphatic vessels appears milky due to its fat content </p><p>“<em>rawfruit or animal juice”</em></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:22:45',NULL,NULL),(19135,877,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Chylus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Chyli</em></strong>), <em>“raw fruit or animal juice”</em></p><p>metaphor of <em>“digestive secretion”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:22:51',NULL,NULL),(19136,877,12,NULL,'<p>CHYLOMICRON</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:22:59',NULL,NULL),(19137,878,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cisterna</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:23:29',NULL,NULL),(19138,878,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Chyli</strong></p><p><em>“Of the lymph fluid”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:23:41',16,'2025-05-14 00:58:26'),(19139,878,13,NULL,'<p>A group of Lymphatic trunks merge and form a sac resembling a reservoir.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:23:47',NULL,NULL),(19140,878,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cisterna</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cisternae</em></strong>), a water jug, reservoir</p><p>figuratively, <em>“lymph fluid reserve”&nbsp;</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:23:54',NULL,NULL),(19142,878,12,NULL,'<p>CISTERNA / CISTERN – MUSCLE PHYSIOLOGY</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:24:25',NULL,NULL),(19143,879,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Classical</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:26:03',NULL,NULL),(19144,879,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Pathways</strong></p><p>Course of action for Complement proteins</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:26:11',16,'2025-05-14 00:58:49'),(19145,879,13,NULL,'<p>Part of the Complement Cascade that leads to Adaptive Immunity.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:26:17',NULL,NULL),(19146,879,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Classical</strong>, sense of default pathway</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:26:31',NULL,NULL),(19147,880,13,NULL,'<p>Small groups of identical B- and T-Lymphocytes respond to antigens by duplicating themselves from small </p><p>groups of identical lymphocytes to large number of clones; they are pre-existing in the immune system that can react to most antigenic particles; some clones can also respond to self- antigens.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:26:48',NULL,NULL),(19148,880,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Clonus / Klon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), a branch or twig of a plant able to sprout identical plant </p><p>This is the origin of <strong><em>Cloning,</em></strong><em> </em><strong><em>Clones</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:26:55',NULL,NULL),(19149,881,13,NULL,'<p>Part of mother’s milk that contain antibodies that protect the infant with undeveloped immune system</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:27:16',NULL,NULL),(19150,881,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Colustrum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Colustra</em></strong>), foremilk, watery milk</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:27:22',NULL,NULL),(19151,882,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Complement</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:27:46',NULL,NULL),(19152,882,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Cascade</strong></p><p>A chain of activated proteins leading to clotting</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:27:54',16,'2025-05-14 00:59:20'),(19153,882,13,NULL,'<p>Complement protein becomes activated in the complement chain in which each component of the series activates the next component to launch a concerted innate and adaptive defense&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:28:01',NULL,NULL),(19154,882,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Complement </strong>(Eng. n.), sense of enhancement</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:28:07',NULL,NULL),(19155,883,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Complement</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:28:25',NULL,NULL),(19156,883,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Protein</strong></p><p>Activated to fight infection</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:28:31',16,'2025-05-14 00:59:57'),(19157,883,13,NULL,'<p>The group of 20 proteins that make up 10% of the Globulin component in Serum that are activated in a series of reaction to an infection, or presence of an Antigen.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:28:38',NULL,NULL),(19158,883,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Complement </strong>(Eng. n.), sense of enhancement, completeness</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:28:45',NULL,NULL),(19159,884,13,NULL,'<p>Outer coat of Lymphatic nodes, gland, outer layer of the brain, or bones, kidneys.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:29:04',NULL,NULL),(19160,884,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cortex</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cortices</em></strong>), nutshell, coat of seeds&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:29:11',NULL,NULL),(19161,885,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cortex</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:29:29',NULL,NULL),(19162,885,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>of Lymph Nodes</strong></p><p>Bean shaped structures 1 to 25 mm in size</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:30:36',16,'2025-05-14 01:00:23'),(19163,885,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of subcapsular sinus beneath the Lymphatic node capsule, cortical sinuses which are separated </p><p>by Diffuse Lymphatic Tissue, Trabeculae, and Lymphatic Nodules.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:30:44',NULL,NULL),(19164,885,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cortex</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cortices</em></strong>), nutshell, coat of seeds </p><p>Coat, capsule of lymph nodes&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:30:49',NULL,NULL),(19165,886,13,NULL,'<p>After the B- or T-cell mount a defense, other cells send signals for co-stimulation by way of molecules released from cells and molecules attached to the surface of the infected or dead cells or infectious </p><p>foreign body</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:31:24',NULL,NULL),(19166,886,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cum</em></strong> (L. prep), with, along with<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Stimulare</em></strong> (L. v.),<strong><em> </em></strong>goad, incite;</p><p><strong><em>Stimulatum </em></strong>(past part.), prodded, incited<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:31:35',NULL,NULL),(19167,886,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>CoStimulation</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, signals to “rally”</em> other cells to fight</p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Co- + Stimulat- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Co-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Cum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Stimulatum </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-io(nes)</em> </strong>(suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:31:46',16,'2025-05-14 01:00:51'),(19168,887,13,NULL,'<p>Proteins or peptides are co-stimulators secreted by<span style=\"color: red;\"> </span>cells for communication with neighboring cells; regulate </p><p>immunity, inflammation, tissue repair, cell growth and other immune processes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:32:03',NULL,NULL),(19169,887,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p><p><strong><em>Kinesis </em></strong>(Gr. n.), movement<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:32:08',NULL,NULL),(19170,887,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cytokinin</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “protein that rally cells” </em>to act</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cyto- + kin- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Cytos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Kin-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Kinesis </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-in </em></strong>(suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:32:19',16,'2025-05-14 01:01:50'),(19171,888,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cytotoxic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:34:00',NULL,NULL),(19172,888,13,NULL,'<p>IgG and IgM attach on the surface of the Antigen, activating a complement cascade; they lyse the infected cell and produce cytokines that activate other components of the immune system; Perforin opens </p><p>through the cell membrane for sodium and water to enter and kill infected cells.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:34:08',NULL,NULL),(19173,888,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Cytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Tox</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Toxes</em></strong>), harm, poison</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:34:15',16,'2025-05-14 01:02:52'),(19174,888,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>CytoToxic</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for poisoning of infected cells</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cyto- + Tox + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Cyto-</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Tox</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:34:24',16,'2025-05-14 01:02:38'),(19175,889,13,NULL,'<p>Instead of responses that eliminate antigen, Immature Lymphocytes exposed to the antigens respond </p><p>by dying due to exposure to self-antigens; this process eliminates self-reactive lymphocytes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:34:43',NULL,NULL),(19176,889,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Deletere </em></strong>(L. v.), to destroy;</p><p><strong><em>Deletum </em></strong>(past part.), destroyed&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:34:58',NULL,NULL),(19177,889,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Deletion</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “elimination by suicide”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Delet- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Deletum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ion(s)</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:35:08',16,'2025-05-14 01:03:10'),(19178,890,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Dendritic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:35:32',NULL,NULL),(19179,890,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Cell</strong></p><p>Cell with long cytoplasmic processes</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:35:39',16,'2025-05-14 01:03:43'),(19180,890,13,NULL,'<p>Large (<strong><em>Dendron,</em></strong> tree) <em>“tree-like” </em>cells with long cytoplasmic extensions capable of taking up and concentrating antigens to activate B- or T-lymphocytes.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:35:45',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO `termline` VALUES (19181,890,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dendron </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Dendra</em></strong>), tree; fruit tree</p><p>Metaphor for dendrons, dendrites branching out</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:35:51',NULL,NULL),(19182,890,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dendritic </em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for the cell possessing dendrites</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Dendron + -ites + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Dendron </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ites </em></strong>(suffix), denotes part of a body (e.g., somite)</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:36:16',16,'2025-05-14 01:04:01'),(19183,890,12,NULL,'<p>DENDRITES - NEUROLOGY</p><p>DENDRON – NEUROLOGY</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:36:31',NULL,NULL),(19184,892,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Diffused</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:37:15',NULL,NULL),(19185,892,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Lymphatic Tissue</strong></p><p>In and around lymphatic nodes/spleen</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:37:24',16,'2025-05-14 01:06:42'),(19186,892,13,NULL,'<p>Contains widely distributed lymphocytes, macrophages, and other cells; blend with the surrounding tissues located in the mucous membranes around lymphatic nodules, on and inside the lymphatic nodes and spleen.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:37:32',NULL,NULL),(19187,892,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diffidere </em></strong>(L. v.), to spread out, pour forth;</p><p><strong><em>Diffusum </em></strong>(past part.), poured around&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:37:40',NULL,NULL),(19188,892,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diffusion</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “spread out and around”</em></p><p><em>Of lymphatic tissue</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Diffus- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Diffusum </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-io(nes)</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:37:52',16,'2025-05-14 01:06:27'),(19189,892,12,NULL,'<p>DIFFUSION - CARDIOVASCULAR</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:38:04',NULL,NULL),(19190,893,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Efferent</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:38:35',NULL,NULL),(19191,893,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Lymphatic Vessels</strong></p><p>Afferent → nodes → Efferent</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:38:43',16,'2025-05-14 01:07:24'),(19192,893,13,NULL,'<p>An Efferent Vessel of one lymph node continues as the Afferent Vessels of next node or may converge to form Lymphatic Trunks.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:38:54',NULL,NULL),(19193,893,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ex </em></strong>(L. prep.), from, out of, off<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ferre </em></strong>(L. v.), to carry;</p><p><strong><em>Ferrens </em></strong>(present part.), carrying&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:39:04',NULL,NULL),(19194,893,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EFerrens,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “carrying from”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>E- + Ferrens</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>E-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Ex</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Ferrens</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:39:22',16,'2025-05-14 01:07:09'),(19195,894,13,NULL,'<p>WBC with cytoplasmic granules that stains bright red with acidic dye; inhibits inflammation by </p><p>neutralizing Histamine; also fight parasites.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:39:42',NULL,NULL),(19196,894,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Eos </em></strong>(Gr. n.) classically, red “<em>Greek goddess of dawn</em>”</p><p><strong><em>Philos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), attraction, affinity, liking, love</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:39:50',NULL,NULL),(19197,894,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Eosinophil</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “attracted to red dye”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em>Eosino- + -phil</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Eosino-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Eos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-phil</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Philos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:40:03',16,'2025-05-14 01:08:00'),(19198,895,13,NULL,'<p>The specific part of Antigen that binds to receptors on the surface of lymphocytes initiating the </p><p>immune system response.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:40:21',NULL,NULL),(19199,895,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p><p><strong><em>Topos </em></strong>(Gr.<strong><em> </em></strong>n.), place</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:40:28',NULL,NULL),(19200,895,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EpiTopes</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “surface receptors of the antigen”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Epi- + Topos</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Epi-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Apices</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Topos</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:40:38',16,'2025-05-14 01:08:28'),(19201,896,13,NULL,'<p>Juvenile Red Blood Cells from Stem Cells; become Pro-erythroblasts, subsequently, mature as Early, then</p><p>Intermediate, to Late Erythroblasts before maturing to RBC.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:41:12',NULL,NULL),(19202,896,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Blastos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), sprout, bud, germinal cells</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:41:18',16,'2025-05-14 01:08:52'),(19203,896,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ErythroBlast</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “germinal </em>Red Blood Cells<em>”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + -Blast</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Erythros </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Blastos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:41:29',16,'2025-05-14 01:09:02'),(19204,898,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Erythroblastosis</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:41:56',NULL,NULL),(19205,898,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Fetalis</strong></p><p>Of the newborn</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:42:06',16,'2025-05-14 01:09:31'),(19206,898,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., Hemolytic Disease of the Newborn; the mother develops Antibodies against an incompatible fetal blood; a high risk of system-wide circulatory clotting for the mother.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:42:14',NULL,NULL),(19207,898,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Erythros </em></strong>(Gk. adj.), red, reddish</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Blastos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), sprout, bud, germinal cells</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:42:20',16,'2025-05-14 01:09:39'),(19208,898,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ErythroBlastosis</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, a “condition of immature RBC”</em></p><p><em>abnormal high count</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Erythro- + -Blast</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Erythros </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Blastos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-osis</em></strong> (comb. suffix), denotes pathology</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:42:33',16,'2025-05-14 01:09:52'),(19209,900,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Germinal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:43:08',NULL,NULL),(19210,900,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Centers</strong></p><p>Diffused tissues, lymph nodes/nodules, Spleen</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:43:19',16,'2025-05-14 01:10:21'),(19211,900,13,NULL,'<p>An area of lymphocyte production by cell division is released into the lymphatic system and eventually </p><p>circulated in the blood stream;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:43:25',NULL,NULL),(19212,900,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Germen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Germines</em></strong>), sprout,<em> </em>growing shoots</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:43:32',NULL,NULL),(19213,900,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Germin- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Germines</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:43:47',16,'2025-05-14 01:10:35'),(19214,901,13,NULL,'<p>Small molecules capable of combining (attaching) with larger molecules like blood proteins to initiate an Adaptive Immune System response.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:44:11',NULL,NULL),(19215,901,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hapten </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Haptines</em></strong>), fastener</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:44:19',NULL,NULL),(19216,902,13,NULL,'<p>The Splenic Artery enters the Spleen at the Hilum, the narrow stem and entry to the spleen; the artery branches out to the various Trabeculae within the Spleen.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:44:39',NULL,NULL),(19217,902,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hilum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Hila</em></strong>), a small trifle, unimportant thing</p><p>(Classical sarcasm?)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:44:44',NULL,NULL),(19218,903,13,NULL,'<p>Protein produced by the decomposition of Histidine tissue. Released from Mast Cells, Basophils, and Platelets; facilitates inflammatory and allergic reaction by vasodilation, vascular permeability; stimulates glandular secretions specially mucus and tears.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:45:03',NULL,NULL),(19219,903,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Histidine </em></strong>(Biochemistry), an essential amino acid</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Amine</em></strong> (Biochemistry), any class of compounds </p><p>derived from ammonia<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:45:10',NULL,NULL),(19220,903,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HistAmine</em></strong></p><p><em>Product of Histidine decomposition</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Hist- + Amine</u></em><u> </u></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Hist-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Histidine</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Amine</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:45:24',16,'2025-05-14 01:11:03'),(19221,904,13,NULL,'<p>(Biochemistry) An essential amino acid constituent of proteins essential for the iron binding site of Hemoglobin&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:45:43',NULL,NULL),(19222,904,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Histidine </em></strong>(Biochemistry), an essential amino acid</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:45:49',NULL,NULL),(19223,905,13,NULL,'<p>Condition of cells or tissues transplanted from the donor to the recipient having similar antigen; such that they are not rejected or phagocytized.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:46:10',NULL,NULL),(19224,905,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Histos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), classically,<em> “fine weave of loom”</em>; metaphor for<em> </em>tissue </p><p><strong><em>Cum</em></strong> (L. prep), with, along with </p><p><strong><em>Pathos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), sensitivity, strong feeling, suffering </p><p><strong><em>Abilitas</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Abilitates</em></strong>), characteristic</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:46:16',NULL,NULL),(19225,905,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HistoComPatibilitas</em></strong></p><p><em>With “strong-feelings</em>”</p><p>metaphor for tissues “<em>matching”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Histo- + Com- + Pathos + Abilitas</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Histo-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Histos</em></strong><em> </em></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Com-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Cum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Pathos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Abilitas</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:46:43',16,'2025-05-14 01:11:42'),(19226,906,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Humoral</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:47:08',NULL,NULL),(19227,906,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Immunity</strong></p><p>Antibody armed immunity</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:47:16',16,'2025-05-14 01:12:11'),(19228,906,13,NULL,'<p>Also called Antibody-Mediated Immunity: initiated by an encounter with a pathogen (Antigen) through infection or by vaccination; T- and B-lymphocytes produce proteins called antibodies to fight the current </p><p>exposure and in future infections; becomes more efficient with each encounter.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:47:26',NULL,NULL),(19229,906,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Humor</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Humores</em></strong>), bodily fluid</p><p>Metaphor for antibodies in plasma</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:47:32',NULL,NULL),(19230,906,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Humor + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Humor</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:47:39',16,'2025-05-14 01:12:28'),(19231,906,12,NULL,'<p>HUMOR, VITREOUS&nbsp;</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:47:51',NULL,NULL),(19232,907,13,NULL,'<p>Hyperactive Immune Response (ex., Rhinitis, caused by fine dust, pollen, dander) caused by Self-antigens </p><p>that stimulate unwanted tissue destruction. Hypersensitivity and Immunity reactions developed out </p><p>of the same mechanism; both require exposure to an antigen; later exposure stimulates much the same </p><p>process that occurs during normal immune system response.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:57:03',NULL,NULL),(19233,907,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hyper-</em></strong> (L. prefix), over the top, excessive, above<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Sentire</em></strong> (L. v.), to feel;</p><p><strong><em>Sensum </em></strong>(past part.), felt<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:57:10',NULL,NULL),(19234,907,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HyperSensitivitas,</em></strong></p><p><em>“Excessive feeling”</em></p><p><em>Metaphor for over-reaction to allergens</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Hyper + Sens- + -ive + -itas</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Hyper-</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Sens-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> sensum </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ivus </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj., denotes function</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-itas</em> </strong>(suffix), forms noun</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:57:31',16,'2025-05-14 01:13:09'),(19235,908,13,NULL,'<p>Describes a person who has built up the ability (Antibodies) to fight off an infection or foreign body (Antigen) before symptoms develop.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:57:56',NULL,NULL),(19236,908,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im- </em></strong>(L. prefix), negative sense (Immature, Insane)</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(L. n.), classically, </span><em style=\"background-color: white;\">civic duties</em><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> </span></p><p>Metaphor for societal <em>“epidemic disease”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:58:03',NULL,NULL),(19237,908,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis,</em></strong></p><p><em>classical sense, \"exempt from common civic duty”</em></p><p><em>Metaphor for exception from epidemic “disease”</em></p><p><em>Imagine the plague. Lots of history behind the term.</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Im- + </u></em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em><u>Mūnis</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Im- </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:58:27',16,'2025-05-14 01:32:38'),(19238,909,13,NULL,'<p>Modern Medicine: a sense of <em>\"protection from epidemic, pandemic\"</em>; the ability to resist damage from foreign substances such as microorganisms and harmful chemicals.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:58:45',16,'2025-05-14 01:33:23'),(19239,909,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im- </em></strong>(L. prefix), negative sense (Immature, Insane)</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(L. n.), classically, </span><em style=\"background-color: white;\">civic duties</em><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> </span></p><p>Metaphor for societal <em>“epidemic disease”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:58:52',NULL,NULL),(19240,909,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis,</em></strong></p><p><em>classical sense, \"exempt from common civic duty”</em></p><p><em>Metaphor for exception from epidemic “disease”</em></p><p><em>Imagine the plague. Lots of history behind the term.</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Im- + </u></em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em><u>Mūnis</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Im- </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 02:59:03',16,'2025-05-14 01:33:07'),(19241,916,13,NULL,'<p>Process of intentionally introducing antigen into the body by Vaccination to generate antibodies actively against common diseases.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:00:41',NULL,NULL),(19242,916,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im- </em></strong>(L. prefix), negative sense (Immature, Insane)</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis </em></strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(L. n.), classically, </span><em style=\"background-color: white;\">civic duties</em><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> </span></p><p>Metaphor for societal <em>“epidemic disease”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:00:47',NULL,NULL),(19243,916,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Im</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis,</em></strong></p><p><em>classical sense, \"exempt from common civic duty”</em></p><p><em>Metaphor for exception from epidemic “disease”</em></p><p><em>Imagine the plague. Lots of history behind the term.</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Im- + </u></em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em><u>Mūnis</u></em></strong><strong><em><u> + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Im- </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Mūnis </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ation</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:01:06',16,'2025-05-14 01:33:50'),(19244,917,13,NULL,'<p>Inflammation is achieved by mediators of inflammation released or activated in the tissue by blood vessels dilation and permeability; Histamine, Kinins, Prostaglandins, Leukotrienes, and other cell mediators induced dilation of blood vessels, trigger inflammation, stimulate pain receptors, and increase the permeability of blood vessels; red bone marrow rally to produce and release large numbers of neutrophils which promote </p><p>Phagocytosis and pyrogens.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:01:29',NULL,NULL),(19245,917,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>In-</em></strong> (L. prep.), in, within</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Flammare </em></strong>(L. v.), to set on fire;</p><p><strong><em>Flammatum</em></strong> (past part.), set on fire</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:01:37',NULL,NULL),(19246,917,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>InFlammation</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “setting on fire”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>In- + Flammat- + -ion</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>In-</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Flammatum</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ion</em></strong>, (suffix), denotes noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:01:46',16,'2025-05-14 01:34:25'),(19247,918,13,NULL,'<p>The function/property of producing inflammation.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:02:38',NULL,NULL),(19248,918,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>In-</em></strong> (L. prep.), in, within</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Flammare </em></strong>(L. v.), to set on fire;</p><p><strong><em>Flammatum</em></strong> (past part.), set on fire</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:02:46',NULL,NULL),(19249,918,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>InFlammatory</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “function to inflame”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>In- + Flammat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>In-</em></strong>, within</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Flammatum</em></strong>, set on fire</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function, location; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:02:54',16,'2025-05-14 01:34:59'),(19250,919,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Innate</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:03:22',NULL,NULL),(19252,919,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Immunity</strong></p><p>Classically, <strong>Im&nbsp;Muni- </strong>-itas, “exempt from payment; exempt from COVID”</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:03:59',NULL,NULL),(19253,919,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., Non-specific Resistance; generalized mechanical and chemical defenses in the tissue, such as the </p><p>skin, mucous membranes, tears in the eyes, saliva and the urinary tract, ciliated mucous membrane, and the </p><p>mucous membranes in the digestive system, coughing and sneezing; the body recognizes and destroy certain </p><p>foreign substances without prior exposure.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:04:05',NULL,NULL),(19254,919,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Innascere </em></strong>(L. v.), to be born in </p><p><strong><em>Innatum </em></strong>(past part.), inborn;&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:04:18',NULL,NULL),(19255,920,13,NULL,'<p>Infected cells stimulate production of Interferons, Protein that protects the body against viral infection by </p><p>preventing viral replication and inhibits infected cell from dividing and kill some forms of cancer cells; <strong><em>-on</em></strong>,</p><p>denotes subatomic particle of antibodies.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:04:54',NULL,NULL),(19256,920,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Inter </em></strong>(L. prep.), among, between</p><p><strong><em>Ferire</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(L. v.),</span><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"> </strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\">to&nbsp;strike</span> with iron</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>-on</em></strong> (Gr. suffix), denotes subatomic particle; </p><p>extremely minute part</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:05:02',NULL,NULL),(19257,920,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>InterFeron</em></strong>,</p><p>Poetically, <em>“subatomic interferons strike with an iron”</em></p><p><em>Against virus</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong> <em><u>Inter + Fer- + -on</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Inter </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Fer-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Ferire</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"> </strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-on</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:05:19',16,'2025-05-14 01:35:34'),(19258,921,13,NULL,'<p>Proteins released from macrophages that enhances the activity of other White Blood Cells promote </p><p>inflammation and rapid T-cell proliferation; Interleukin act as agents of communication among different </p><p>population of leukocytes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:05:38',NULL,NULL),(19259,921,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Inter </em></strong>(L. prep.), among, between</p><p><strong><em>Leukos</em></strong> (Gk. adj.), white<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:05:43',NULL,NULL),(19260,921,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>InterLeukin</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, protein “among Whitte Blood Cells</em>”</p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Inter + Leuk- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Inter </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Leukos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:06:31',16,'2025-05-14 01:36:05'),(19261,922,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Intestinal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:08:51',NULL,NULL),(19262,922,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Trunks</strong></p><p>Bundled Enlarged lymphatic vessels</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:10:05',16,'2025-05-14 01:36:29'),(19263,922,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic Intestinal Trunks drain lymph from abdominal organs such as intestines, stomach, pancreas, </p><p>spleen, and liver.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:10:16',NULL,NULL),(19264,922,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Intestinus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj), pertaining to the inside</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:10:29',NULL,NULL),(19265,922,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Intestina- + -al</u> </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Intestina</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:10:47',16,'2025-05-14 01:36:39'),(19266,923,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Jugular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:13:24',NULL,NULL),(19267,923,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Trunks</strong></p><p>Enlarged lymphatic vessels</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:13:51',NULL,NULL),(19268,923,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic jugular trunks drain lymph from the head and neck.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:14:01',NULL,NULL),(19269,923,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Jugulum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Jugula</em></strong>), the throat</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:14:14',NULL,NULL),(19270,923,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Jugular,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “from the neck”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Jugula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Jugula</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:14:31',16,'2024-12-31 03:19:41'),(19271,924,13,NULL,'<p>Enzyme that neutralizes Kinin from over-reaction.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:15:13',NULL,NULL),(19272,924,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Kinesis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), movement<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:15:21',NULL,NULL),(19273,924,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Kinase</em></strong>,</p><p>Enzyme that modulates action of Kinin</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Kin- + -ase</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Kin </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Kinesis</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ase </em></strong>(suffix), denotes enzyme</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:15:59',16,'2025-05-14 01:37:03'),(19274,925,13,NULL,'<p>Polypeptides derived from plasma proteins; promotes movement of Leukocytes, inflammation by vasodilation, increase vascular permeability, stimulate pain receptors, and attract Neutrophils.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:16:34',16,'2025-05-14 01:37:43'),(19275,925,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Kinesis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), movement<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:16:42',NULL,NULL),(19276,925,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Kinin</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “hormone for call to action of WBC”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Kin- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Kin-</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Kinesis</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:18:36',16,'2025-05-14 01:37:29'),(19277,925,12,NULL,'<p>KINOCILIUM – SPECIAL SENSES</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:18:48',NULL,NULL),(19278,926,13,NULL,'<p>The lumen small intestine is lined with Microvilli of the Brush Border with Special Lymphatic Capillaries, named Lacteals, along with Arterial-Venous Capillaries; it absorbs and transports digested fats and pass through the lymphatic vessels, eventually passing into venous circulation.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:20:26',NULL,NULL),(19279,926,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lactis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lactes</em></strong>), milk</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:20:32',NULL,NULL),(19280,926,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lacteal</em></strong></p><p><em>Figurative for the milky color of digested fat</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Lacte- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lactes</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj..</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:20:41',16,'2025-05-14 01:38:11'),(19281,927,13,NULL,'<p>A lipid produced by White Blood Cells during an immune response; causes prolonged smooth muscle </p><p>contraction, increased vascular permeability; attract neutrophils and eosinophils; contributes to asthma </p><p>and inflammatory reactions.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:21:39',NULL,NULL),(19282,927,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Leukos</em></strong> (Gk. adj.), white</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Triene </em></strong>(Org. Chem.),<strong><em> </em></strong>any compound containing <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>three double bonds&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:21:46',NULL,NULL),(19283,927,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>LeukoTriene</em></strong></p><p><em>Hormone produced by WBC </em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Leuko- + Triene</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Leukos</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Triene&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:22:00',16,'2025-05-14 01:40:00'),(19284,928,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lingual</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:22:20',NULL,NULL),(19285,928,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Tonsil</strong></p><p>Adenoid in the throat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:22:27',16,'2025-05-14 01:42:19'),(19286,928,13,NULL,'<p>Loose colony of lymphatic molecules on the posterior surface of the tongue.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:22:36',NULL,NULL),(19287,928,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Lingua </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Linguae</em></strong>), tongue&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:22:41',16,'2025-05-14 01:42:27'),(19288,928,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lingua + -al</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lingua</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:22:48',16,'2025-05-14 01:42:37'),(19289,929,13,NULL,'<p>Thymus capsule divides the gland into several Lobules in sections reaching deep into the Medulla.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:23:11',NULL,NULL),(19290,929,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lobulus</em></strong> (L. n.), <em>“small husk, pod”</em></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Lobus</em></strong> (L. n), husk, pod</p><p>metaphor for smaller sections of Thymus</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:23:19',NULL,NULL),(19291,930,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lumbar</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:23:51',NULL,NULL),(19292,930,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Trunks</strong></p><p>Group of afferent / efferent Lymphatic vessels</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:24:07',16,'2025-05-14 01:42:57'),(19293,930,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic Lumbar trunks drain lymph from the tributary lower limbs, pelvic and abdominal walls, pelvic organs, ovaries or testes, kidneys, and adrenal glands.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:24:13',NULL,NULL),(19294,930,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lumbus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Lumbi</em></strong>), the loin, lower back&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:24:20',NULL,NULL),(19295,930,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lumb- + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lumbus </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-aris</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:24:27',16,'2025-05-14 01:43:49'),(19296,930,12,NULL,'<p><strong>LUMBAR</strong> VERTEBRAE / SPINE – SKELETAL SYSTEM</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:24:39',NULL,NULL),(19297,931,13,NULL,'<p>Approximately Three liters of Interstitial Fluid flow in and out of the Interstice and extra cellular </p><p>compartments and enter the lymphatic capillaries for filtration where the fluid is called Lymph; it causes </p><p>edema if stagnant.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:25:00',NULL,NULL),(19298,931,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:25:28',NULL,NULL),(19299,932,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymph</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:26:22',NULL,NULL),(19300,932,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Nodes,</strong></p><p>Encapsulated chains of lymphatic filters varying sizes</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:26:29',16,'2025-05-14 01:45:31'),(19301,932,13,NULL,'<p>Small, round, oval, or bean shaped structures 1 to 25 mm in size filter the Lymph, removing bacteria and </p><p>other waste material; distributed along the chain of lymphatic vessels; Lymphocytes congregate and </p><p>proliferate within the Lymph Nodes.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:26:35',NULL,NULL),(19302,932,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:26:45',NULL,NULL),(19303,936,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Capillaries,</strong></p><p>Smaller than Lymphatic Arterioles within Diffused Lymphatic Tissues</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:03',16,'2025-05-14 01:48:45'),(19304,936,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic capillaries are in almost all tissues of the body; excess fluid passing through the tissue spaces </p><p>and entering lymphatic capillaries become lymph; no lymphatic capillaries are found in the central </p><p>nervous system, the bone marrow, avascular tissue like cartilage, the dermis and cornea.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:12',NULL,NULL),(19305,936,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:18',NULL,NULL),(19306,936,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:26',16,'2025-05-14 01:48:55'),(19307,937,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:45',NULL,NULL),(19308,937,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic circulation connects to larger veins in the thorax or join larger vessels called lymphatic </p><p>ducts which then connect to large veins</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:53',NULL,NULL),(19309,937,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:28:59',NULL,NULL),(19310,937,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:29:11',16,'2025-05-14 01:49:24'),(19311,938,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:29:39',NULL,NULL),(19312,938,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Follicles,</strong></p><p>Lymphatic Filtration units with the nodes/nodules</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:29:49',16,'2025-05-14 01:49:46'),(19313,938,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic nodules found in the lymph nodes and spleen</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:29:55',NULL,NULL),(19314,938,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:30:02',NULL,NULL),(19315,938,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:30:12',16,'2025-05-14 01:49:55'),(19316,939,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:30:34',NULL,NULL),(19317,939,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Nodules,</strong></p><p>Smaller than nodes, compact and spherical</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:30:43',16,'2025-05-14 01:50:20'),(19318,939,13,NULL,'<p>Dense arrangements of lymphoid tissue organized in compact, spherical structure ranging in size </p><p>from a few hundred microns to a few mm. in diameter and located in the lose connective tissue of the digestive, respiratory, urinary, reproductive system</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:30:51',NULL,NULL),(19319,939,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:30:57',NULL,NULL),(19320,939,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:31:04',16,'2025-05-14 01:51:03'),(19321,940,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:31:25',NULL,NULL),(19322,940,13,NULL,'<p>Lymph nodes, Lymphocytes and Macrophages are packed around reticular (net-like) fibers collectively </p><p>to form Lymphatic Tissue; in other areas the reticular fibers extend across open spaces to form </p><p>Lymphatic Sinuses</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:31:31',NULL,NULL),(19323,940,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:31:37',NULL,NULL),(19324,940,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:31:43',16,'2025-05-14 01:51:23'),(19325,941,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:33:15',NULL,NULL),(19326,941,13,NULL,'<p>Includes lymph, lymphatic vessels, lymphatic tissue, lymphatic nodules, lymph nodes, tonsils, spleen, and the Thymus.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:33:20',NULL,NULL),(19327,941,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:33:26',NULL,NULL),(19328,941,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:33:32',16,'2025-05-14 01:51:55'),(19329,942,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:33:53',NULL,NULL),(19330,942,13,NULL,'<p>Consists primarily of Lymphocytes, but also includes Macrophages, Dendritic cells, reticular cells, </p><p>and other types cells.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:33:58',NULL,NULL),(19331,942,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:34:04',NULL,NULL),(19332,942,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:34:12',16,'2025-05-14 01:52:15'),(19333,943,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:34:38',NULL,NULL),(19334,943,13,NULL,'<p>Several or a group of Lymphatic Vessels converged to form larger vessels called Lymphatic Trunks.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:34:45',NULL,NULL),(19335,943,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:34:51',NULL,NULL),(19336,943,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:34:59',16,'2025-05-14 01:52:37'),(19337,944,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:35:32',NULL,NULL),(19338,944,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic Capillaries join to form larger Lymphatic Vessels which resemble small veins; they have </p><p>beaded appearance because of the presence of one-way valves identical to valves of veins.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:35:41',NULL,NULL),(19339,944,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong> (L. n.), pure water, spring water</p><p>Metaphor for filtered lymph</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:35:47',NULL,NULL),(19340,944,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lympha + -tic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-tic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:35:53',16,'2025-05-14 01:53:02'),(19341,945,13,NULL,'<p>Immature Lymphocytes rapidly proliferate when an antigen (infection) is present&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:36:13',NULL,NULL),(19342,945,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Lymphae</em></strong>), pure, spring water</p><p><strong><em>Blastos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), germinal cells, sprout</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:36:25',NULL,NULL),(19343,945,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lymphoblast</em></strong></p><p>metaphorically, <em>“germinal cells from pure water”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Lympho- + -blast</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-blast </em></strong><em>derived from </em><strong><em>Blastos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:36:36',16,'2025-05-14 01:53:22'),(19344,946,13,NULL,'<p>White Blood Cells originating from red bone marrow carried by the blood to lymphatic organs and other tissues become specific antibodies that have been produced during the first infection and subsequent exposures to specific antigens; lymphocytes multiply in response to infections and foreign substances.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:36:56',NULL,NULL),(19345,946,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Lymphae</em></strong>), pure, spring water</p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:37:01',NULL,NULL),(19346,946,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lymphocyte</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “cells from pure water”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Lympho- + -cyte</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympho- </em></strong><em>derived from </em><strong><em>Lympha</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Cytos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:37:13',16,'2025-05-14 01:53:42'),(19347,947,13,NULL,'<p>Cytokines, produced by Lymphocytes, often called Lymphokines, are messenger proteins for other WBC </p><p>to mount a concerted immune defense.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:37:36',NULL,NULL),(19348,947,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Lymphae</em></strong>), pure, spring water</p><p><strong><em>Kinesis</em></strong> (Gr. n.), movement</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:37:40',NULL,NULL),(19349,947,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>LymphoKines,</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for call-to-action WBC.</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Lympho- + Kines</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympha </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Kinesis</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:37:51',16,'2025-05-14 01:54:03'),(19350,948,13,NULL,'<p>Secreted by Cytotoxic T-cells; kills marked target cells.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:38:08',NULL,NULL),(19351,948,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lympha </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Lymphae</em></strong>), pure, spring water</p><p><strong><em>Tox</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Toxes</em></strong>), harm, poison</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:38:12',NULL,NULL),(19352,948,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>LymphoToxin</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for, infected cells, antigen marked for assassination </em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Lympho- + Tox + -in</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lympho- </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Tox</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:38:27',16,'2025-05-14 01:54:32'),(19353,949,13,NULL,'<p>Bactericidal Enzymes produced by Neutrophils.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:38:51',NULL,NULL),(19355,949,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lysis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lytes</em></strong>), destruction, dissolution</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Zymos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), leaven, </p><p>Metaphor for action of yeast</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:39:12',NULL,NULL),(19356,949,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lysozyme</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “enzyme for destruction”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Lyso- + -zyme</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lyso- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Lysis</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-zyme</em></strong><em> derived from</em><strong><em> Zymos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:39:22',16,'2025-05-14 01:54:59'),(19357,950,13,NULL,'<p>pertaining to destruction</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:39:40',NULL,NULL),(19358,950,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lysis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lytes</em></strong>), destruction, dissolution</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:39:45',NULL,NULL),(19359,950,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lytic, </em></strong></p><p>Greek for destructive</p><p><strong style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Lyt- + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Lyt-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Lytes </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:40:14',16,'2025-05-14 01:55:20'),(19360,951,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Macrocytic</strong>, adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:40:43',NULL,NULL),(19361,951,13,NULL,'<p>Located throughout the body, they intercept foreign substances and infectious bacteria; act on tissue repair in later stages of infection by ingesting dead cells and debris.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:40:49',NULL,NULL),(19362,951,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Macros </em></strong>(Gr. adj.),<strong><em> </em></strong>large, giant</p><p><strong><em>Cytos/ Kytos, </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:40:55',NULL,NULL),(19363,951,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Macrocytic</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “giant cells” </em>that devour</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Macro- + -cyte + -icus</u></em> </strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Macros </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Cytos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:41:07',16,'2025-05-14 01:55:39'),(19364,952,13,NULL,'<p>One of the 5 WBC, located in the Liver, Spleen and Lymphatic tissues; initiate recycling of hemoglobin from ruptured RBC to Amino acids, iron, and Bilirubin.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:41:29',NULL,NULL),(19365,952,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Macros </em></strong>(Gr. adj.),<strong><em> </em></strong>large, giant</p><p><strong><em>Phagus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Phagi</em></strong>), eating, devour, consume</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:41:36',NULL,NULL),(19366,952,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>MacroPhagus</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “devouring giant cell”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Macro- + Phagus</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Macro-</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Phagus</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:41:45',16,'2025-05-14 01:56:18'),(19367,953,13,NULL,'<p>Large motile cell in connective tissues that promote inflammation throughout the organism by the release of chemical mediators for inflammatory process.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:42:01',NULL,NULL),(19368,953,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Mast</strong> (Eng. n.), upright, vertical structure</p><p>Metaphor for a commanding position</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:42:07',NULL,NULL),(19369,956,13,NULL,'<p>central core of a gland, the central part of organs, kidneys, adrenals, brain, bones, Lymph Nodes</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:42:48',NULL,NULL),(19370,956,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullus, -a, -um </em></strong>(adj.), small central part</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:42:53',NULL,NULL),(19371,956,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullary</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “function of the small middle section”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Medulla + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Medulla</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function, location</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:43:04',16,'2025-05-14 01:56:52'),(19372,957,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Medullary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:43:24',NULL,NULL),(19373,957,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Cords</strong></p><p>Arranged like nets for filtration</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:43:32',16,'2025-05-14 01:57:10'),(19374,957,13,NULL,'<p>The medulla of Lymphatic nodes is organized into branching irregular strands of diffuse Lymphatic Tissue, called the Medullary Cords separated by Medullary sinuses.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:43:40',NULL,NULL),(19375,957,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullus, -a, -um </em></strong>(adj.), small central part</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:43:47',NULL,NULL),(19376,957,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullary</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “function of the small middle section”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Medulla + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Medulla </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function, location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:44:01',16,'2025-05-14 01:57:20'),(19377,958,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Membrane</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:44:24',NULL,NULL),(19378,958,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Attack Complex</strong></p><p>A round-about complexities to kill infected cells</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:44:34',16,'2025-05-14 01:57:42'),(19379,958,13,NULL,'<p>Complement proteins bore holes on the cell membrane of infected cell, consequently, sodium and water flow into the cells and cause lysis of the diseased cell.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:44:40',NULL,NULL),(19380,958,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Membranum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Membrana</em></strong>), thin film, thin covering</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:44:47',NULL,NULL),(19381,959,13,NULL,'<p>Memory is the characteristic of Adaptive Immunity to remember previous encounters with a specific </p><p>substance or organism resulting in specific rapid defensive response before symptoms are experienced.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:45:11',NULL,NULL),(19382,959,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Memor </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Memores</em></strong>), mindful, remembering</p><p>Metaphor for <em>“specific recognition”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:45:17',NULL,NULL),(19383,960,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Monoclonal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:46:14',NULL,NULL),(19384,960,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Antibody</strong></p><p>Fights antigen, bacterial infection&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:46:25',16,'2025-05-14 01:58:04'),(19385,960,13,NULL,'<p>When an antigen is injected into a laboratory animal it activates the B-cells against the antigen and </p><p>produce only one kind of antibody specific for that antigen.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:46:41',NULL,NULL),(19386,960,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Monos </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), one, single, containing one</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Clonus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cloni</em></strong>), cane from a vine </p><p>that can sprout same plant (grape vine)</p><p>origin of <strong>Clones, Cloning</strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:46:51',NULL,NULL),(19387,960,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>MonoClonal</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “billions of clones against one antigen</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Mono- + Clon- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Monos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Clon-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Clonus</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:47:06',16,'2025-05-14 01:58:18'),(19388,961,13,NULL,'<p>White Blood Cells with nuclei that are unlobed, appear mono-nucleated and agranulous (no grainy cytoplasm); they leave the blood circulation and enters injured or damaged tissues to become a macrophage.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:47:32',NULL,NULL),(19389,961,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Monos </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), one, single, containing one</p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:47:39',NULL,NULL),(19390,961,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Monocyte</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “one-celled”</em> WBC&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Mono- + -cyte</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Monos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Cytos</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:47:49',16,'2025-05-14 01:59:12'),(19391,962,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Mucosa</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:48:06',NULL,NULL),(19392,962,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Associated Lymphoid Tissue</strong></p><p>System-wide mucous membranes</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:48:16',16,'2025-05-14 01:59:29'),(19393,962,13,NULL,'<p>Groups of encapsulated lymphatic tissue found in and beneath the mucous membranes lining the digestive, inspiratory, urinary, and reproductive tracts; includes diffuse lymphatic tissue; lymphatic nodules in the tonsils that intercept microorganisms as they enter the digestive system.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:48:23',NULL,NULL),(19394,962,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Mucosus, -a, -um </em></strong>(adj.), <em>“phlegm-like”</em></p><p><em>Mucous membranes of digestive, inspiratory, urinary, and reproductive tracts</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:48:41',NULL,NULL),(19395,964,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., POLYMORPHONUCLEAR NEUTROPHIL; figuratively, <em>“neutral to”</em> basic or acidic dyes for purposes of microscopy; the most common WBC characterized by granules in the cytoplasm and lobed nucleus.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:49:10',16,'2025-05-28 00:30:57'),(19396,964,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Neuter</em></strong> (L. adj.), <em>“neither one, nor the other”</em></p><p><strong><em>Philos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), attraction, liking, love</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:49:16',NULL,NULL),(19397,964,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Neutrophil</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “attracted to basic or acidic dye”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Neutro- + -phil</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>Neuter</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     &nbsp;<strong><em>-phil</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Philos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:49:29',16,'2025-05-14 01:59:53'),(19398,967,13,NULL,'<p>Substances that make an antigen more susceptible to phagocytosis. Antibody IgG act as an Opsonin by connecting to an antigen through the variable region of the antibody and to a macrophage through the </p><p>constant region of the antibody; the macrophage then engulfs the antigen and antibody.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:50:14',NULL,NULL),(19399,967,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Opsonium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Opsonia</em></strong>), food, victuals</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:50:21',NULL,NULL),(19400,967,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Opsonin</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“spicing up” </em>the antigen With hormone</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Opson- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·             </em></strong><strong><em>Opsonium</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex. Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:50:30',16,'2025-05-28 00:32:57'),(19401,968,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Palatine</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:50:52',NULL,NULL),(19402,968,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Tonsils</strong></p><p>Adenoid in the throat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:01',16,'2025-05-28 00:31:26'),(19403,968,13,NULL,'<p>Large oval lymphoid masses on each side of the junction between the oral cavities and the pharynx.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:08',NULL,NULL),(19404,968,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Palatinus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), pertaining to the palate</p><p><strong><em>Palatum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Palata</em></strong>), palate</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:14',NULL,NULL),(19405,969,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Passive</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:37',NULL,NULL),(19406,969,13,NULL,'<p>Passive Immunity is acquired when another person develops antibodies and the antibodies are transferred to</p><p>a non-immune individual by vaccination, breastfeeding.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:43',16,'2025-05-28 00:34:10'),(19407,969,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pati </em></strong>(L. v.), to undergo;</p><p><strong><em>Passum </em></strong>(past part.), undergone</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:51',NULL,NULL),(19408,969,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Pass- + -ivus</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Passum </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ive&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:51:57',16,'2025-05-28 00:33:42'),(19409,970,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pathways</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:52:17',NULL,NULL),(19410,970,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Complement Cascade</strong></p><p>Completing the chain of events</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:52:26',16,'2025-05-28 00:35:27'),(19411,970,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Two pathways of Complement Cascade: 1. Classical Pathway leads to the development of antibodies and reactivation of Adaptive Immune System; </p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">2. Alternative Pathway is the activation of Innate Immunity against foreign substances</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:52:32',16,'2025-05-28 00:35:12'),(19412,970,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Pathway </strong>(Eng. n.), a narrow walkway;</p><p>in this sense, a course of action that</p><p>completes a series of cause and effect</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:52:38',16,'2025-05-28 00:35:54'),(19413,971,13,NULL,'<p>Natural killer cells; chemical emitted by infected cells by virus and secreted by cytotoxic T-cell; it bore holes in the membrane of target cells, killing the infected cell.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:52:57',NULL,NULL),(19414,971,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Perforare </em></strong>(L. v.), to bore through, to<strong><em> </em></strong>pierce through&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:53:02',NULL,NULL),(19415,971,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Perforin</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, Boring holes in cell membrane, mark for execution</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Perfor- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Perforare </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (ex. Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:53:11',16,'2025-05-28 00:37:33'),(19416,972,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Patches,</strong></p><p>Distributed in the small intestine</p><p><br></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:53:31',NULL,NULL),(19417,972,13,NULL,'<p>Groups of Lymphatic Nodules in the distal half of the small intestine and the appendix.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:53:38',NULL,NULL),(19418,972,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Peyer</em></strong>, Johann Conrad<em> </em><span style=\"background-color: white;\">(1653 – 1712), Swiss&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black; background-color: white;\">anatomist</span><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> described lymphoid tissue in the </span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: white;\">peritoneum</span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 03:53:43',16,'