2024-12-31 04:00:20',NULL,NULL),(19451,981,12,NULL,'<p>SERUM - CARDIOVASCULAR</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:00:32',NULL,NULL),(19452,982,13,NULL,'<p>The specificity of memory is characteristics of adaptive immunity, the ability to recognize a particular antigenic substance or parts of it from previous encounter amongst a myriad of bacteria invading the human body.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:00:49',NULL,NULL),(19453,982,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Species </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Speciei</em></strong>), appearance, shape<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Facere</em></strong> (L. v.), to make;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Factum </em></strong>(past part.), made<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:00:58',NULL,NULL),(19454,982,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Specific</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “certain shape and appearance”;</em></p><p><em>“facial-recognition”, </em>of sort</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Species + -fic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Species</em></strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-fic </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Factum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:01:06',16,'2025-05-28 00:47:57'),(19455,983,13,NULL,'<p>A lymphoid gland roughly the size of a clenched fist located on the left side the most superior part of the abdominal cavity</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:01:26',16,'2025-05-28 00:48:30'),(19456,983,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Splen</em></strong> (Gr. n.), ill humor, temper, spite</p><p>Ancient thoughts held spleen as seat of passion, spirit and courage</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:01:33',16,'2025-05-28 00:48:41'),(19457,983,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Splen + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Splen</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:01:39',16,'2025-05-28 00:48:51'),(19458,984,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Splenic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:01:57',NULL,NULL),(19459,984,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Cords</strong></p><p>weaved like nets for filtration</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:02:09',NULL,NULL),(19460,984,13,NULL,'<p>Network of reticular cells which produce reticular fibers; the spaces between the reticular cells are </p><p>occupied by splenic macrophages and blood cells coming from the capillaries.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:02:15',NULL,NULL),(19461,984,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Splen</em></strong> (Gr. n.), ill humor, temper, spite </p><p>Ancient thoughts held spleen as seat of passion,</p><p>spirit and courage</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:02:21',NULL,NULL),(19462,984,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Splen + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Splen</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:02:28',NULL,NULL),(19463,985,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Subclavian</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:02:49',NULL,NULL),(19464,985,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Trunks</strong></p><p>Merging of groups afferent or efferent lymph vessels</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:02:56',16,'2025-05-28 00:49:15'),(19465,985,13,NULL,'<p>Lymphatic subclavian trunks drain lymph from the upper limbs, superficial thoracic wall, and mammary glands</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:03:02',NULL,NULL),(19466,985,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sub </em></strong>(L. prep.), under, below</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Clavis</em></strong>, clavicle; classically, <em>“door bolt, a key”</em></p><p><strong><em>Claviculum,</em></strong> (dim., <strong>Clavis;</strong> L. n.), small bolt or key</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:03:11',16,'2025-05-28 00:52:13'),(19467,985,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em><u>Sub + Clavian</u></em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “under the Clavicle”</em></p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sub + Clavian</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Sub </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Clavian</em></strong>, clavicle</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:03:21',16,'2025-05-28 00:49:32'),(19468,986,13,NULL,'<p>Butterfly shaped gland lying at the anterior base of the neck made mostly of lymphatic tissue and accessory to the production of T-cells of the immune system; reduces in size and function with growth and physical </p><p>Maturity.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:03:43',NULL,NULL),(19469,986,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thymus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thymi</em></strong>), extraordinary growth in animals </p><p>Metaphor for reduction in size at maturity</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:03:51',NULL,NULL),(19470,988,13,NULL,'<p>State of unresponsiveness of lymphocytes to specific antigen preventing the immune system from responding to self-antigens</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:04:20',NULL,NULL),(19471,988,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tolerare </em></strong>(L. v.), to give allowance</p><p><strong><em>Tolerans</em></strong> (present part.), allowable variation;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:04:29',NULL,NULL),(19472,989,13,NULL,'<p>Large group of lymphatic nodules and diffused lymphatic tissue responding to self-antigens; located deep to the mucous membranes within the pharynx; provides protection against bacteria and other potentially harmful substance entering the digestive system through the nose or mouth.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:04:49',16,'2025-05-28 00:58:20'),(19473,989,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tonsilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tonsillae</em></strong>), gland in the throat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:04:54',NULL,NULL),(19474,992,13,NULL,'<p>Lattice structural pattern of cancellous bone featuring “<em>small posts, beams and cross braces</em>”; also known as, spongy bones.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:05:28',16,'2025-05-28 00:59:58'),(19475,992,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trabeculum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Trabecula</em></strong>), small lattice structure<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>Diminutive of<strong> <em>Trabs </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Trabes</em></strong>), support lattice formation<strong> </strong></p><p>Metaphor for the structural make up of medullary spongy bone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:05:38',NULL,NULL),(19476,993,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Trabeculae</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:05:55',NULL,NULL),(19477,993,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic Nodes,</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Small, round or oval, bean shaped structures, 1 - 25 mm long, filter the Lymphatic fluid.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:06:03',16,'2025-05-28 01:01:15'),(19478,993,13,NULL,'<p>Continuous with the capsule, a Delicate internal skeleton of Reticular Fibers extending from the capsule into the medulla to form a fibrous structural filtering network throughout the interior of the Lymphatic Nodes.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:06:11',NULL,NULL),(19479,993,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trabeculum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Trabecula</em></strong>), small lattice structure<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>Diminutive of<strong> <em>Trabs </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Trabes</em></strong>), lattice formation<strong> </strong></p><p>Metaphor for internal skeleton of Reticular Fibers of lymph nodes</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:06:26',NULL,NULL),(19480,993,12,NULL,'<p><strong>TRABECULAE</strong> CARNEAE - CARDIOVASCULAR</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:06:38',NULL,NULL),(19481,994,13,NULL,'<p>antigen developed and extracted from the cow serum (traditionally) introduced into humans to stimulate the immune system to achieve<strong> </strong>specific Active Artificial Immunity.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:07:04',16,'2025-05-28 01:27:06'),(19482,994,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vacca </em></strong>(L. n.), cow</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:07:11',NULL,NULL),(19483,994,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vaccine</em></strong></p><p><em>Many animals are used for serum.</em></p><p><em>Vacca</em> is the original.</p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Vacc- + -ine</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Vacca </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ine </em></strong>(suffix), forms adjective&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:07:22',16,'2025-05-28 01:27:22'),(19484,995,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Venous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:07:39',NULL,NULL),(19485,995,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Sinuses</strong></p><p>Miniscule spaces amongst myriad of veins in the lymphatic nodes</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:07:56',16,'2025-05-28 01:27:58'),(19486,995,13,NULL,'<p>Enlarged capillaries between the splenic cords; the venous sinuses typically connected to the trabecular veins which unite to form vessels that leave the spleen to form splenic veins.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:08:03',16,'2025-05-28 01:27:43'),(19487,995,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Venosus, -a, -um</em></strong>, pertaining to the vein&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 04:08:08',NULL,NULL),(19488,3896,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Necrosis</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 05:49:02',NULL,NULL),(19489,3896,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Tumor___Factor,</strong></p><p>Dead tumor cells promote pyrogens</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 05:49:10',16,'2025-05-28 01:28:32'),(19490,3896,13,NULL,'<p>Tumor Necrosis Factor activates macrophages and promotes fever by secreting Pyrogens.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 05:49:17',NULL,NULL),(19491,3896,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Necrosis </em></strong>/ <strong><em>Nekrosis</em></strong> (Gr. n.,), death</p><p>Metaphorically. <em>“dead cells promoting fever”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 05:49:24',NULL,NULL),(19492,3898,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., LEUKOCYTES; collectively termed Leukocytes, white cells, due to lack of Hemoglobin, red color; 5 types: Neutrophils, Basophils, Eosinophils, Lymphocytes, Monocytes; each type with specific functions; produced in red bone marrow and lymphatic tissue and are released into the blood stream and transported </p><p>throughout the body. They moved into tissues by Chemotaxis to mount an immune defense.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2024-12-31 05:52:36',NULL,NULL),(19493,1012,12,NULL,'<p>CORNEA</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:55:17',NULL,NULL),(19494,1015,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cortical</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:56:07',NULL,NULL),(19495,1015,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Hair Shaft,</strong></p><p>Hair strand itself</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:56:14',16,'2025-06-02 00:25:08'),(19496,1015,13,NULL,'<p>Forms the bulk of the hair shaft and consists of layers cells containing hard keratin.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:56:24',NULL,NULL),(19497,1015,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cortex</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cortices</em></strong>), nutshell, coat of seeds&nbsp;</p><p>Metaphor for “o<em>uter coat, outer layer”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:56:34',NULL,NULL),(19498,1015,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cortic- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Cortices</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; Eng., -al /-ar</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:56:41',16,'2025-06-02 00:25:19'),(19499,1016,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Cutaneous, </strong>adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:57:03',NULL,NULL),(19500,1016,13,NULL,'<p>The skin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:57:08',NULL,NULL),(19501,1016,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cutis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cutes</em></strong>), skin</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:57:16',NULL,NULL),(19502,1017,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., EPONYCHIUM; thickened layer of skin surrounding fingernails and toenails; Stratum Corneum around the nail folds encroach into the nail body</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:57:44',NULL,NULL),(19503,1017,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cuticulus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Cuticuli</em></strong>), small pieces of skin; </p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Cutis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cutes</em></strong>), skin</p><p>metaphorically, <em>“small piece of skin</em>”</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:57:52',NULL,NULL),(19504,1018,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cuticle</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:58:15',NULL,NULL),(19505,1018,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Hair Shaft,</strong></p><p>Hair Strand itself</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:58:27',16,'2025-06-02 00:25:53'),(19506,1018,13,NULL,'<p><em>“Layers of scales of the hairshaft”</em>, a single layer of hard Keratinocytes; on magnification they are arranged like overlapping roofing shingles on the hair shaft; or layers of fish scales.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:58:45',NULL,NULL),(19507,1018,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cuticulus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Cuticuli</em></strong>), small pieces of skin;<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><em>diminutive of </em><strong><em>Cutis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cutes</em></strong>), skin</p><p>metaphorically, <em>“small hair scales</em>” like roof shingles</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:58:53',NULL,NULL),(19508,1019,13,NULL,'<p>A severe deprivation of blood oxygen (Anoxia) producing bluish skin color; a decrease in blood flow, such as in vascular shock, cause the skin to appear pale.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:59:13',NULL,NULL),(19509,1019,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cyanos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), dark-blue substance</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:59:18',NULL,NULL),(19510,1019,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cyanosis,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“dark blue condition” </em>of skin</p><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Cyan- + -osis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Cyanos</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-osis</em></strong> (suffix), denotes pathology</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:59:29',16,'2025-06-02 00:26:14'),(19511,1020,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Dendritic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:59:46',NULL,NULL),(19512,1020,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., LANGERHANS\' CELLS; Dendritic Cells scattered throughout lymphatic system, specifically on the skin, are large motile cells with long cytoplasmic extension for Phagocytosis.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 00:59:55',NULL,NULL),(19513,1020,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dendron </em></strong>(Gr. n.; plu., <strong><em>Dendra</em></strong>), tree; fruit tree</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:00:01',NULL,NULL),(19514,1020,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dendritic, </em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “with dendrites”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Dendr- + -ites + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Dendron </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ites </em></strong>(suffix), denotes part of a body (e.g., somite)</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability . . .; Eng., -ic</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:00:18',16,'2025-06-02 00:27:11'),(19515,1021,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Dermal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:00:41',NULL,NULL),(19516,1021,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Root Sheath</strong></p><p>Skin enclosing the hair root bulb</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:00:48',16,'2025-06-02 00:27:43'),(19517,1021,13,NULL,'<p>Outer portion of the dermis that surrounds the Epithelial root sheath divide into external part </p><p>that has all the Strata found in skin, and internal part having only the Stratum Germinativum</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:00:57',NULL,NULL),(19518,1021,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Dermes</em></strong>), skin</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:01:05',NULL,NULL),(19519,1022,13,NULL,'<p>The structural strength of the skin is made up of two layers, Reticular and Papillary layers; </p><p>Reticular is dense irregular connective tissue; collectively, comprised of Collagen, Fibroblast </p><p>Adipose cells and Macrophages. Papillary layer is the most superficial.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:01:34',NULL,NULL),(19520,1022,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Dermes</em></strong>), skin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:02:29',NULL,NULL),(19521,1023,13,NULL,'<p>Transverse sections on the surface of the skin corresponding to sensory innervation at the levels of Spinal Nerves Roots.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:02:57',NULL,NULL),(19522,1023,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Dermes</em></strong>), skin</p><p><strong><em>Tomos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), a cut off, a section</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:03:03',NULL,NULL),(19523,1023,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DermaTome</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for imaginary transverse slices of the body by nerve root levels</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><u> </u><strong><em><u>Derma- + -tome + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Dermais </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Tomos</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:03:16',16,'2025-06-02 00:28:11'),(19524,1024,13,NULL,'<p>Following a Dermatome pattern</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:03:34',NULL,NULL),(19525,1024,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Dermes</em></strong>), skin</p><p><strong><em>Tomos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), a cut off, a section</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:03:40',NULL,NULL),(19526,1024,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DermaTomal</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphor for slices of the body by nerve root levels</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><u> </u><strong><em><u>Derma- + -tome + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Dermis </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Tomos</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; Eng., -al&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:03:50',16,'2025-06-02 00:28:35'),(19527,1025,13,NULL,'<p>Epidermal new cells push off the old ones and slough off, and newer skin cells surface.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:04:15',NULL,NULL),(19528,1025,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>De- </em></strong>(L. prefix), down from, reduced, off</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Squama</em></strong> (pl., <strong><em>Squamae</em></strong>), scale&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:04:20',16,'2025-06-02 00:29:05'),(19529,1025,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>DeSquamation</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><em>figuratively, process of</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>“descaling”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><em>sloughing off of old skin</em></p><p><br></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>De- + Squama + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>De- </em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Squama</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ation</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:04:31',16,'2025-06-02 00:29:18'),(19530,1026,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Ecrine</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:04:53',NULL,NULL),(19531,1026,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Sweat Glands</strong></p><p>Merocrine glands</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:05:01',16,'2025-06-02 00:29:43'),(19532,1026,13,NULL,'<p>Glands with ducts lined with epithelium leading out of the body; alternatively, some parts of the glands become separated and sloughed off from the epithelium of origin.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:05:08',NULL,NULL),(19533,1026,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ex </em></strong>(L. prep.), from, out of, off<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), secretion</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:05:14',NULL,NULL),(19534,1026,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ECrine</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, partially “secreted from”</em> the whole gland</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>E- + Crine</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>E- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Ex </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:05:32',16,'2025-06-02 00:29:53'),(19535,1027,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Epidermal</strong>, adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:05:58',NULL,NULL),(19536,1027,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of stratified squamous cell superior to the Dermis Papillary Layer; the basement </p><p>membrane is made up of keratinocytes, responsible for structural strength; Melanocytes </p><p>for skin coloring, and Phagocytes for bacterial protection; Langerhans cells, and Merkel’s cells.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:06:06',NULL,NULL),(19537,1027,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p><p><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Dermes</em></strong>), skin</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:06:12',NULL,NULL),(19538,1027,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EpiDermal</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, pertaining to the layer “above skin”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Epi- + Derm- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Epi-Apices</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:06:21',16,'2025-06-02 00:30:23'),(19539,1028,13,NULL,'<p>Surface connective tissue containing capillaries that are shaped like teats under magnification</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:06:39',NULL,NULL),(19540,1028,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p><p><strong><em>Thelium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Thelia</em></strong>), teat, buds, nipple</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:06:44',NULL,NULL),(19541,1028,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EpiThelium</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “teats on surface lining”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Epi- + Thelium</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Epi-</em></strong><em> derived from</em> <strong><em>Apices</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Thelium</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:06:56',16,'2025-06-02 00:30:53'),(19542,1029,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Epithelial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:28:14',NULL,NULL),(19543,1029,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Root Sheath</strong></p><p>Surface dermal invagination of the hair follicle</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:28:28',16,'2025-06-02 00:31:15'),(19544,1029,13,NULL,'<p>Part of the Hair Follicle divided into external part that has all the strata found in skin, and </p><p>internal part having only the Stratum Germinativum.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:28:36',NULL,NULL),(19545,1029,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p><p><strong><em>Thelium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Thelia</em></strong>), teat, buds, nipple</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:28:45',NULL,NULL),(19546,1029,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EpiThelial</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “teats on the surface lining”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Epi- + Thelia + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Epi-</em></strong><em> derived from</em> <strong><em>Apices</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Thelia</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:28:56',16,'2025-06-02 00:31:34'),(19547,1030,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., CUTICLE; Stratum Corneum thickened layer of skin surrounding fingernails and toenails encroaches over the nail plate, becoming the cuticle</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:29:26',NULL,NULL),(19548,1030,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apex</em></strong><em> </em>(plu., <strong><em>Apices</em></strong>), peak, top, above</p><p><strong><em>Onychion </em></strong>(Gr. n.), little claw</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:29:32',NULL,NULL),(19549,1030,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>EpOnychion</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “above the small claw”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Ep- + Onychion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Epi-</em></strong><em> derived from</em> <strong><em>Apices</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Onychion</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:29:43',16,'2025-06-02 00:32:01'),(19550,1031,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Erector</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:30:10',NULL,NULL),(19551,1031,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pili</strong></p><p>Hair</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:30:21',NULL,NULL),(19552,1031,13,NULL,'<p>Each hair follicle has a smooth muscle that extend from the Dermal Root Sheath of the </p><p>hair follicle to the Papillary Layer of the Dermis; it pulls follicle into a position perpendicular to the surface skin causing the hair to stand on skin</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:30:30',NULL,NULL),(19553,1031,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Erigere </em></strong>(L. v.), to guide, to straighten up</p><p><strong><em>Erectum</em></strong> (past part.), straightened, upright;<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:30:37',NULL,NULL),(19554,1031,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Erector,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, make hair “stand”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Erect- + -or</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Erectum </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-or(s)</em></strong> (suffix), denotes agent of action</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:30:51',16,'2025-06-02 00:32:43'),(19555,1032,13,NULL,'<p>Layer of whitish connective tissue covering and separating groups of muscles.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:31:15',NULL,NULL),(19556,1032,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fascia </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Fasciae</em></strong>), bandage, wrapping</p><p>Metaphor for the whitish muscle wrapping</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:31:21',NULL,NULL),(19557,1035,13,NULL,'<p>To sprout, grow shoots</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:32:37',NULL,NULL),(19558,1035,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Germinare </em></strong>(L. v.), to put forth shoots;</p><p><strong><em>Germinatum </em></strong>(past part.), sprouted seedlings&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 01:32:51',NULL,NULL),(19559,1037,13,NULL,'<p>Fine grain (under microscopy)</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:11:33',NULL,NULL),(19560,1037,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Granulus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Granuli</em></strong>), fine grain</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Granus</em></strong>, grain</p><p>figuratively, distributed fine speckles in the cell plasma</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:11:41',NULL,NULL),(19561,1039,13,NULL,'<p>In humans, hair is found everywhere on the skin except palms, soles, lips, nipples, parts of the penis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:12:13',NULL,NULL),(19562,1040,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Hair</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:12:31',NULL,NULL),(19563,1040,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Bulb</strong></p><p>Enlarged base of hair follicle</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:12:38',16,'2025-06-02 00:36:06'),(19564,1040,13,NULL,'<p>The base of the root is expanded to form the hair bulb into their base; the dermis invaginates into </p><p>the bulb to supply blood vessels and for anchoring into the scalp.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:12:44',NULL,NULL),(19565,1041,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Hair</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:13:01',NULL,NULL),(19566,1041,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Color,</strong></p><p>Black, blond, brown, grey</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:13:09',16,'2025-06-02 00:37:00'),(19567,1041,13,NULL,'<p>Melanin is produced by melanocytes within the hair bulb matrix and pass to keratinocytes in the </p><p>hair cortex and medulla like the skin; amounts of types of melanin cause different shades of </p><p>hair color.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:13:16',NULL,NULL),(19568,1042,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Hair</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:13:35',NULL,NULL),(19569,1042,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Follicle</strong></p><p>Classically, <strong><em>Folliculus</em></strong>, small coin purse;</p><p>metaphor for the hair bulb</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:13:50',16,'2025-06-02 00:37:20'),(19570,1042,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of dermal root sheath, the portion of the dermis that surrounds the external and </p><p>internal epithelial root sheath.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:13:56',NULL,NULL),(19571,1043,13,NULL,'<p>GROWTH STAGE / RESTING STAGE cycle; hairs formed by the cells of the matrix undergo cell differentiation become Keratinized and die and replaced with new ones.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:14:38',NULL,NULL),(19572,1044,13,NULL,'<p>Sebaceous Glands of the skin is a Holocrine Gland because it sheds entire epithelial cells after accumulating secretory products in their cytoplasm, they rupture, and are secreted.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:14:58',NULL,NULL),(19573,1044,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Holo</em></strong> (Gr. adj.), whole, entire, complete</p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:15:04',NULL,NULL),(19574,1044,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HoloCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “secretions of whole cell”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Holo + Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Holo</em></strong> (Gr. adj.), whole, entire, complete</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:15:19',16,'2025-06-02 00:37:48'),(19575,1045,13,NULL,'<p>Subcutaneous Tissue or Superficial Fascia consisting of loose connective Collagen and Elastin fibers is attached to the underlying bones and muscles are highly vascularized and innervated; not a part of the Integumentary System</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:15:36',NULL,NULL),(19576,1045,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hypo</em></strong> (L. prep.), under, below, deficient</p><p><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong> (L. n.), skin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:15:41',NULL,NULL),(19577,1045,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HypoDermis,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “under the skin”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Hypo- + Dermis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Hypo</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Dermis</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:15:50',16,'2025-06-02 00:38:19'),(19578,1046,13,NULL,'<p>Thickened region of the Stratum Corneum under the free edge of the nail body, <em>“cuticles”</em></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:16:06',NULL,NULL),(19579,1046,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hypo</em></strong> (L. prep.), under, below, deficient</p><p><strong><em>Onychion </em></strong>(Gr. n.), little claw</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:16:12',NULL,NULL),(19580,1046,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HypOnychion</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “below the claw”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Hypo + Onychion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Hypo</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Onychion</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:16:32',16,'2025-06-02 00:40:11'),(19581,1047,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Integumentary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:16:52',NULL,NULL),(19582,1047,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of the skin, sensory structures, hair, nails, glands; functions for protection, sensation, temperature regulation, vitamin D production.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:16:57',NULL,NULL),(19583,1047,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Integumentum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Integumenta</em></strong>), covering&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:17:03',NULL,NULL),(19584,1047,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Integumentary</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>\"function for covering\"</em></p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em>Integumenta + -ary</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Integumenta</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:17:56',16,'2025-06-02 00:41:40'),(19585,1048,13,NULL,'<p>The Stratum Corneum consists of Cornified Cells (<strong><em>Cornu</em></strong>, horn) which are dead cells with hard protein, Keratin, a mixture of Keratin fibers and Keratohyalin.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:18:59',NULL,NULL),(19586,1048,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), horn</p><p>Metaphor for the dead, hardened protein</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:19:08',NULL,NULL),(19587,1048,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratin,</em></strong></p><p><em>figurative for hard protein of dead skin, hair, like horns</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Kerat- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Keratos</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:19:27',16,'2025-06-02 00:42:02'),(19588,1049,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Keratinized</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:19:48',NULL,NULL),(19589,1049,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Epithelial Cells</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Surface lining cells</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:19:58',16,'2025-06-02 00:42:20'),(19590,1049,13,NULL,'<p>One daughter epithelial skin cell becomes new Stratum Basale cells and divide again but the other daughter cells is pushed toward the surface and becomes Keratinized.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:20:05',NULL,NULL),(19591,1049,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), horn</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:20:11',NULL,NULL),(19592,1049,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratinized,</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “Exposed and hardened”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Kerat- + -in + -ized</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ized</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:20:24',16,'2025-06-02 00:42:32'),(19593,1050,13,NULL,'<p>Cells from the epidermis move from the deeper epidermal layers to the surface; the cells change shape and chemical composition becoming Keratinized and produce an outer layer of cells that resist abrasions and form a permeable barrier.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:20:51',NULL,NULL),(19594,1050,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), horn</p><p>figurative for hard protein, like hornscells that resist abrasions and form a permeable barrier.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:20:56',NULL,NULL),(19595,1050,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratinization</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “Exposed and hardened”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Kerat- + -in + -ized + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ize</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ation</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of actionsions and form a permeable barrier.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:21:15',16,'2025-06-02 00:43:03'),(19596,1051,13,NULL,'<p>Contain keratin protein, a mixture of Keratin fibers and Keratohyalin, responsible for structural strength and permeability of the epidermis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:21:37',NULL,NULL),(19598,1051,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), horn</p><p>figurative for dead, hardened protein, like horns</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:21:58',NULL,NULL),(19599,1051,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratinocytes</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “</em><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=integumentary&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><em>horned cells</em></a><em>”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Kerat- + -ino- + cytes</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Cytos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:22:13',16,'2025-06-02 00:43:29'),(19600,1052,13,NULL,'<p>Non-membrane-bound protein granules that accumulate in the cytoplasm of the keratinocytes in Stratum Granulosum to become Keratin fibers.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:23:37',NULL,NULL),(19601,1052,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Keratos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), horn</p><p>figurative for hardened protein, like horns</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Hyalinus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), transparent;<strong> </strong></p><p><strong><em>Hyalus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Hyali</em></strong>), glass</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:24:20',NULL,NULL),(19602,1052,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>KeratoHyaline</em></strong></p><p>figuratively, <em>“</em><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=integumentary&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><em>transparent</em></a><em> horn protein”</em></p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Kerato- + Hyaline</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Keratin </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Hyalinus</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:25:44',16,'2025-06-02 00:43:52'),(19603,1053,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Lamellar</strong>, adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:26:13',NULL,NULL),(19604,1053,13,NULL,'<p>Thin layered coverings</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:26:19',NULL,NULL),(19605,1054,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Lamellar</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:26:42',NULL,NULL),(19606,1054,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Bodies</strong></p><p>Lipid cell organelles</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:26:54',16,'2025-06-02 00:44:16'),(19607,1054,13,NULL,'<p>Additional keratin fibers and lipid filled membrane-bound organelles called Lamellar Bodies are formed inside the cells of Stratum Spinosum.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:27:00',NULL,NULL),(19608,1054,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lamella</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lamellae</em></strong>), thin layer of covering<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>membrane-bound</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:27:06',NULL,NULL),(19609,1054,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Lamella + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Lamella</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:27:14',16,'2025-06-02 00:44:26'),(19610,1055,13,NULL,'<p>Dendritic Cells on the skin are called Langerhans’ Cells; they are large motile cells with long cytoplasmic extension for Phagocytosis scattered throughout lymphatic system.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:27:33',NULL,NULL),(19612,1055,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Langerhans</strong>, Paul (1847 – 1888), German&nbsp;</p><p>Pathologist, Physiologist and Biologist&nbsp;</p><p>discovered dendritic cells in the skin.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:28:24',16,'2025-06-02 00:44:56'),(19613,1056,13,NULL,'<p>Unpigmented fetal hair, characteristic at six-month fetal development.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:28:41',NULL,NULL),(19614,1056,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lanugo</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Lanugines</em></strong>), wooliness, down hair</p><p>Metaphor for soft white hair of fetus</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:28:47',NULL,NULL),(19615,1058,13,NULL,'<p>Whitish crescent shaped nail base seen through the nail body; appears white because the blood </p><p>vessels cannot be seen through the thicker nail.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:29:16',NULL,NULL),(19616,1058,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lunula </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Lunulae</em></strong>), small moon<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Luna</em></strong>, moon</p><p>figuratively, whitish <em>“small moon” </em>at base of nail</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:29:22',NULL,NULL),(19617,1059,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Mammary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:29:41',NULL,NULL),(19618,1059,13,NULL,'<p>Modified Apocrine Glands in the breast that produce milk.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:29:48',NULL,NULL),(19619,1059,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Mamma</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Mammae</em></strong>), breast&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:29:53',NULL,NULL),(19620,1059,9,NULL,'<p>comp.,<strong> <em><u>Mamma + -arium</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Mamma</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Mammae</em></strong>), breast</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-arium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location; Eng., -ary</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:30:00',16,'2025-06-02 00:45:25'),(19621,1060,13,NULL,'<p>A mass of undifferentiated epithelial cells inside a hair bulb which produce the hair (growth zone) and internal epithelial root sheath; the dermis of the skin invaginates to make room for the hair bulb, and a papilla that contains blood vessels anchors the hair to the scalp.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:32:45',NULL,NULL),(19622,1060,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Matrix </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Matrices</em></strong>), foundation; </p><p>classically., female farm animal for reproduction</p><p>metaphor for foundation of epithelial cells.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:32:52',NULL,NULL),(19623,1061,13,NULL,'<p>middle</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:33:20',NULL,NULL),(19624,1061,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medius, -ia, -ium</em></strong> (adj.), center</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:33:26',NULL,NULL),(19625,1062,13,NULL,'<p>Middle core, the central part of organs, brain, bones, kidneys, glands, and hair strand inner shaft.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:33:43',NULL,NULL),(19626,1062,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullus, -a, -um </em></strong>(adj.), small center; </p><p>literally, <em>“small central”</em> part</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:33:48',NULL,NULL),(19627,1063,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Medulla</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:34:05',NULL,NULL),(19628,1063,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Hair Shaft</strong></p><p>A strand of hair has a middle pith</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:49:06',16,'2025-06-02 00:45:54'),(19629,1063,13,NULL,'<p>Central axis inside the hair shaft consisting of two or three layers of Keratinocytes, laid like roof shingles.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:49:12',NULL,NULL),(19630,1063,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullus, -a, -um </em></strong>(adj.), small center;</p><p>literally, <em>“small central”</em> shaft of the hair</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:49:18',NULL,NULL),(19631,1064,13,NULL,'<p>Meisner corpuscles are mechanoreceptors for sensitivity for light touch and simultaneous two-point discrimination.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:49:43',NULL,NULL),(19632,1064,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Meissner</strong>, George (1829- 1905) and Wagner, Rudolf, German anatomists</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:49:49',NULL,NULL),(19633,1065,13,NULL,'<p>A group of pigments produced by Melanocytes, responsible for skin hair and eye color; believed </p><p>to provide protection against ultraviolet light of the sun.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:50:08',NULL,NULL),(19634,1065,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanos / Melas </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), black, dark</p><p>Metaphor for the effects of melanin on skin color</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:50:15',NULL,NULL),(19635,1065,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em><u>Melanin</u></em></strong></p><p>Literally, <em>“skin darkening protein”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Melano- + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Melanos</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:50:27',16,'2025-06-02 00:46:32'),(19636,1066,13,NULL,'<p>Melanin producing cells with many long processes that extend between the keratinocytes </p><p>of Stratum Basale and Stratum Spinosum contributing to skin color.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:50:46',NULL,NULL),(19637,1066,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanos / Melas </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), black, dark</p><p>Metaphor for the effects of melanin on skin color</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:50:55',NULL,NULL),(19638,1066,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanocytes</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “skin darkening protein cell”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Melano- + -cytes</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Melano-</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Cytos</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:51:04',16,'2025-06-02 00:46:51'),(19639,1067,13,NULL,'<p>(Pathology), skin cancer caused by abnormally hyperactive Melanocytes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:51:25',NULL,NULL),(19640,1067,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanos / Melas </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), black, dark</p><p>Metaphor for the effects of melanin on skin color</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:51:31',NULL,NULL),(19641,1067,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanoma</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“black cancer” </em>of melanocytes</p><p><br></p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Melano- + -oma</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Melanos</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-oma </em></strong>(suffix), denotes tumors, abnormal growth</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:51:40',16,'2025-06-02 00:47:11'),(19642,1068,13,NULL,'<p>(Cell Biology), Cell Organelles in Melanocyte synthesize Melanin; the Golgi Apparatus package Melanin in Vesicles called Melanosome and are exocytosis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:52:28',NULL,NULL),(19643,1068,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanos / Melas </em></strong>(Gr. adj.), black, dark</p><p>Metaphor for the effects of melanin on skin color</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Sōma</em></strong> (Gr. n.), body, organelles in cell plasma&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:52:34',NULL,NULL),(19644,1068,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Melanosoma</em></strong></p><p><em>Melanin containing organelles in cell plasma&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Melano- + -soma</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Melano-</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-some</em></strong><em> derived from</em> <strong><em>Sōma</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:52:45',16,'2025-06-02 00:47:42'),(19645,1068,12,NULL,'<p>MELATONIN - NEUROLOGY</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:52:54',NULL,NULL),(19646,1069,13,NULL,'<p>Specialized epidermal cells associated with nerve endings responsible for detecting light touch and superficial pressure</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:53:13',NULL,NULL),(19647,1069,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Merkel,</strong> Friedrich Sigmund, leading German anatomist in late 19th Century; described Merkel’s Cells in 1878</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:53:19',NULL,NULL),(19648,1070,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Merocrine</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:53:38',NULL,NULL),(19649,1070,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Glands</strong></p><p>Secrete sweat, sebum</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:53:47',16,'2025-06-02 00:48:14'),(19650,1070,13,NULL,'<p>Merocrine glands such as water producing sweat glands secrete products derived from partial contribution of cellular material; secretions are either actively transported or packaged vesicles and then released by the process of exocytosis.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:53:53',NULL,NULL),(19651,1070,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Meros </em></strong>(Gr. n.), part of, fraction </p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:54:02',NULL,NULL),(19652,1070,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>MeroCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “partially secreted”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Mero- + Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Meros </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:54:13',16,'2025-06-02 00:48:23'),(19653,1071,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Merocrine</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:54:39',NULL,NULL),(19654,1071,13,NULL,'<p>Merocrine sweat glands are most numerous in the palms, the soles of feet but are absent from the margin of the Labia Minora, the tips of the penis, and clitoris.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:54:44',NULL,NULL),(19655,1071,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Meros </em></strong>(Gr. n.), part of, fraction </p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:54:50',NULL,NULL),(19656,1071,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>MeroCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “partially secreted”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Mero- + Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Meros </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:55:00',16,'2025-06-02 00:49:04'),(19657,1072,13,NULL,'<p>Nails are continuous with Stratum Corneum; protect the ends of digits essential in manipulating and grasping of small objects, scratching</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:55:20',NULL,NULL),(19658,1073,13,NULL,'<p>Taste buds in the tongue, appearing like Pimples on the surface of the tongue</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:55:52',NULL,NULL),(19659,1073,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Papilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Papillae</em></strong>), a teat, bud, nipple-like</p><p>Rough surface of cell linings.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:55:57',NULL,NULL),(19660,1074,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Papillary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:56:15',NULL,NULL),(19661,1074,13,NULL,'<p>The papillary layer derived its name from numerous highly vascularized surface projections called Papillae loosely arranged connective tissue of the Dermis because it has thin fibers.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:56:23',NULL,NULL),(19662,1074,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Papilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Papillae</em></strong>), a teat, bud, nipple-like</p><p>Rough surface of cell linings.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:56:30',NULL,NULL),(19663,1074,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Papillary</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “teat-like</em>” layer</p><p><br></p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Papilla + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Papilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Papillae</em></strong>), a teat, bud, nipple-like</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-arium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location; Eng., -ary&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:56:53',16,'2025-06-02 00:49:41'),(19664,1076,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reticular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:57:26',NULL,NULL),(19665,1076,13,NULL,'<p>The main layer of the Dermis (and Papillary layers) comprised of dense irregular connective </p><p>Tissues.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:57:32',NULL,NULL),(19666,1076,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), small fishing net </p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong>, net<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:57:42',NULL,NULL),(19667,1076,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticular</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>net-like</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Reticula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Reticula</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:58:11',16,'2025-06-02 00:50:06'),(19668,1076,12,NULL,'<p><strong>RETICULAR</strong>&nbsp;FORMATION – NEUROLOGY</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:58:23',NULL,NULL),(19669,1077,13,NULL,'<p>Skin receptor for continuous touch or light pressure</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:58:47',NULL,NULL),(19670,1077,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ruffini</em></strong>, Angelo<strong><em> </em></strong>(1874 – 1929), Italian Anatomist </p><p>described Ruffini’s corpuscle in the skin of fingers </p><p>as pressure sensors</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:58:52',NULL,NULL),(19671,1078,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sebaceous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:59:10',NULL,NULL),(19672,1078,13,NULL,'<p>Located in the dermis are simple or compound Alveolar Glands connected by a duct in the </p><p>upper part of the hair follicles that secrete Sebum which prevents drying and provides </p><p>protection against bacteria.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:59:19',NULL,NULL),(19673,1078,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sebaceus, -ea, -eum</em></strong> (adj.), fatty; Literally, <em>“oily”</em></p><p><strong><em>Sebum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Seba</em></strong>), tallow, grease</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:59:28',NULL,NULL),(19674,1079,13,NULL,'<p>Oily white substance, rich lipids, released by Alveolar Sebaceous Glands</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 02:59:53',NULL,NULL),(19675,1079,13,NULL,'<p>Oily substance produced by Meibonian glands that coats the eyelids and prevent tears from flowing through the eyelid margins</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:00:01',NULL,NULL),(19676,1079,13,NULL,'<p>Modified Merocrine sweat glands in the ear canal combined secretions of Ceruminous Glands and Sebaceous Glands</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:00:07',NULL,NULL),(19677,1079,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sebum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Seba</em></strong>), tallow, grease,<em> </em>oil</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:00:16',NULL,NULL),(19678,1080,13,NULL,'<p>Pigments of the skin, blood circulating under the skin, diet and the thickness of the Stratum Corneum together determine skin color.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:00:35',NULL,NULL),(19679,1082,13,NULL,'<p>Five layers of the Epidermis: Stratum Basale, Stratum Spinosum, Stratum Granulosum, </p><p>Stratum Lucidum, Stratum Corneum</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:01:12',NULL,NULL),(19680,1082,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:01:17',NULL,NULL),(19681,1083,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stratum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:01:39',NULL,NULL),(19682,1083,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Basale</strong></p><p>Base layer</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:01:46',16,'2025-06-02 00:50:46'),(19683,1083,13,NULL,'<p>Deepest portion of the epidermis is a single layer of cuboidal or columnar cells provides </p><p>structural and germinative foundation of the Epidermis.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:01:52',NULL,NULL),(19684,1083,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:02:00',NULL,NULL),(19685,1084,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stratum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:02:45',NULL,NULL),(19686,1084,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Corneum</strong></p><p>Hardened dead squamous cells</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:02:52',16,'2025-06-02 00:51:05'),(19687,1084,13,NULL,'<p>Most superficial stratum of the epidermis composed of 25 or more layers of dead squamous cells attach together by Desmosomes; when the Desmosomes break down cells are slough off from the </p><p>surface of the skin.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:02:58',NULL,NULL),(19688,1084,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:03:03',NULL,NULL),(19689,1085,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stratum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:03:23',NULL,NULL),(19690,1085,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Germinativum</strong></p><p>Able to reproduce skin cells</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:03:32',16,'2025-06-02 00:51:23'),(19691,1085,13,NULL,'<p>Together the Stratum Spinosum and Stratum Basale are called Stratum Germinativum because cell division occur in this level, above this level there is no mitosis occurring.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:03:39',NULL,NULL),(19692,1085,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:03:43',NULL,NULL),(19693,1086,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stratum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:43:36',NULL,NULL),(19694,1086,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Granulosum</strong></p><p>Granules of plasma of Keratohyalin cells</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:43:44',16,'2025-06-02 00:51:41'),(19695,1086,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of 20-25 layers of flatten diamond shaped cells with long axis that are oriented </p><p>parallel to the surface of the skin; this stratum derives its name from the non-membrane-bound </p><p>proteins granules of Keratohyalin.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:43:51',NULL,NULL),(19696,1086,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:43:56',NULL,NULL),(19697,1087,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stratum<span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span></strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:44:19',NULL,NULL),(19698,1087,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Lucidum</strong></p><p>Clear layers of dead cells with keratin fibers</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:44:28',16,'2025-06-02 00:52:02'),(19699,1087,13,NULL,'<p>Layers of dead cells containing keratin fibers with undefined boundary appear as a thin clear </p><p>zone above the Stratum Granulosum.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:44:36',NULL,NULL),(19700,1087,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:44:42',NULL,NULL),(19701,1088,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stratum</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:44:58',NULL,NULL),(19702,1088,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Spinosum</strong></p><p>Cells appear spiny in microscopy</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:45:16',16,'2025-06-02 00:52:20'),(19703,1088,13,NULL,'<p>Consists of 8 to 10 layers of many-sided cells pushed up by younger cells become flat; appear </p><p>spiny in microscopic examination, thus the name Stratum Spinosum</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:45:22',NULL,NULL),(19704,1088,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stratum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Strata</em></strong>), layer</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:45:29',NULL,NULL),(19705,1089,13,NULL,'<p>STRETCH MARKS: Dermis layer rupture and leave lines that are visible through the epidermis when skin is overstretched; usual in abdomens and breasts of women.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:46:00',NULL,NULL),(19706,1089,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stria</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Striae</em></strong>), stripe, scoriations, furrow <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:46:06',NULL,NULL),(19707,1089,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Stria + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Stria</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ation</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:46:21',16,'2025-06-02 00:52:42'),(19708,1090,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Subcutaneous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:46:54',NULL,NULL),(19709,1090,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Hypodermis</strong> or <strong>Superficial Fascia</strong>, consisting of loose connective tissue Collagen and Elastin is attached to the underlying bones and muscles supplied with blood vessels and nerves; not a part of the Integumentary System</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:47:00',NULL,NULL),(19710,1090,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sub- </em></strong>(L. prefix), denotes under</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Cutaneous</em></strong> (L. adj.), pertaining to the skin</p><p><strong><em>Cutis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cutes</em></strong>), skin</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:47:09',NULL,NULL),(19711,1090,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SubCutaneous</em></strong></p><p><em>literally,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>under the skin</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Sub- + Cutaneous</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Sub- </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Cutaneous</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:47:22',16,'2025-06-02 00:53:07'),(19712,1091,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sudoriferous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:47:49',NULL,NULL),(19713,1091,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., SWEAT GLANDS; Merocrine or Apocrine sweat glands are the most common type of sweat glands; they are simple coiled tubular glands that open directly into the surface of the skin through the sweat pores</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:47:56',NULL,NULL),(19714,1091,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sudor </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Sudores</em></strong>), sweat<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><em>Ferre</em></strong> (L. v.), to carry</p><p><strong><em>Ferous </em></strong>(adj.), able to carry, carrying;<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:48:02',NULL,NULL),(19715,1091,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SudoriFerous</em></strong></p><p><em>literally</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“sweat bearing”</em> glands</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Sudor + Ferous</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Sudor</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Ferous</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:48:11',16,'2025-06-02 00:53:29'),(19716,1092,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Superficial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:48:45',NULL,NULL),(19717,1092,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Fascia</strong></p><p><em>“bandange or wrapping” </em>around hypodermal layer</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:48:57',NULL,NULL),(19718,1092,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Subcutaneous Tissue</strong> or <strong>Hypodermis</strong> consisting of loose connective tissue; Collagen and Elastin fibers is attached to the underlying bones and muscles supplied with blood vessels and nerves; not a part of the Integumentary System.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:49:03',NULL,NULL),(19719,1092,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. prep), above, high </p><p><strong><em>Facies </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Faciei</em></strong>), face</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:49:09',NULL,NULL),(19720,1092,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SuperFacial</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “above the surface”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Super + Faci- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Super </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Facies </em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:49:20',16,'2025-06-02 00:53:58'),(19721,1093,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Tension</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:49:43',NULL,NULL),(19722,1093,13,NULL,'<p>CLEAVAGE: Elastin and collagen fibers of the skin are oriented in regular directions and produce visible cleavage or tension lines in the skin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:49:49',NULL,NULL),(19723,1093,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tendere </em></strong>(L. v.), to expand, to stretch out;</p><p><strong><em>Tensum </em></strong>(past part.), stretched out&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 03:49:58',NULL,NULL),(19724,1093,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tension</em></strong></p><p>Literally, <em>“stretch mark”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Tens- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(5