L,16,'2025-01-02 23:19:01',NULL,NULL),(20141,2717,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Mucosus, -a, -um </em></strong>(L. adj.), <em>“phlegm-like”</em></p><p><strong><em>Mucus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Muci</em></strong>), <em>“phlegm from the nose”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:19:08',NULL,NULL),(20142,2720,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., MUSCULAR LAYER deeper than the perimetrium; the middle and the thickest layer of the uterine wall; consists of thick layer of longitudinal and circular smooth muscle cells.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:19:49',NULL,NULL),(20143,2720,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Myos</em> </strong>(Gr. n.), muscle</p><p><strong><em>Metrium </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Metria</em></strong>), the womb</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:19:55',NULL,NULL),(20144,2720,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Myo</em></strong><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=asthenia&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em>Metrium</em></strong></a><strong><em>,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “Muscle of the uterus”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Myo- + </u></em></strong><a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=asthenia&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\"><strong><em>Metrium</em></strong></a></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Myos</em> </strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Metrium</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:20:09',NULL,NULL),(20145,2721,13,NULL,'<p>Externally the breast of the male and female have raised central nipple surrounded by a circular pigmented Areola; the breasts differ in form and functions between the sexes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:20:28',NULL,NULL),(20146,2722,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Nitric</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:21:06',NULL,NULL),(20147,2722,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Oxide,</strong></p><p>A compound of 1 Oxygen + 1 other element, common in earth crust</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:21:15',NULL,NULL),(20148,2722,13,NULL,'<p>A Neurotransmitter substance that initiates blood engorgement of the penis; works along with Acetylcholine; diffuses into the smooth muscle cells of blood vessels causing smooth muscles to relax, blood rushes in to fill up the erectile tissues.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:21:25',NULL,NULL),(20149,2722,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Nitron </em></strong>(Gr. n.; also, <strong><em>Niter, Natron</em></strong>), hydrated sodium carbonate</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:21:31',NULL,NULL),(20150,2722,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Nitr- + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Nitron </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:21:39',NULL,NULL),(20151,2723,13,NULL,'<p>An unborn female fetus may contain in both Ovaries 5 million Oogonia, most of which self-destruct at birth; the remaining will undergo meiosis and mature to become Oocytes throughout the reproductive years of the female.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:21:58',NULL,NULL),(20152,2723,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Oo </em></strong>(Gr. n.), egg<strong><em> </em></strong>(Gr. variant of <strong><em>Ovum</em></strong>)</p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:22:04',NULL,NULL),(20153,2723,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Oocytes</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “egg cell”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Oo- + -cytes</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Oo </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cytos</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:22:15',NULL,NULL),(20154,2725,13,NULL,'<p>Production of secondary oocytes from Oogonia within the ovaries.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:22:56',NULL,NULL),(20155,2725,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Oo </em></strong>(Gr. n.), egg<strong><em> </em></strong>(Gr. variant of <strong><em>Ovum</em></strong>)</p><p><strong><em>Genesis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Geneses</em></strong>), beginning, origin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:23:04',NULL,NULL),(20156,2725,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>OoGenesis</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“origin of egg”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-center\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Oo + Genesis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Oo </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Genesis</em></strong> </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:23:14',NULL,NULL),(20157,2726,13,NULL,'<p>Primordial Oocytes; female fetus may contain in both Ovaries 5 million Oogonia; at birth most degenerates; the remaining undergo meiosis and mature to become Oocytes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:23:34',NULL,NULL),(20158,2726,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Oo </em></strong>(Gr. n.), egg<strong><em> </em></strong>(Gr. variant of <strong><em>Ovum</em></strong>)</p><p><strong><em>Gonas</em> </strong>(plu., <strong><em>Gonades</em>)</strong>, seed, ancestors</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:23:39',NULL,NULL),(20159,2726,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>OoGonia</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally,</em> <em>“eggs from the gonads”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Oo + Gon- + -ia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Oo </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Gonas</em> </strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ia </em></strong>(suffix), denotes condition, state (Absentia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:23:48',NULL,NULL),(20160,2728,13,NULL,'<p>Associated with the Ejaculation of sperm beginning with sexual arousal, Erection of the penis, secretion of mucus into the urethra, Ejaculation, and Emission, and Resolution (Would you a smoke, babe?)</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:24:21',NULL,NULL),(20161,2728,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Orgasmos</em></strong> <a href=\"http://etymonline.com/index.php?term=orgasm&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: black;\">(Gr. n.)</a>, sexual climax, <em>\"excitement, swelling\"</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:24:26',NULL,NULL),(20162,2730,13,NULL,'<p>Small opening of oviduct to the uterus</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:24:59',NULL,NULL),(20163,2730,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ostium </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Ostia</em></strong>), an entrance, mouth of the river</p><p>Metaphor for the opening to the uterus</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:25:03',NULL,NULL),(20164,2731,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Oval,</strong> adj.</p><p>metaphorically, “egg-shaped”</p><p><br></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:25:39',NULL,NULL),(20165,2731,13,NULL,'<p>Egg(s)&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:25:45',NULL,NULL),(20166,2731,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ovum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ova</em></strong>), egg</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:25:51',NULL,NULL),(20167,2733,13,NULL,'<p>Two small (2-3.5 X 1-1.5cm) organs for egg production attached by Mesovarium to the posterior surface of the broad ligament of the Uterus; also secured by Suspensory and </p><p>Ovarian Ligaments; capped by the Fimbriae of Fallopian Tube that catches the released egg.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:26:24',NULL,NULL),(20168,2733,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ovum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ova</em></strong>), egg</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:26:29',NULL,NULL),(20169,2733,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ovary</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “function for egg production”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Ova + -arium</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ova</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-arium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function, site; Eng., -ary</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-02 23:26:40',NUL