Duct during orgasm.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:07:18',NULL,NULL),(20334,2791,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Semen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Semines</em></strong>), semen, seed</p><p>The top seed!</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:07:24',NULL,NULL),(20335,2792,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Seminiferous</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:07:43',NULL,NULL),(20336,2792,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Tubules</strong></p><p>Extra fine tubes that channel semen</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:07:51',NULL,NULL),(20337,2792,13,NULL,'<p>Contains Spermatogonia, Primary and Secondary Spermatocytes, spermatids and sperm cells along the tightly wound Seminiferous Tubules in every lobule of the testicles; combined length from both testes is approximately .5 mile.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:07:59',NULL,NULL),(20338,2792,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Semen</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Semines</em></strong>), semen, seed<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p>The top seed!</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ferre</em></strong> (L. v.), to carry;</p><p><strong><em>Ferous </em></strong>(adj.), bearing, carrying<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:08:10',NULL,NULL),(20339,2792,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SeminiFerous,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “Semen bearing”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>Semini- + Ferous</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Semines</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ferous</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:08:19',NULL,NULL),(20340,2793,13,NULL,'<p>Dividers between lobules in the testes the continuation of the cortex forming lobules of Seminiferous Tubules; Each Testis contain 300 to 400 cone-shaped lobules.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:08:45',NULL,NULL),(20341,2793,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Septum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Septa</em></strong>), a fence, a partition, dividing wall</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:08:51',NULL,NULL),(20342,2793,12,NULL,'<p><strong>SEPTUM</strong>, INTERATRIAL – CARDIOVASCULAR</p><p><strong>SEPTUM</strong>, INTERVENTRICULAR – CARDIOVASCULAR</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:09:16',NULL,NULL),(20343,2794,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., SUSTENTACULAR CELLS / NURSE CELLS; Large cells that occupy the lumen of </p><p>the Seminiferous Tubules nursing the Germinal Cells and producing together with Interstitial (Leydig) Cells, Androgens, Estrogens, and Inhibins; also secrete the androgen-binding protein.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:09:39',NULL,NULL),(20344,2794,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sertoli</em></strong>, Enrico (1842–1910), Italian histologist described </p><p>the Sustencular cells and Germinal Cells in the </p><p>Seminiferous Tubules&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:09:45',NULL,NULL),(20345,2796,13,NULL,'<p>Derived from Germs Cells, the final phase of Spermatogenesis containing 23 Chromosomes with potential to fertilize the female Ovum, also possessing 23 Chromosomes.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:10:35',NULL,NULL),(20346,2796,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sperma </em></strong>(Gr. n), seed<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Zoon </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Zoa</em></strong>), animal</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:10:41',NULL,NULL),(20347,2797,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sperm</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:10:59',NULL,NULL),(20348,2797,13,NULL,'<p>short for SPERMATOZOON / plu., SPERMATOZOA; derived from Germs Cells, the final phase of Spermatogenesis containing 23 Chromosomes with potential to fertilize the female Ovum, also possessing 23 Chromosomes.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:11:05',NULL,NULL),(20349,2797,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spermatozoon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), animal seed</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:11:11',NULL,NULL),(20350,2798,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spermatic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:11:31',NULL,NULL),(20351,2798,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Cord</strong></p><p>Inguinal cord</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:11:38',NULL,NULL),(20352,2798,13,NULL,'<p>Collectively comprised of the Ductus Deferens, testicular artery, venous plexus, lymphatic vessels, nerve fibers, fibrous remnants of the Process Vaginalis.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:11:44',NULL,NULL),(20353,2798,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spermatozoon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), animal seed</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:11:50',NULL,NULL),(20354,2801,13,NULL,'<p>Secondary Spermatocytes undergo second meiosis producing smaller cells called Spermatids, the last phase of Spermatogenesis to form mature Sperm Cells or Spermatozoa; Spermatids develop into mature Sperm Cells complete with Acrosome, head, midbody, and Flagellum in the last phase of Spermatogenesis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:12:27',NULL,NULL),(20355,2801,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spermatozoon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), animal seed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:12:32',NULL,NULL),(20356,2801,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Sperma- + -tid</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sperma </em></strong><em>derived from</em> <strong><em>Spermatozoon </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-tid</em></strong> (suffix),<strong><em> </em></strong>offspring, descendant</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:12:39',NULL,NULL),(20358,2802,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., SPERMIOGENESIS. The stages of sperm cell development from Spermatogonia to Primary and Secondary Spermatocytes, to Spermatids, to Sperm Cells within the seminiferous </p><p>tubules start from the basement membrane for the most immature germs cells moving into the lumen.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:21:35',NULL,NULL),(20359,2802,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spermatozoon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), animal seed</p><p><strong><em>Genesis</em></strong> (L. n.), beginning, origin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:21:39',NULL,NULL),(20360,2802,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SpermatoGenesis</em></strong> </p><p>From spermatogonia to developed sperm</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Spermato- + Genesis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spermatozoon </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Genesis</em></strong> (L. n.), beginning, origin</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:21:47',NULL,NULL),(20361,2803,13,NULL,'<p>Most immature Germ Cells containing 46 Chromosomes lodged closest to the basement membrane of the Seminiferous Tubules; nursed by Sertoli/sustentacular cells.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:22:21',NULL,NULL),(20362,2803,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spermatozoon</em></strong> (Gr. n.), animal seed</p><p><strong><em>Gonas</em> </strong>(plu., <strong><em>Gonades</em>)</strong>, seed, semen</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:22:26',NULL,NULL),(20363,2803,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SpermatoGonia</em></strong> </p><p>Literally, <em>“sperm from the Gonads”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Spermato- + Gon- + -ia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spermatozoon </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Gon- </em></strong><em>derived from</em> <strong><em>Gonades</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-ia</em></strong> (suffix), denotes condition, state (Absentia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:22:47',NULL,NULL),(20364,2804,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spiral</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:23:12',NULL,NULL),(20365,2804,13,NULL,'<p>Spiral Glands consisting of Cuboidal endometrial cells, residual epithelial cells in the endometrium are replaced by columnar cells to form tubular spiral glands that supply nutrients to the new endometrial cells with fluid rich in glycogen.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:23:18',NULL,NULL),(20366,2804,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Speira </em></strong>(L. n.), anything wound or coiled</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:23:25',NULL,NULL),(20367,2804,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Spira + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Speira </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:23:32',NULL,NULL),(20368,2806,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spongy</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:24:08',NULL,NULL),(20369,2806,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Urethra,</strong></p><p>Tube from the bladder to the penile orifice</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:24:16',NULL,NULL),(20370,2806,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., PENILE URETHRA; Part of the urethra that spans the length of the penis from the pelvic floor to the Penile Orifice</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:24:24',NULL,NULL),(20371,2806,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spongiosus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), porous </p><p>Metaphor for the spongy tissue when engorged in blood</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:24:30',NULL,NULL),(20372,2807,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Superficial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:24:58',NULL,NULL),(20373,2807,13,NULL,'<p>Opening of the inguinal canal through the Aponeurosis (junction of muscle and tendon) of Transversus Abdominis Muscles; ends at the Deep Inguinal Rings, opens into the </p><p>Aponeurosis of External Abdominal Oblique Muscles.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:25:04',NULL,NULL),(20374,2807,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Superficial, </em></strong></p><p>Sense of being above the surface</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:25:09',NULL,NULL),(20375,2809,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Suspensory</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:25:38',NULL,NULL),(20376,2809,13,NULL,'<p>Attaches the Mesovarium to the pelvic wall.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:25:45',NULL,NULL),(20377,2809,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Suspendere </em></strong>(L. v.),<strong><em> </em></strong>to hang;</p><p><strong><em>Suspensum </em></strong>(past part.), hanged&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:25:52',NULL,NULL),(20378,2809,12,NULL,'<p>SUSPENSORY LIGAMENTS – SPECIAL SENSES</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:26:03',NULL,NULL),(20379,2810,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sustentacular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:26:36',NULL,NULL),(20380,2810,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., SERTOLI CELLS /NURSE CELLS; Large cells that occupy the lumen of the Seminiferous Tubules nurse the Germinal Cells and produce together with Interstitial (Leydig) Cells, Androgens, Estrogens, and Inhibins; also secrete the androgen-binding protein.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:26:43',NULL,NULL),(20381,2810,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sustentaculum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Sustentacula</em></strong>), small support </p><p>diminutive of<strong><em> Sustentum</em></strong>, support</p><p>Sustains. Sustenance.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:26:49',NULL,NULL),(20382,2811,13,NULL,'<p>Inside the Scrotum are two Small ovoid organs, about 4 to 5 cm long; contain approximately a combined, 0.5 miles of Seminiferous Tubules and Leydig Cells; function both as Exocrine and Endocrine glands producing sperm cells and testosterone.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:27:16',NULL,NULL),(20383,2811,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Testiculus </em></strong><u>(plu., </u><strong><em>Testiculi</em></strong>), small gonad </p><p>diminutive of<strong><em> Testis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Testes</em></strong>), gonad</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:27:22',NULL,NULL),(20384,2813,13,NULL,'<p>Major male hormone secreted by the Testes classified as Androgen, stimulating the development of male reproductive apparatus and secondary sexual characteristics.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:28:09',NULL,NULL),(20385,2813,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Testis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Testes</em></strong>), gonad </p><p><strong><em>Ester</em></strong>, Esterol</p><p><strong><em>Hormon</em></strong> (L. n.), stimulant<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:28:15',NULL,NULL),(20386,2813,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>TestoEsterone,</em></strong></p><p><em>“man-maker” hormone</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Testo- + Ester- + </u></em></strong><a href=\"http://www.etymonline.com/index.php?term=-one&amp;allowed_in_frame=0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_bl