rowth</p><p><strong><em>Blastos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), germinal cell, a bud, sprout&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:30:41',NULL,NULL),(20397,2817,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>TrophoBlasts,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “embryo stakes a spot on the uterus by eating it”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Tropho + Blasts</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trophos</em></strong> </p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Blastos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:30:55',NULL,NULL),(20398,2819,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Tubuli</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:31:59',NULL,NULL),(20399,2819,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Recti</strong></p><p>Straight, upright</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:32:06',NULL,NULL),(20400,2819,13,NULL,'<p>Tubules within each lobule become Tubuli Recti and join with the other Tubuli Recti of another lobules to form Rete Testes, a network of Tubuli Recti.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:32:14',NULL,NULL),(20401,2819,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tubuli</em></strong>, small tubes; </p><p>plural form of <strong><em>Tubulus Rectus</em></strong>.</p><p>diminutive of<strong><em> Tubus</em></strong>, tube, pipe</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:32:21',NULL,NULL),(20402,2820,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Tunica</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:32:42',NULL,NULL),(20403,2820,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Albuginea</strong></p><p>Dense whitish fibrous connective tissue</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:32:50',NULL,NULL),(20404,2820,13,NULL,'<p>Thick outer coat of the Testes, consisting of fibrous connective tissue, hundreds of invaginations into the medulla of the Testes that are septa between 300-400 cone-shaped lobules </p><p>containing Seminiferous Tubules&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 06:32:57',NULL,NULL),(20405,2820,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tunicum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tunica</em></strong>), protective sleeved garment worn like a coat</p><p>m