ncoming Action Potential can be responded to by the muscle.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:23:41',NULL,NULL),(20485,1808,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Absolvere</em></strong> (L. v.), to unbind, to set free;</p><p><strong><em>Absolutus </em></strong>(past part.), unbound, freed<em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></p><p>Metaphor for the muscle being <em>“unbound” </em></p><p>From a resting membrane potential</p><p>by an Action Potential&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:23:48',44,'2025-03-31 01:18:58'),(20486,1809,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Accessory</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:24:08',NULL,NULL),(20487,1809,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Cranial Nerve XI</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:24:14',NULL,NULL),(20488,1809,13,NULL,'<p>Literally<em> “helping”</em> nerve for added depth of breathing by innervating the Levator Scapulae Muscle</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:24:21',NULL,NULL),(20489,1809,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Accedere</em></strong> (L v.), to aid, to add to<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Accessum </em></strong>(past. part.), added to</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:24:28',NULL,NULL),(20490,1809,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Accessory</em></strong></p><p>Literally,<em> “helping” </em>nerve.</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Access- </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Accessum</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ory</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:24:36',16,'2025-06-03 00:55:48'),(20491,1810,13,NULL,'<p>The responses of muscles to reset back to Resting Membrane Potential (-70 to -90Mv) are diminished with repeated depolarization-repolarization cycles.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:24:53',NULL,NULL),(20492,1810,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Accomodare</em></strong> (L. v.), to fit, adapt; </p><p><strong><em>Accomodatum</em></strong> (past part). adapted&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:25:01',NULL,NULL),(20493,1810,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Accomodation,</em></strong></p><p>Literally, “<em>getting calloused”</em></p><p><em>by repeated depolarization-repolarization</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Accomodat- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Accomodatum</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-ion, </em></strong>suffix, forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:25:11',16,'2025-06-03 00:56:12'),(20494,1811,13,NULL,'<p>Neurochemical stimuli released from the Pre-Synaptic Membrane in the Motor Unit for uptake to the Post-Synaptic Membrane, on the muscle side, for Action Potential Propagation.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:26:09',NULL,NULL),(20495,1811,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Acetum </em></strong>(L. n.), classically: vinegar, acid,<em> “wine turned sour”</em></p><p><strong><em>Choline</em></strong>, Quaternary Ammonium Cation; Vit. B complex, Lecithin</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 10:26:16',NULL,NULL),(20496,1811,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AcetylCholine</em></strong>,</p><p>electro-chemical neurotransmitter</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Acet-</u></em></strong><u> </u><strong><u>+ </u><em><u>-yl + Choline</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Acetum</em></strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs