rong><em>Collus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Colli</em></strong>), neck</p><p>(imagery is questionable, except for the location, small neck) </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:14:50',NULL,NULL),(20735,1886,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., FUNICULI / TRACTS / PATHWAYS; made up of axons grouped in columns along the Spinal Cord; relay sensory or motor messages to/from the brain.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:15:12',NULL,NULL),(20736,1886,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Columna</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Columnae</em></strong>), the peak, stature, support </p><p>Metaphor for unique pathways for nerve impulses</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:15:20',NULL,NULL),(20737,1889,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Commissural</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:16:39',NULL,NULL),(20738,1889,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Fibers</strong></p><p>nerve fibers, axons, dendrites</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:16:49',NULL,NULL),(20739,1889,13,NULL,'<p>Nerve tracts are either <u>association</u>, <u>projection</u>, and <u>commissural</u>: </p><p><strong>Association</strong>: &nbsp;connects to the same hemisphere; </p><p><strong>Projection</strong>: &nbsp;connects the cerebrum to other parts of the brain and spinal cord; </p><p><strong>Commissural fibers</strong>: criss-cross over, left to right/right to left, to the other hemisphere.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:16:56',NULL,NULL),(20740,1889,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Commisura</em></strong> (L. n.), sending with </p><p>literally, <em>“send messages with”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-03 23:17:19',NULL,NULL),(20741,1889,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Commisura </u></em></strong><u>+ </u><strong><em><u>-al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>Commisura</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 65, 85); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·            </em></strong><strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>'