,'2025-01-05 02:53:09',NULL,NULL),(21341,2091,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Ranvier</strong></p><p>1835-1922, described discontinuities of myelination</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 02:53:17',NULL,NULL),(21342,2091,13,NULL,'<p>Notches between Myelinated axons where rapid Saltatory Depolarization takes place; Action Potentials jump from node to node, rather than inch through the full length of axons.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 02:53:28',NULL,NULL),(21343,2091,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Nodus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Nodi</em></strong>), a knot, knob</p><p><strong>Nodes</strong>, unmyelinated breaks along the axons</p><p>RANVIER, study of minute anatomy</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 02:53:34',NULL,NULL),(21344,2092,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., NOREPINEPHRINE; precursor to Adrenaline produced by the Adrenal Gland; exerts Sympathetic Mode effect on Cardiovascular system, liver and adipocytes: increased heart-beat, increased blood flow to muscles, more glucose into circulation.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 02:54:04',NULL,NULL),(21345,2092,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Nore-</em></strong> (Chemistry prefix), denotes origin</p><p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards</p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 02:54:12',NULL,NULL),(21346,2092,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>NorAdRenaline</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “coming from above the kidney”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Nor + -Ad + Renal + -ine</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Nore-</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Renal</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ine </em></strong>(suffix), simple compound <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 02:54:29',NULL,NULL),(21347,2093,13,NULL,'<p>a.