02:57',NULL,NULL),(21586,2183,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pupilla</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pupillae</em></strong>), imagery: <em>“a tiny creature”</em>; </p><p>Diminutive form of: <strong><em>Pupa</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pupae</em></strong>), a small creature, a doll. </p><p>metaphorically, <em>“a tiny creature (image) in the eye”</em> </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:03:07',NULL,NULL),(21587,2184,13,NULL,'<p>Bilateral prominent mounds on the anterior aspect of the Medulla Oblongata, inferior to the Olivary; figuratively named for its pyramidal shape, despite their miniscule size.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:03:30',NULL,NULL),(21588,2184,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pyramid</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pyramides</em></strong>), funeral pyre and storage of Pharao’s wealth </p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pyre</u></em></strong><u>,</u><strong><em><u> </u></em></strong><u>funeral pyre</u><strong><em><u> + mids</u></em></strong><u>,</u><strong><em><u> </u></em></strong><u>storage</u></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:03:36',NULL,NULL),(21589,2185,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pyramidal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:03:54',NULL,NULL),(21590,2185,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Decussation</strong></p><p>Cross-over </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:04:01',NULL,NULL),(21591,2185,13,NULL,'<p>Neuron fibers<em> </em>bridging each side of the pyramids for bilateral communication for motor control.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:04:07',NULL,NULL),(21592,2185,8,NULL,'<p>metaphorically, pyramid-like <em>\"mound\"</em></p><p><strong><em>Pyramid</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pyramides</em></strong>), funeral pyre and storage of Pharao’s wealth </p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Pyre</u></em></strong><u>,</u><strong><em><u> </u></em></strong><u>funeral pyre</u><strong><em><u> + mids</u></em></strong><u>,</u><strong><em><u> </u></em></strong><u>storage</u></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:04:15',NULL,NULL),(21593,2191,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Receptors</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:05:37',NULL,NULL),(21594,2191,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Site</strong></p><p>matching ligands</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:05:43',NULL,NULL),(21595,2191,13,NULL,'<p>Are proteins or glycoproteins that are equipped with protein marker to which specific Ligands match and attach for transport purposes.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:05:49',NULL,NULL),(21596,2191,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Recipire </em></strong>(L. v.), to take back;</p><p><strong><em>Receptum</em></strong> (past part.), taken, received&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:05:57',NULL,NULL),(21597,2192,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Receptor</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:06:19',NULL,NULL),(21598,2192,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Potential</strong></p><p>Action potential</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:06:28',NULL,NULL),(21599,2192,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., GENERATOR POTENTIALS; a stimulus can trigger a local potential to a receptor, </p><p>responded to rapidly by PRIMARY RECEPTORS; sort of <em>“atopic”</em> Action Potential.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:06:37',NULL,NULL),(21600,2192,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Recipire </em></strong>(L. v.), to take back</p><p><strong><em>Receptum</em></strong> (past part.), taken, received;&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:06:45',NULL,NULL),(21601,2194,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reciprocal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:07:17',NULL,NULL),(21602,2194,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Innervation</strong></p><p>By Antagonist Vs. Agonist muscles in harmony</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:07:24',NULL,NULL),(21603,2194,13,NULL,'<p>Works in response to a withdrawal reflex by relaxing the extensor muscles when the flexor muscle reflexively contract; avoids avulsion of extensor muscles on sudden flexion.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:07:30',NULL,NULL),(21604,2194,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reciprocare</em></strong> (L. v.), to respond; alternate back and forth <strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Antagonist </em></strong>Vs. <strong><em>Agonist </em></strong></p><p>literally, <em>\"mutually reciprocating”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:07:37',NULL,NULL),(21605,2195,13,NULL,'<p>Homeostatic response to a stimulus that occurs without conscious volition. Involuntary nervous response regulated by the Autonomic Nervous System;<em> </em>literally, <em>“bent again” </em>to respond.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:07:56',NULL,NULL),(21606,2196,13,NULL,'<p>Characteristic of responding automatically and instantaneously without volition;<em> </em>literally, <em>“bent again” </em>to respond.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:08:15',NULL,NULL),(21607,2197,13,NULL,'<p>Bending of light through a lens, or through transparent medium. scientifically <em>\"re-breaking” </em>of light.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:08:34',NULL,NULL),(21608,2197,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Frangere </em></strong>(L. v.), to break; <strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Fractum </em></strong>(past part.), broken, shattered&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:08:42',NULL,NULL),(21609,2198,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Refractory</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:09:40',NULL,NULL),(21610,2198,13,NULL,'<p>Reduced sensitivity of muscles for further stimulation when an Action Potential is in progress; two types: absolute and relative</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:09:46',NULL,NULL),(21611,2198,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Frangere </em></strong>(v.), to break; <strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Fractum </em></strong>(past part.), broken, shattered&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>-ory </em></strong>(suffix), denotes function location</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:09:57',NULL,NULL),(21612,2199,13,NULL,'<p>Process of re-setting electrical polarity in muscle membrane to Resting Membrane Potential at -72 to -90 mV.; driven by Na-K -/+ ionic concentration gradient.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:10:19',NULL,NULL),(21613,2199,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Polaris </em></strong>(adj.), opposite;<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Polus</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Poli</em></strong>), pole, opposite ends of spectrum</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:10:27',NULL,NULL),(21614,2199,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>RePolarisation</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “resetting opposite forces (+/-)”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Re- + Polaris + -ation</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Polaris</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ation</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:11:11',NULL,NULL),(21615,2200,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Reticular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:11:30',NULL,NULL),(21616,2200,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Formation</strong></p><p>Screening&nbsp;network for self-reflection</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:11:39',NULL,NULL),(21617,2200,13,NULL,'<p>A group of nuclei distributed along the brainstem that receive messages from the senses that control the face and emotion.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:11:45',NULL,NULL),(21618,2200,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticulum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Reticula</em></strong>), small fishing net</p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong>,&nbsp;net</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:11:55',NULL,NULL),(21619,2200,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Reticular,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “screening for face and emotion”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Reticula + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Reticula</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:12:04',NULL,NULL),(21620,2201,13,NULL,'<p>Innermost neuronal tunic of the eye; serves as a protective covering of the Vitreous Humor, </p><p>contains Pigmented Retina and the Sensory Retina for the rods and cones, and relay neurons.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:12:24',NULL,NULL),(21621,2201,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Retina </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Retines</em></strong>), a small net; <strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong>, a net</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:12:33',NULL,NULL),(21622,2202,13,NULL,'<p>Inflammation of the retina</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:12:49',NULL,NULL),(21623,2202,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Retina </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Retines</em></strong>), a small net; <strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Rete</em></strong>, a net</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:12:55',NULL,NULL),(21624,2202,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Retin- + -itis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Retina</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-itis </em></strong>(suffix), denotes inflammation</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:13:04',NULL,NULL),(21625,2203,13,NULL,'<p>Rod shaped photo receptors contains discs Protein; Opsin covalently bound to pigmented </p><p>Retinal that responds to light stimuli and breakdown in the absence of light.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:13:28',NULL,NULL),(21626,2203,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Rhodos </em></strong>(Gr.), shades of red, pink, purple, </p><p><strong><em>Ops</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Opses</em></strong>), sight, vision, appearance<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:13:32',NULL,NULL),(21627,2203,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>RhodOpsin</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “red eye protein”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Rhodos + Ops + -in</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Rhodos</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ops</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:13:41',NULL,NULL),(21628,2204,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Ruffini</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:14:10',NULL,NULL),(21629,2204,13,NULL,'<p>Terminal knobs of Dendrites branching off axons protected by connective tissue capsule; </p><p>sensors for pressure and stretch on the skin surfaces.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:14:19',NULL,NULL),(21630,2204,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ruffini</em></strong>, Angelo<strong><em> </em></strong>(1874 – 1929), Italian Anatomist </p><p>described Ruffini’s corpuscle in the skin of fingers </p><p>as pressure sensors</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:14:24',NULL,NULL),(21631,2206,13,NULL,'<p>short for <strong>Os Sacrum</strong>, poetically, “<em>sacred bone</em>”</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:14:56',NULL,NULL),(21632,2206,13,NULL,'<p>4-5 fused bones in the inferior Vertebral Column; articulates with the Ilium of the Os Coxae forming the Pelvic Basin; Sacrum was thought of as a sacred bone.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:15:05',NULL,NULL),(21633,2206,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sacrus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), holy, sacred&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:15:11',NULL,NULL),(21634,2207,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Sacral</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:15:35',NULL,NULL),(21635,2207,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Plexus</strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><em>“folded, braided” </em>Ventral Roots of Spinal Nerves</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 