Sphincter</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:24:00',NULL,NULL),(21678,2219,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pupillae&nbsp;</strong></p><p>“of the pupil” (eye)</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:24:09',NULL,NULL),(21679,2219,13,NULL,'<p>Smooth muscle that narrows-constricts the diameter of the pupil.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:24:15',NULL,NULL),(21680,2219,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sphingere </em></strong>(L. v.), to grip, to hold tight</p><p><strong><em>Sphinctum </em></strong>(past part.), held tight, gripped;&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:24:22',NULL,NULL),(21681,2219,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sphinctor</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “constrictor”</em> muscle</p><p><span style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sphinct- + -or</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sphinctum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-or(s)</em></strong> (suffix), denotes agent of action</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:24:31',NULL,NULL),(21682,2220,13,NULL,'<p>Pointed posteriorly processes of Vertebrae from the Cervicals to the Thoracic levels are spinous, thus “<em>spine</em>”; the lumbar spines are thick and blunt.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:24:55',NULL,NULL),(21683,2220,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spina </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Spinae</em></strong>), classically, <em>“thorn, spine”</em></p><p>metaphor for Vertebral Spinous Process</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:25:02',NULL,NULL),(21684,2221,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spinal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:25:19',NULL,NULL),(21685,2221,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Column</strong></p><p>Support, pillar</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:25:27',NULL,NULL),(21686,2221,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Vertebral Column;</strong> composed of: 26 Vertebrae in situ (7 Cervical, 12 Thoracic, 5 Lumbar), 1 Sacrum (4-5 fused bones), 1 Coccyx (3-4 fused bones).&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:25:35',NULL,NULL),(21687,2221,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spina </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Spinae</em></strong>), classically, <em>“thorn, spine”</em></p><p>metaphor for Vertebral Spinous Process</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:25:41',NULL,NULL),(21688,2222,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spinal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:07',NULL,NULL),(21689,2222,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Cord</strong></p><p>Composed of afferent-efferent, spinal nerve tracts</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:15',NULL,NULL),(21690,2222,13,NULL,'<p>Housed in the Vertebral Canal is the “<em>freeway</em>” for Sensory and Motor innervations between the brain and the Peripheral Nervous System. Injury resulting in severance to the Spinal Cord cuts off sensory and motor innervation inferior to the injury.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:22',NULL,NULL),(21691,2222,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spina </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Spinae</em></strong>), classically, <em>“thorn, spine”</em></p><p>metaphor for Vertebral Spinous Process</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:27',NULL,NULL),(21692,2223,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Spinal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:45',NULL,NULL),(21693,2223,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Nerves</strong></p><p>Originate from Spinal Cord à Spinal Nerve Root</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:53',NULL,NULL),(21694,2223,13,NULL,'<p>Anterior nerve roots and Posterior nerve roots originating from the Spinal Cord merging at the vertebral foramina as Spinal Nerve Roots; each nerve root, Ventral and Dorsal combined, is a bundle of 6-8 rootlets.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:26:59',NULL,NULL),(21695,2223,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spina </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Spinae</em></strong>), classically, <em>“thorn, spine”</em></p><p>metaphor for Vertebral Spinous Process</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:27:11',NULL,NULL),(21696,2225,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Splanchnic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:27:49',NULL,NULL),(21697,2225,13,NULL,'<p>Sympathetic innervation to the abdominal Viscera; monitors abnormal growth, stretches and swelling</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:27:57',NULL,NULL),(21698,2225,13,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Splanchna</em></strong> (Gr. n.), visceral entrails, intestinal organs</p><p>poetically, the wellspring of <em>“melancholy”</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:28:03',NULL,NULL),(21699,2226,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Stapes</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:28:26',NULL,NULL),(21700,2226,13,NULL,'<p>One of three Auditory Ossicles that responds (moves) to mechanical stimulus of external sound vibrations, yet to be interpreted in the cortex. <strong><em>Stapedius Muscle.</em></strong>, attenuating muscle for <strong><em>Stapes</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:28:32',NULL,NULL),(21701,2226,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stapes</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Stapedes</em></strong>), a stirrup<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Stapedius, -ia, -ium</em></strong> (L. adj.), pertaining to the Stapes</p><p>metaphor for the shape of Stapes</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:28:41',NULL,NULL),(21702,2227,13,NULL,'<p>Homeostasis, state of balance for water, blood profusion, temperature, chemistry throughout the body.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:29:00',NULL,NULL),(21703,2227,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stasis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Stases</em></strong>), state of standing still, stable condition</p><p>literally, <em>“standing still, stable”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:29:06',NULL,NULL),(21704,2228,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Static</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:29:28',NULL,NULL),(21705,2228,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Labyrinth</strong></p><p>Cavernous twisting and turning passageway</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:29:37',NULL,NULL),(21706,2228,13,NULL,'<p>Utricle and Saccule of the Vestibule in the auditory apparatus evaluates head position and linear acceleration.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:29:45',NULL,NULL),(21707,2228,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Stare </em></strong>(L. v.), to stay still</p><p><strong><em>Statum 