 04:45:34',NULL,NULL),(21773,2249,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Tentorium</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:47:05',NULL,NULL),(21774,2249,13,NULL,'<p>The membrane separating the Cerebrum and Cerebellum; appearing like <em>“tent”</em> of the Cerebellum</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:47:10',NULL,NULL),(21775,2249,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tentorium</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tentoria</em></strong>), tent, roof</p><p>figuratively, <em>“tent”</em> of the Cerebellum</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:47:16',NULL,NULL),(21776,2250,13,NULL,'<p>Largest part of the center of Diencephalon, a cluster of nuclei with two lateral lobes connected by Interthalamic Adhesion; sensory inputs synapse within the nuclei and project to the cerebral cortex, subthalamus, epithalamus, hypothalamus.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:47:56',NULL,NULL),(21777,2250,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Thalamus</strong> (plu., <strong>Thalami</strong>), Classically, <em>“an inner bedroom for intimacy”</em></p><p>an apartment for women in ancient Greece</p><p>metaphor for Thalamus secluded location in the brain</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:48:24',NULL,NULL),(21778,2251,13,NULL,'<p>Responds to changes in temperature; disorder of this receptor results in frequent burns.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:48:46',NULL,NULL),(21779,2251,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thermos</em></strong> (Gr. n.), heat<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Recipire </em></strong>(L. v.), to take back</p><p><strong><em>Receptum</em></strong> (past part.), taken, received;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-05 04:48:56',NULL,NULL),(21780,2251,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ThermoReceptor</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “heat sensor”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Thermo- + Recept- + -or</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thermos</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Receptum</em></s