ining to the palate</p><p><em>derived from</em></p><p><strong><em>Palatum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Palata</em></strong>), classically, “<em>sense of taste”</em></p><p><strong> </strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:38:00',16,'2025-04-29 00:45:06'),(23233,4083,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Parietal</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:38:17',16,'2025-04-24 01:27:26'),(23234,4083,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Bone</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:38:24',16,'2025-04-29 00:45:34'),(23235,4083,13,NULL,'<p>Cranial Bones on the lateral aspects of the Calvarium.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:38:30',NULL,NULL),(23236,4083,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Pares</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Parieta</em></strong>) classically, <em>wall</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:38:39',16,'2025-04-29 00:46:14'),(23237,4083,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Parietal</em></strong>,</p><p>metaphorically, <em>“walls”</em> of the brain case</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Pariet- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Parietes</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:38:46',16,'2025-04-29 00:45:59'),(23238,4084,13,NULL,'<p>The knee cap; large Sesamoid bone of the Quadriceps Femoris that Articulates with the <strong>Patellar Groove</strong> of the Femur for sliding motion with the <strong>Patellar Facets</strong> during knee extension-flexion.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:39:04',16,'2025-04-24 01:27:55'),(23239,4084,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Patella</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, a small plate</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">metaphor for the large sesamoid knee <em>“cap” </em>bone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:39:11',16,'2025-04-29 00:47:05'),(23240,4085,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Patellar</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:39:27',16,'2025-04-24 01:29:12'),(23241,4085,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Facets, </strong></p><p>smooth bony surfaces on a bone process for sliding joint</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:39:31',16,'2025-04-29 00:47:48'),(23242,4085,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The posterior patella is wedge-shaped, smooth surfaces on both sides that articulates with the <strong>Patellar Groove</strong> of the Femur, also equipped with facets for sliding motion.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:39:42',16,'2025-04-29 00:48:05'),(23243,4085,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Patella</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, a <em>“small plate”</em></p><p>metaphor for the large sesamoid knee <em>“cap” </em>bone<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:39:50',16,'2025-04-29 00:48:22'),(23244,4086,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Patellar</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:40:06',16,'2025-04-24 01:29:41'),(23245,4086,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Groove, </strong></p><p>V- shaped canal</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:40:11',16,'2025-04-29 00:49:21'),(23246,4086,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The V-shaped groove at the anterior-inferior end of the Femur provides smooth sliding surfaces for the Patellar Facets ( posterior aspect of the patella) during knee flexion-extension.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:40:22',16,'2025-04-29 00:51:08'),(23247,4086,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Patella</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, a <em>“small plate”</em></p><p>metaphor for the large sesamoid knee <em>“cap” </em>bone<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:40:30',16,'2025-04-29 00:51:21'),(23248,4087,15,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Patellar</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:40:48',16,'2025-04-29 00:51:53'),(23249,4087,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Retinaculum, </strong></p><p>Metaphorically, <em>“net-like strap”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:40:52',16,'2025-04-29 00:52:06'),(23250,4087,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Fibrocartilaginous portion of the Quadriceps Femoris Tendons that prevents the patella from lateral dislocation.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:41:03',16,'2025-04-29 00:52:18'),(23251,4087,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Patella</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, a <em>“small plate”</em></p><p>metaphor for the large sesamoid knee <em>“cap” </em>bone<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:41:16',16,'2025-04-29 00:52:31'),(23252,4088,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Zygopophyseal Processess</strong>; the bilateral Pedicles arising from the posterior Vertebral Body give rise to the Superior and Inferior Articular Processes of Vertebrae, the Lamina and the Posterior arches, that form the Vertebral Canal of the Vertebral Column, in situ.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:41:40',16,'2025-04-24 01:30:07'),(23253,4088,8,NULL,'<p>  <strong><em>Pes</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pedes</em></strong>), a foot </p><p>  </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:41:48',NULL,NULL),(23254,4088,9,NULL,'<p>  <strong><em>Pediculus</em></strong> </p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Pes</em></strong>, small foot; </p><p>metaphor for the process giving rise to the Articular Processes</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong> <em><u>Pedi- + -culus</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Pedes</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-culus </em></strong>(suffix), denotes dim. form</p><p>  </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:41:57',NULL,NULL),(23255,4089,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Pes</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:44:09',16,'2025-04-24 01:30:30'),(23256,4089,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Anserinus</strong>, </p><p>Figuratively, <em>“goose-like”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 13:44:14',NULL,NULL),(23257,4089,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Insertions of 3 thigh Adductor muscles on the proximal Tibia at the medial 