(MM.)</p><p><a href=\"about:blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TRANSVERSARIUS</a> (M.)</p><p>TRANSVERSE (ARYTENOID M.)</p><p>TRANSVERSE (COLON)</p><p>TRANSVERSE (MESECOLON) </p><p>TRANSVERSE (MUSCLE)</p><p>TRANSVERSE<strong> / </strong>TRANSVERSUS<strong> </strong></p><p>TRANSVERSUS (ABDOMINIS M.)</p><p>TRANSVERSUS (PERINEI PROFUNDUS M.)</p><p>TRANSVERSUS (PERINEI SUPERFICIALIS M.)</p><p>TRANSVERSUS (THORACIS M.)</p><p>BIO<u>TRANS</u>FORMATION</p><p>  </p>',8,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:28:18',NULL,NULL),(23458,4142,13,NULL,'<p>1 of 8 Carpal Bones: <strong><em>Trapezium, Lunate, Capitate, Hamate, Trapezoid, Scaphoid, Triquetrum, Pisiform.</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:28:36',16,'2025-04-24 02:47:16'),(23459,4142,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Trapezium</em></strong> (L. n.), 4-sided plane with unequal sides</p><p>metaphor for the shape of Trapezium Bone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:28:43',16,'2025-04-29 02:11:53'),(23460,4143,13,NULL,'<p>1 out of 8 Carpal bones; <strong><em>Triquetrum, Lunate, Capitate, Hamate, Trapezoid, Scaphoid, Pisiform.</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:29:02',16,'2025-04-24 02:49:17'),(23461,4143,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Triquetrus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), having 3-cornered</p><p>Figurative for the shape of <strong><em>Triquetrum Bone</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:29:09',16,'2025-04-29 02:10:43'),(23462,4144,13,NULL,'<p>Femoral Tuberosity close to the femoral neck, the insertion of the major walking/running muscles&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:29:31',16,'2025-04-24 02:49:43'),(23463,4144,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Trokhanter </em></strong>(Gr. n.), figuratively, <em>“pulley”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><em>derived from </em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Trekhein </em></strong>(Gr. v.), to run</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Muscles “pull” on the trochanter during extension in the act of running.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:29:39',16,'2025-04-29 02:14:33'),(23464,4145,13,NULL,'<p>small area of prominent rough bony landmark for tendinous attachment</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:29:55',16,'2025-04-24 02:50:25'),(23465,4145,8,NULL,'<p> <strong><em>Tuberculum</em></strong>, classically, <em>“small root crop”</em> (diminutive form)</p><p><strong><em>Tuber </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Tuberes</em></strong>), classically, “<em>root crop</em>” </p><p>Metaphor for rough surface, small bumps on bones </p><p>  </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:30:06',NULL,NULL),(23466,4146,13,NULL,'<p>Bony landmark characterized by prominent rough bumps on surface; site for tendon attachment</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:30:22',NULL,NULL),(23467,4146,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Tuberosus</em></strong> (L. adj.), rough surface</p><p><strong><em>Tuber </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Tuberes</em></strong>), classically, “<em>root crop</em>”</p><p>Metaphor for rough surface on bones</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:30:30',16,'2025-04-29 02:15:29'),(23468,4147,13,NULL,'<p>Rough prominent bumps on surfaces of bones, sites of tendinous attachment.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:30:47',16,'2025-04-24 02:50:55'),(23469,4147,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Tuberosus</em></strong> (L. adj.), figuratively, <em>“rough surface”</em></p><p><strong><em>Tuber </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Tuberes</em></strong>), classically, “<em>root crop</em>”</p><p>Metaphor for rough surface on bones</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:30:53',16,'2025-04-29 02:16:03'),(23470,4148,13,NULL,'<p>Forearm bone on the medial aspect ; prominent feature: Olecranon Process, the elbow.</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">(Radial Bone is on the lateral aspect)</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:31:10',16,'2025-04-29 02:16:56'),(23471,4148,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Ulna</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ulnera</em></strong>), classically, <em>elbow</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:31:20',16,'2025-04-29 02:17:15'),(23472,4166,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Translation:<strong> </strong><em>“of the Ulnar bone”</em>; description of muscles in the forearm moving hands and fingers. The bone prominent part is the <strong><em>Olecranon</em></strong> Process, elbow</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:32:04',16,'2025-04-30 00:46:58'),(23473,4166,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Ulneris,</em></strong> <em>“of the Ulnar bone”</em><strong><em> </em></strong>(possessive form)</p><p><strong><em>Ulna</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ulnera</em></strong>), elbow</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:32:13',16,'2025-04-30 00:47:12'),(23474,4149,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Uncinate</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:32:30',16,'2025-04-24 02:51:23'),(23475,4149,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Process,</strong></p><p>Prominent projecting part of a bone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:32:37',16,'2025-04-29 02:17:37'),(23476,4149,13,NULL,'<p>Hook-like process.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:32:42',NULL,NULL),(23477,4149,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Uncinatus, -a, -um</em></strong> (adj.), literally, <em>“provided with a hook”</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:32:48',16,'2025-04-29 02:18:06'),(23478,4150,7,NULL,'<p>  Vertebrae, plu.<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p>  </p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:33:04',NULL,NULL),(23479,4150,13,NULL,'<p>26 Vertebrae of the Vertebral Column: 7 Cervical; 12 Thoracic; 5 Lumbar; 2 bones, Sacrum and Coccyx, that are fused from 3-4 bones, SYNOSTOTIC BONES, not strictly vertebrates.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:33:10',16,'2025-04-29 02:21:03'),(23480,4150,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Vertere</em></strong> (L. v.), classically, <em>“to twist, bend, turn”</em>;</p><p>Metaphor for the action of the Vertebral Column</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:33:21',16,'2025-04-29 02:21:14'),(23481,4151,15,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Vertebral</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:33:42',16,'2025-04-29 02:27:14'),(23482,4151,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Articular Processes, </strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">Projections of bone, setting for joints</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:33:49',16,'2025-04-29 02:22:34'),(23483,4151,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Bilateral Pedicles, </strong>Posteriorly projecting from the bodies of Vertebrae give rise to superiorly and inferiorly <strong>Articular Processes</strong>; they provide articulation for the vertebral column forming the Articular Pillar.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:33:58',16,'2025-04-29 02:26:17'),(23484,4151,8,NULL,'<p> <strong><em>Vertere</em></strong> (L. v.), classically, <em>“to twist, bend, turn”</em>; </p><p>Metaphor for the action of the Vertebral Column</p><p>  </p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:34:05',NULL,NULL),(23485,4152,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Vertebral</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:34:26',16,'2025-04-30 00:26:41'),(23486,4152,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Canal,</strong></p><p>Collective formation of Vertebral arch</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:34:31',NULL,NULL),(23487,4152,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">a.k.a., <strong>Spinal Canal</strong>; When the spinal column is in situ the canal is formed by the collective Vertebral Foraminae; houses the Spinal Cord from <strong><em>Foramen Magnum</em></strong> to the <strong><em>Filum Terminalis.</em></strong></p><p><strong> </strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:34:38',16,'2025-04-30 00:26:57'),(23488,4152,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Vertere</em></strong> (L. v.), classically, <em>“to twist, bend, turn”</em>; </p><p>Metaphor for the action of the Vertebral Column</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Canal</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Canales</em></strong>), ditch, watercourse; </p><p>In this case, a channel that houses the Spinal Cord.&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:34:46',NULL,NULL),(23489,4153,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Vertebral</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:07',16,'2025-04-24 02:52:09'),(23490,4153,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Column,</strong></p><p>Classically, temple pillar, support;</p><p>Metaphor for the function of Axial Skeleton</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:11',16,'2025-04-30 00:27:40'),(23491,4153,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">a.k.a., <strong>Spinal Column</strong> consists of: 5 sections: (24 Vertebrae / 26 bones): Cervical (7), Thoracic (12), Lumbar (5), Sacrum (1) and Coccyx (1).</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:18',16,'2025-04-30 00:27:55'),(23492,4153,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Vertere</em></strong> (L. v.), classically, <em>“to twist, bend, turn”</em>;</p><p>Metaphor for the action of the Vertebral Column</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:25',16,'2025-04-30 00:28:15'),(23493,4154,13,NULL,'<p>Upright straight line at 90 degrees to the horizontal line</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:40',NULL,NULL),(23494,4154,8,NULL,'<p>  <strong><em>Vertex</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Vertices</em></strong>), the top</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:51',NULL,NULL),(23495,4154,9,NULL,'<p>  comp., <strong><em><u>Vertices + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Vertices</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p><p>  </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:35:59',NULL,NULL),(23496,4155,14,NULL,'<p><strong>Neurocranium,</strong></p><p>bones of the skull encasing the brain</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:36:16',16,'2025-04-30 00:29:27'),(23497,4155,13,NULL,'<p>Bones of the skull forming the facial structure.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:36:22',NULL,NULL),(23498,4155,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Viscus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Visceres</em></strong>), soft flesh</p><p><strong><em>Kranion </em></strong>/<strong><em>Cranium </em></strong>(Gr. n.), skull</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:36:31',16,'2025-04-30 00:29:43'),(23499,4155,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>VisceroCranium</em></strong>,</p><p>Figuratively, <em>“soft cranium”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Viscero- + Cranium</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Viscero- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Visceres</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Cranium</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:36:42',16,'2025-04-30 00:30:01'),(23500,4155,12,NULL,'<p>VISCERA&nbsp;</p><p>VISCERAL LAYER</p><p>VISCERAL PERICARDIUM&nbsp;</p><p>VISCERAL PERITONEUM</p><p>VISCERAL PLEURA</p><p>VISCOSITY</p><p><br></p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:36:50',NULL,NULL),(23501,4156,13,NULL,'<p>A viscero-cranial bone, foundation of the face that forms the Nasal Septum.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:37:05',16,'2025-04-30 00:30:37');
INSERT INTO `termline` VALUES (23502,4156,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Vomer</em></strong> (L. n.), classically, <em>“plowshare”</em>;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">figuratively, the bone resembles a “<em>plowshare”.</em></p><p>Metaphor for the shape of Vomer.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:37:24',16,'2025-04-30 00:31:13'),(23503,4157,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Xiphoid</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:37:40',16,'2025-04-24 02:55:35'),(23504,4157,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Process, </strong></p><p>prominent projection in bone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:37:45',16,'2025-04-30 00:32:10'),(23505,4157,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The sharp, pointed inferiorly projection, process, of the Sternum</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:37:50',16,'2025-04-30 00:31:59'),(23506,4157,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Xiphus </em></strong>(L. n.), knife;</p><p>Metaphor for the pointed tip of sternum</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:37:59',16,'2025-04-30 00:32:36'),(23507,4157,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Xiphoid</em></strong>,</p><p>simile, “<em>knife-like”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Xiph- + -oid</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Xiph- </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Xiphus</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-oid</em></strong> (suffix), forms simile; resembling . . .</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:38:06',16,'2025-04-30 00:32:48'),(23508,4158,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Xiphosternal</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:38:24',16,'2025-04-24 02:55:54'),(23509,4158,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Joint</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:38:29',16,'2025-04-30 00:33:43'),(23510,4158,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The junction where the Xiphoid process articulates with the inferior end of the body of the Sternum.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:38:35',16,'2025-04-30 00:33:33'),(23511,4158,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Xiphus </em></strong>(L. n.), knife;</p><p>Metaphor for the pointed tip of sternum</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Sternum</em></strong>, (plu., <strong><em>Sterna</em></strong>), classically, “breastplate”, breastbone</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:38:50',16,'2025-04-30 00:33:58'),(23512,4158,9,NULL,'<p>  comp., <strong><em><u>Xipho- + Sterna + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Xiphus</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Sterna</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p><p>  </p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:39:00',NULL,NULL),(23513,4159,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><span style=\"background-color: white;\">paired, matched</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:39:24',16,'2025-04-30 00:34:39'),(23514,4159,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Zygon </em></strong>(Gr. n.), yoke, partner</p><p><strong><em>Zygos </em></strong>(Gr. adj.),<strong><em> </em></strong>joined, paired</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:39:39',16,'2025-04-30 00:34:51'),(23515,4159,12,NULL,'<p>ZYGOTE – REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM</p><p>ZYGOMATICUS (MAJOR M.) </p><p>ZYGOMATICUS (MINOR M.) </p><p>ZYGOPOPHYSEAL (JOINT)</p><p>AZYGOUS (VEINS)&nbsp;</p><p>HEMIAZYGOUS (ACCESORY VEIN)</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:39:46',NULL,NULL),(23516,4160,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The <strong><em>Zygomaticus Bone </em></strong>fuses with the <strong><em>Zygomatic</em></strong> <strong><em>Process</em></strong> of Temporal Bone forming the <strong><em>Zygomatic Arch</em></strong>, the \"prominent cheek bone\"</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:41:02',16,'2025-04-30 00:36:00'),(23517,4160,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Zygoma </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Zygomata</em></strong>), yoke, pair</p>',2,0,NUL