p;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:42:39',16,'2025-04-30 00:37:04'),(23526,4161,12,NULL,'<p>  ZYGOTE – REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM</p><p>ZYGOMATICUS (MAJOR M.) </p><p>ZYGOMATICUS (MINOR M.) </p><p>ZYGOPOPHYSEAL (JOINT)</p><p>AZYGOUS (VEINS)&nbsp;</p><p>HEMIAZYGOUS (ACCESORY VEIN)</p><p>  </p>',8,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:42:47',NULL,NULL),(23527,4162,15,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Zygopophyseal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:43:14',16,'2025-04-30 00:38:02'),(23528,4162,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Process, </strong></p><p>prominent projection in bone</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:43:21',16,'2025-04-30 00:38:14'),(23529,4162,13,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">a.k.a., <strong>Pedicles;</strong> posterior bilateral processes of vertebral bodies that give rise to the superior-inferior Articular Processes, the Spinal Laminae, the Posterior Arches, and the Spinous Processes.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:43:28',16,'2025-04-30 00:38:27'),(23530,4162,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Zygos </em></strong>(Gr. adj.),<strong><em> </em></strong>joined, paired</p><p><strong><em>Physis </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Physes</em></strong>), body</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:43:36',16,'2025-04-30 00:38:39'),(23531,4162,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em><u>ZygopoPhyseal</u></em></strong>,</p><p>literally, <em>“paired bodies”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Zygo- + Physe- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Zygos </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Physes</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al </em></strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:43:43',16,'2025-04-30 00:38:56'),(23532,4162,12,NULL,'<p>ZYGOTE – REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM</p><p>ZYGOMATICUS (MAJOR M.)&nbsp;</p><p>ZYGOMATICUS (MINOR M.)&nbsp;</p><p>ZYGOPOPHYSEAL (JOINT)</p><p>AZYGOUS (VEINS)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>HEMIAZYGOUS (ACCESORY VEIN)</p><p><br></p>',8,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 14:43:52',NULL,NULL),(23533,3417,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Adrenal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 22:58:42',NULL,NULL),(23534,3417,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Gland,</strong></p><p>produces hormones, digestive juices, sexual fluid, exudates</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 22:59:24',NULL,NULL),(23535,3417,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a <strong>Suprenal Gland</strong>; glands superimposed on the kidneys; excrete several hormones influencing water homeostasis and the Autonomic Nervous System</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:00:42',NULL,NULL),(23536,3417,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Ad</strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at</p><p><strong>Ren</strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:01:36',NULL,NULL),(23537,3417,9,NULL,'<p><strong>AdRenal</strong></p><p>figuratively, <em>\"gland above the kidney\"</em></p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong>Ad + Ren + Al</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ad</strong></li><li><strong>Ren</strong></li><li><strong>-al </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</li></ul>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:02:55',NULL,NULL),(23538,3418,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Adrenal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:03:19',NULL,NULL),(23539,3418,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Medullary Mechanism</strong></p><p>produce hormones for sympathetic influence, distinct from Cortical</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:03:33',NULL,NULL),(23540,3418,13,NULL,'<p>Adrenal Medulla releases Epinephrine and Norepinephrine during high Sympathetic stimulation to the heart and blood vessels.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:03:40',NULL,NULL),(23541,3418,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:03:46',NULL,NULL),(23542,3418,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenal</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Figuratively, “</em></strong><em>gland above the kidney</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ad- + Ren + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ren</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:03:57',NULL,NULL),(23543,3419,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Epinephrine</strong>; an Adrenergic Hormone, hormone produced by the Adrenal Gland </p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">(precursor: Noreadrenaline); trigger Sympathetic Action/mode effect on Cardiovascular system, </p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">liver and adipocytes; raises heart-beat, increased blood flow to muscles, more glucose into circulation.</p><p><br></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:04:16',NULL,NULL),(23544,3419,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:04:21',NULL,NULL),(23545,3419,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenaline</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, hormone from “gland above the kidney</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ad- + Ren + -al + -ine</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ren</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-alis</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ine </em></strong>(suffix), denotes basic chemical substance</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:04:37',NULL,NULL),(23546,3420,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Adrenergic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:05:56',NULL,NULL),(23547,3420,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Hormones,</strong></p><p>Horman (Gr. v.), to stimulate</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:03',NULL,NULL),(23548,3420,13,NULL,'<p>Collective term for Epinephrine and Norepinephrine, stimulant hormones from Adrenal Gland that influence the Sympathetic Autonomic Nervous System.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:09',NULL,NULL),(23549,3420,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, towards, at<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney </p><p><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Ergones</em></strong>), work</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:16',NULL,NULL),(23550,3420,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AdRenergic</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “energy by the Adrenal Gland”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Ad</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>Ren</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-erg-</u></em></strong><u> + </u><strong><em><u>-icus</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ad</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ren</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-erg-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-icus</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:26',NULL,NULL),(23551,3421,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Afferent</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:44',NULL,NULL),(23552,3421,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Arteriole,</strong></p><p>smallest diameter artery, larger than Capillary</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:51',NULL,NULL),(23553,3421,13,NULL,'<p>Arteriole that enters the Renal Corpuscle, the Bowman’s Capsule, for filtering the blood through the Glomerular network</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-08 23:06:59',NULL,NULL),(23554,3421,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong> (L. prep.), to, at, towards</p><p>