lices from several Renal Pyramids combine into Major Calices, and merge together as the Renal Pelvis&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:50:42',NULL,NULL),(23823,3520,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Majoris</em></strong>, greater; </p><p>comparative of<strong><em> Magnus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), great</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:50:48',NULL,NULL),(23824,3524,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Medullary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:51:28',NULL,NULL),(23825,3524,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Concentration Gradient,</strong></p><p>differences of amount of Solute between 2 compartment<strong>s</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:51:36',NULL,NULL),(23826,3524,13,NULL,'<p>Concentrating urine (achieved by re-absorption of H2O from renal filtrate) occurs deeper into the Renal Medulla Interstitial Capillaries where Concentration of Solutes increases from 300 mOsm/kg in the Cortex to 1200 mOsm/kg Osmotic Pressure at the Apex of the Renal Pyramids.</p><p>FYI:&nbsp;GRADIENT, difference in concentration of solutes between compartments separated by semi-permeable </p><p>membrane; H2O gravitates to higher concentration.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:51:43',NULL,NULL),(23827,3524,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullus, -a, -um </em></strong>(L. adj.), small central part</p><p>Diminutive form of <strong><em>Medius</em></strong> (L. adj.), center</p><p>The <em>“small middle”</em> portion</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:51:49',NULL,NULL),(23828,3524,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullary,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “function of the small middle.”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Medulla + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Medulla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ary</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:51:59',NULL,NULL),(23829,3525,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Medullary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 00:52:29',NULL,NULL),(