) X (Concentration of Solutes in Urine) <strong>÷ </strong>(Concentration of Solutes in Plasma)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:03:13',NULL,NULL),(23886,3547,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Plasma</em> </strong>(Gr. n.), classical, something molded, formed</p><p>metaphorically, “<em>formed elements</em>” in the blood</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:03:19',NULL,NULL),(23887,3549,13,NULL,'<p>The Visceral layer of Bowman’s Capsule is made up of cells with <em>“feet”</em> processes (more like tentacles) that <em>“wrap around”</em> the Glomerular Capillaries forming Filtration Slits.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:03:49',NULL,NULL),(23888,3549,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pous / Pos </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Podos</em></strong>), foot </p><p><strong><em>Cytos / Kytos </em></strong>(Gr. n.), cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:03:54',NULL,NULL),(23889,3549,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Podocyte</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “feet cells</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Podo- + -cyte</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Podos</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cytos&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:04:02',NULL,NULL),(23890,3551,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Proximal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:04:29',NULL,NULL),(23891,3551,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Convoluted,</strong></p><p>loops are turned, twisted and bent</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:04:37',NULL,NULL),(23892,3551,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Proximal Tubule</strong>. Histologically originates from the Parietal Layer of the Bowman’s Capsule; the tubule turns, twists and bends before it becomes the Descending Limb; then becomes the distal</p><p>part of the Loop of Henle.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:04:43',NULL,NULL),(23893,3551,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Proximus, -a, -um</em></strong>, nearest</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:04:48',NULL,NULL),(23894,3554,13,NULL,'<p>Most of the H2O and useful Solutes are re-absorbed by various forces of Diffusion, Facilitated Diffusion, Transport, Co-transport and Reabsorption by Osmotic pressure, after waste products and excess Solutes are sifted out&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:05:31',NULL,NULL),(23895,3554,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Absorbare </em></strong>(v.), to suck<strong><em>; </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Absorptum </em></strong>(past part.), sucked up;&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:05:39',NULL,NULL),(23896,3554,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ReAbsorption</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically</em><strong><em>, </em></strong><em>“sucking back”</em> of H2O</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Absorpt- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Absorptum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-io(nes)</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:05:49',NULL,NULL),(23897,3558,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Renal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:06:27',NULL,NULL),(23898,3558,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Arteries,</strong></p><p><strong>(see brief definition)</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:06:33',NULL,NULL),(23899,3558,13,NULL,'<p>Originate directly from the Abdominal Aorta and enters the kidney through the Hilum into </p><p>the Renal Sinus.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:06:39',NULL,NULL),(23900,3558,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ren</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Renes</em></strong>), the kidney&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:06:51',NULL,NULL),(23901,3558,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Ren + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ren</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<s