rong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:27:40',NULL,NULL),(24007,3590,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Tubular</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:27:56',NULL,NULL),(24008,3590,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Secretion,</strong></p><p>Filtrate to urine</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:28:03',NULL,NULL),(24009,3590,13,NULL,'<p>Excess bi-products of Metabolism, drugs, foreign body, foreign molecules are moved into the Nephron by Passive and Active Transport for urination.&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:28:10',NULL,NULL),(24010,3590,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tubulus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Tubuli</em></strong>), figuratively, <em>“small tube”</em></p><p>diminutive of<strong><em> Tubus</em></strong> (L. n.), tube, pipe</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:28:20',NULL,NULL),(24011,3590,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Tubul- + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Tubulus </em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ar</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:28:47',NULL,NULL),(24012,3591,13,NULL,'<p>A molecular solute, bi-product of protein Metabolism; exerts the strongest Osmolality in the Renal Medulla due to the high Permeability to Urea in the Descending Limbs and Collecting Ducts&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:29:03',NULL,NULL),(24013,3591,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Urea </em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em> Ouron</em></strong>, urine), biproduct of protein </p><p>metabolism in urine&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:29:09',NULL,NULL),(24014,3592,13,NULL,'<p>The Renal Pelvis funnels the urine through the Ureter originating from the Hilum of the kidneys to the Urinary Bladder.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:29:24',NULL,NULL),(24015,3592,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Oureter</em></strong> (Gr. n.,), urinary duct of the kidneys </p><p>to the bladder</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:29:29',NULL,NULL),(24016,3593,13,NULL,'<p><strong>#1&nbsp;</strong>Duct for passage of urine from the Bladder to the outside (short distance on females).</p><p><strong>#2 </strong>The Urinary Bladder to the orifice of the Glans Penis (finally, to the outside world): combined length is approximately 20 cm long composed of Prostatic Urethra, Membranous Urethra, Spongy Urethra, enclosed by Corpus Spongiosum.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:29:56',NULL,NULL),(24017,3593,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ourethra</em></strong> (coined by Hippocrates), urethra</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:30:01',NULL,NULL),(24018,3598,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Urethral</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:31:06',NULL,NULL),(24019,3598,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Glands,</strong></p><p>(see definition)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:31:13',NULL,NULL),(24020,3598,13,NULL,'<p>Small glands in the urethra secrete mucus into the Urethra during sexual excitement</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:31:18',NULL,NULL),(24021,3598,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ourethra</em></strong> (coined by Hippocrates), urethra</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:31:24',NULL,NULL),(24022,3602,13,NULL,'<p>Approximately, 1% of the Glomerular Filtrate is collected in the Urinary Bladder and excreted.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:32:09',NULL,NULL),(24023,3602,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ouron</em></strong> (Gr. n.), urine</p><p><strong><em>Ourein </em></strong>(Gr. v.), to urinate<strong><em> </em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:32:16',NULL,NULL),(24024,3603,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Urinary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:34:31',NULL,NULL),(24025,3603,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Bladder,</strong></p><p>Urine storage</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:34:38',NULL,NULL),(24026,3603,13,NULL,'<p>Muscular container for storage of Urine before excreting out; located in the anterior Pelvic Basin</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 01:34:45',NULL,NULL),(24027,3603,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ouron</em></strong> (Gr. n.), urine</p><p><strong><em>