,16,'2025-01-09 04:13:06',NULL,NULL),(24316,2921,13,NULL,'<p>Inherited disease affecting multiple organs, including the alveoli in the lungs; the lung secretions are absent preventing gas diffusion and movement of Cilia, causing lung infections due to inability to expel bacteria and foreign body.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:13:11',NULL,NULL),(24317,2921,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Cystis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cystes</em></strong>), bladder, blister<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:13:17',NULL,NULL),(24318,2922,13,NULL,'<p>The total Atmospheric pressure is the sum total of every Partial Pressure contributed by each gas in the atmosphere. Atmospheric Pressure at sea level = 760mm Hg.; the pressure exerted by a component of the air, ex., Oxygen is 21% of total air. Partial Pressure of Oxygen is 760 X 21% = 159 mm Hg.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:13:42',NULL,NULL),(24319,2922,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Dalton, John </strong>(1766 – 1844), English Physicist/Chemist; </p><p>Expounded Atmospheric Pressure is summed up total of all partial </p><p>Pressure of all gases in the atmosphere</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:13:48',NULL,NULL),(24320,2923,13,NULL,'<p>Blood infused with O2 from the lungs is circulated for release into the tissues from the Capillary bed via concentration gradient difference, and replaced with Deoxygenated Blood saturated with CO2 (in place of oxygen).</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:03',NULL,NULL),(24321,2923,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>De </em></strong>(L. prep.), down from, off</p><p><strong><em>Oxygen</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:08',NULL,NULL),(24322,2923,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DeOxygen</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “off Oxygen”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.</em><strong><em>, <u>De- + Oxygen</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;De </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Oxygen&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:15',NULL,NULL),(24323,2924,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Diaphragmatic</strong>, adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:33',NULL,NULL),(24324,2924,13,NULL,'<p>The double-domed principal muscle of inspiration separates the Thoracic Cavity from the Abdominal cavity; relaxation of the Diaphragm contributes to 2/3 of the increase in Thoracic Volume needed during inspiration.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:39',NULL,NULL),(24325,2924,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Di-</em></strong> (prefix), two parts</p><p><strong><em>Phragma </em></strong>(Gr. n.), partition, hedge, fence&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:45',NULL,NULL),(24326,2924,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DiPhragma,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “double partition”</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Di- + Phragma</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Di-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Phragma </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-tic, </em></strong>forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:14:54',NULL,NULL),(24327,2926,13,NULL,'<p>During capillary exchange nutrients and O2 in the blood are downloaded (diffused) into the interstitial; in exchange CO2 and waste products in the capillary is “picked-up” by the blood via Concentration Gradient, Osmotic pressure and Selective Permeability.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:27:16',NULL,NULL),(24328,2926,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diffidere </em></strong>(L. v.), to spread out, pour forth;<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Diffusum </em></strong>(past part.), poured around</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:27:25',NULL,NULL),(24329,2926,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diffusion</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, “distribute by</em> <em>pouring around</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Diffus- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Diffusum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:27:32',NULL,NULL),(24330,2927,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Diffusion</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:32:48',NULL,NULL),(24331,2927,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Co-efficient</strong></p><p>influencing co-factors</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:32:58',NULL,NULL),(24332,2927,13,NULL,'<p>The measure of gas to diffuse through liquid or the interstitia is determined by the gas’ solubility and its molecular weight and mass.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:33:05',NULL,NULL),(24333,2927,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diffidere </em></strong>(L. v.), to spread out, pour forth;<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Diffusum </em></strong>(past part.), poured around<strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:33:13',NULL,NULL),(24334,2927,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diffusion</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>distribute by</em> <em>pouring around</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Diffus- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Diffusum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:33:23',NULL,NULL),(24335,2928,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Diffusion</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:33:41',NULL,NULL),(24336,2928,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Gases Through Liquids,</strong></p><p>oxygen, CO2, nitrogen, etc.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:33:57',NULL,NULL),(24337,2928,13,NULL,'<p>HENRY\'S LAW: Gases dissolve when expose to liquid (H2O); concentration of such gas solute depends on the gas’s Partial Pressure and its Solubility Coefficient.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:34:03',NULL,NULL),(24338,2928,8,NULL,'<p>