trong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Diffusum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:35:15',NULL,NULL),(24345,2930,13,NULL,'<p>Caused by Corynebacterium Diptheriae; infects the throat and coats the airway with false membrane totally blocking the airway.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:35:34',NULL,NULL),(24346,2930,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Dipther </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Dipthera</em></strong>), membrane, skin, covering</p><p><br></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:35:39',NULL,NULL),(24347,2930,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Diptheria,</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “coated throat”</em></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp., <strong><em><u>Dipther + -ia</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Dipther </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ia </em></strong>(suffix), denotes pathology (ex., Dementia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:35:48',NULL,NULL),(24348,2933,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Dorsal / Dorsalis,</strong> adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:36:21',NULL,NULL),(24349,2933,13,NULL,'<p>The back of humans or animal</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:36:27',NULL,NULL),(24350,2933,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dorsum </em></strong>(plu.,<strong><em> Dorsi</em></strong>), backside of humans or animals</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:36:32',NULL,NULL),(24351,2934,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Dorsal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:36:56',NULL,NULL),(24352,2934,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Respiratory Group,</strong></p><p>Concentrated in Medulla Oblongata</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-09 04:37:03',NULL,NULL),(24353,2934,13,NULL,'<p>Dorsal half of the Medullary Respiratory center (the other half is Ventral Respiratory Groups) located in the Medulla Oblongata, in communication with each oth