i</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-in</em></strong> (suffix), denotes protein, hormone (Insulin)</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:51:20',NULL,NULL),(24443,2963,13,NULL,'<p>Maintenance of stability of blood volume and blood pressure within normal limits in the closed blood circulatory system by an automatic feedback system of receptors.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:51:51',NULL,NULL),(24444,2963,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Haima </em></strong>(Gr. n.), blood</p><p><strong><em>Stasis</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Stases</em></strong>), stable condition,<strong><em> </em></strong>standing still</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:51:56',NULL,NULL),(24445,2963,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HemoStasis,</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically,</em><strong><em> “</em></strong><em>blood stability</em>”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp., <strong><em><u>Hemo- + Stasis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hemo-</em></strong><em> derived from </em><strong><em>Haima</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Stasis</em></strong> </p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:52:07',NULL,NULL),(24446,2965,13,NULL,'<p>Stretch receptors in the walls of Bronchi and Bronchioles limit over-inflation of the lungs.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:52:32',NULL,NULL),(24447,2965,8,NULL,'<p>Named after Joseph Breuer and Ewald Hering</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:52:38',NULL,NULL),(24448,2966,13,NULL,'<p>The <em>“stem of the Lungs”</em> where the Primary Bronchus, Blood Vessels, Nerves, and Lymphatic Vessels enter and exit the lungs</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:53:41',NULL,NULL),(24449,2966,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hilum</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Hila</em></strong>), a small trifle, unimportant thing</p><p>(Imagery cannot be explained.)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:53:47',NULL,NULL),(24450,2967,13,NULL,'<p>Caused by <u>Histoplasma Capsulatum</u>, fungal spores that enter the lungs from the environment; characterized by anemia, fever, emaciation</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:54:02',NULL,NULL),(24451,2967,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Histoplasma Capsulatum</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:54:07',NULL,NULL),(24452,2968,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Hyaline</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:54:23',NULL,NULL),(24453,2968,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Membrane Disease</strong></p><p>a.k.a., sudden infant death</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:54:29',NULL,NULL),(24454,2968,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Respiiratory Distress Syndrome</strong>; common in premature births of less than 7 months gestation; the surfactants at this stage in the alveolar surfaces are not adequately developed. Immature surfactant cannot penetrate Hyaline Membrane.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:54:36',NULL,NULL),(24455,2968,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hyalinus, -a, -um</em></strong> (L. adj.), transparent </p><p><strong><em>Hyalus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Hyali</em></strong>), glass, crystal&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:54:42',NULL,NULL),(24456,2969,13,NULL,'<p>A condition in Ventilation causing greater than normal level of CO2 in the blood&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:55:09',NULL,NULL),(24457,2969,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hyper-</em></strong> (Gr. prefix), over the top, excessive, above&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Kapnos</em></strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> (Gr. n.)&nbsp;smoke</span></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:55:16',NULL,NULL),(24458,2969,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hyper</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Kapn</em></strong><strong><em>ia</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “too much smoke inhaled”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Hyper- + </u></em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em><u>Kapnos</u></em></strong><strong><em><u> + -ia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hyper</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong><strong style=\"background-color: white;\"><em>Kapnos</em></strong><span style=\"background-color: white;\"> </span></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ia</em></strong> (suffix), denotes condition, state (Absentia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:55:25',NULL,NULL),(24459,2970,13,NULL,'<p>A condition in Ventilation with a decrease in O2 levels below normal values; when Arterial Partial Pressure of O2 falls below 50% it begins to trigger increased rate and depth of breathing.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:55:40',NULL,NULL),(24460,2970,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hypo</em></strong> (Gr. prep.), under, below, deficient</p><p><strong><em>-ox-</em></strong>,<strong> </strong>oxygen<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:55:48',NULL,NULL),(24461,2970,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Hypooxia</em></strong>,<strong> </strong></p><p><em>literally, “low O2 condition”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Hypo + -ox- + -ia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Hypo</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ox- </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ia</em></strong> (suffix), denotes state, condition (Absentia)</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:55:56',NULL,NULL),(24462,2971,13,NULL,'<p>Viral infection of the respiratory System, characterized by cold-like symptoms, chills, high fever, headaches, muscle aches.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:56:14',NULL,NULL),(24463,2971,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Influentia</em></strong>, traditionally, <em>\"visitation”</em> (of the stars), on astral or occult influence; </p><p>poetically, <em>\"power from the stars acting through the character or destiny of men”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:56:22',NULL,NULL),(24464,2973,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Inspiratory</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:56:59',NULL,NULL),(24465,2973,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Capacity,</strong></p><p>available space</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:57:05',NULL,NULL),(24466,2973,13,NULL,'<p>Tidal Volume + Inspiratory Reserve Volume = maximum air that can be inspired after a normal inspiration</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:57:10',NULL,NULL),(24467,2973,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>En </em></strong>(L. prep.), in, into</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breathe</p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed;&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:57:22',NULL,NULL),(24468,2973,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em><u>EnSpiratory</u></em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “function of breathing in”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong> <em><u>En + Spirat- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;En</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spiratum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location; Eng., -ory</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:57:34',NULL,NULL),(24469,2974,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Inspiratory</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:57:52',NULL,NULL),(24470,2974,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Reserved Volume,</strong></p><p>deeper inspiration after normal inspiration</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:57:59',NULL,NULL),(24471,2974,13,NULL,'<p>Amount of air forcefully inhaled after Tidal Volume is inhaled</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:58:05',NULL,NULL),(24472,2974,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>En </em></strong>(L. prep.), in, into</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breathe</p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed;&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:58:13',NULL,NULL),(24473,2974,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em><u>EnSpiratory</u></em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “function of breathing in”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong> <em><u>En + Spirat- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;En</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spiratum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/location; Eng., -ory</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:58:22',NULL,NULL),(24474,2975,13,NULL,'<p>Made up of the external shell of 9 Cartilages: Thyroid Cartilage, Cricoid Cartilage, Epiglottis, Arytenoid Cartilage, Corniculate Cartilage, Cuneiform Cartilage, Vestibular Folds, Vocal Folds, and Glottis.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:58:38',NULL,NULL),(24475,2975,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>&nbsp;Larynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Larynges</em></strong>t), classically, throat, voice box<u> </u></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:58:46',NULL,NULL),(24476,2976,13,NULL,'<p>Inflammation of the Larynx</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:59:03',NULL,NULL),(24477,2976,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Larynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Larynges</em></strong>), the throat, voice box<u> </u></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:59:13',NULL,NULL),(24478,2976,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Laryng- + -itis</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Larynges</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-itis </em></strong>(suffix), denotes inflammation</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 05:59:19',NULL,NULL),(24479,2977,13,NULL,'<p>Inferior Pharynx from the tip of the Epiglottis to the Esophagus posterior to the Larynx.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:03:34',NULL,NULL),(24480,2977,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Larynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Larynges</em></strong>), the throat, voice box<u> </u></p><p><strong><em>Pharynx</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Pharynges</em></strong>), throat</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:03:43',NULL,NULL),(24481,2977,9,NULL,'<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;comp., <strong><em><u>Laryngo- + Pharynx</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Larynges</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pharynx</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:03:55',NULL,NULL),(24482,2978,13,NULL,'<p>The Limbic System is the primordial brain, functioning for basic survival, memory, sex, hunger, emotions; located in the middle of Cerebrum bordering around the Diencephalon.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:04:16',NULL,NULL),(24483,2978,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Limbus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Limbi</em></strong>), classical, the edge, or borderline</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:04:22',NULL,NULL),(24484,2978,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Limbicus</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “border” </em>(between instinct and will &amp; reason)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Limbi + -ic</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: windowtext;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><strong><em>Limbus</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:04:36',NULL,NULL),(24485,2979,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Limbic System</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:04:55',NULL,NULL),(24486,2979,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Ventilation Control,</strong></p><p>rate and depth of breathing</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:05:02',NULL,NULL),(24487,2979,13,NULL,'<p>Strong emotions, anger, flight and fight responses prompted by the Limbic System override the Medullary Center of Rhythmic Ventilation.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:05:08',NULL,NULL),(24488,2979,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Limbus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Limbi</em></strong>), classical, the edge, or borderline</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:05:14',NULL,NULL),(24489,2979,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Limbicus</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “border” </em>(between instinct and will &amp; reason)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>comp.,<strong><em> <u>Limbi + -icus</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: windowtext;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><strong><em>Limbus</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ic</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.; ability&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:05:27',NULL,NULL),(24490,2981,13,NULL,'<p>Segments of the lungs separated by Fissures; 3 lobes in the right lung, 2 in the left; each lobe is supplied by independent Secondary bronchus and separate blood supply</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:07:00',NULL,NULL),(24491,2981,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lobus</em></strong> (plu.,<strong><em> Lobi</em></strong>), hull, husk, pod</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:07:05',NULL,NULL),(24492,2982,13,NULL,'<p>Subdivisions of Bronchopulmonary Segments separated by partial connective tissue walls, supplied by bronchioles</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:07:23',NULL,NULL),(24493,2982,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Lobulus</em></strong>, classically, <em>“small husk, pod”</em></p><p>diminutive of <strong><em>Lobus</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:07:28',NULL,NULL),(24494,2982,12,NULL,'<p><strong>LOBE</strong>, CORTICAL -NERVOUS SYSTEM</p><p><strong>LOBULES</strong>, CEREBELLAR – NERVOUS SYSTEM</p>',6,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:07:44',NULL,NULL),(24495,2983,13,NULL,'<p>Principal organ of Respiration, the largest organ of the body, triangular in shape the base is attached to the Diaphragm, the principal muscle of Respiration.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:08:05',NULL,NULL),(24496,2984,13,NULL,'<p>The lungs recoil due to resistance to inflation (as if to inflate a ballon); it is caused by the elastic fibers in the Alveolar walls and the surface tension of the watery film lining the Alveoli.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 06:08:22',NULL,NULL),(24497,2986,13,NULL,'<p>Tunnel-like passageway under each Concha, air passage for warming the air before reaching the lungs. Also refers to 