(24655,3053,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Residua + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Residua</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:11:58',NULL,NULL),(24657,3054,15,NULL,'<p>The total functions of Respiratory System: <strong>Ventilation</strong>, the flow of air in and out of the lungs; <strong>Diffusion</strong> gas exchange in the Alveolar Surfaces; <strong>Transport</strong> of O2 to the tissues; <strong>Exchange</strong> of O2/CO2 within the tissue Capillaries; <strong>Expiration</strong> of CO2 back to the lungs for exhalation.</p><p>FYI:&nbsp;The term also refers to Cellular Metabolism of Glucose for ATP production.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:12:34',NULL,NULL),(24658,3054,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:12:43',NULL,NULL),(24659,3054,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -io</u>n</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ion</em></strong> (suffix), forms noun of action</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:12:52',NULL,NULL),(24660,3055,13,NULL,'<p>Originate from the divisions (branches of bronchial tree) and further 7 sub-sub-divisions ending at Terminal Bronchioles, the thinnest Respiratory Bronchioles, where the Alveoli are attached.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:13:12',NULL,NULL),(24661,3055,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:13:19',NULL,NULL),(24662,3055,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:13:26',NULL,NULL),(24663,3056,13,NULL,'<p>In the Medulla Oblongata, two on the Dorsal aspect and two on the Ventral aspect; they are paired for mutual communications amongst the 4 elongated Nuclei for symmetrical breathing.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:13:45',NULL,NULL),(24664,3056,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:13:55',NULL,NULL),(24665,3056,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:14:01',NULL,NULL),(24666,3057,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Hyaline Membrane Disease</strong>;<em> </em>Common in premature births of less than 7 months gestation since surfactants in the Alveoli are not adequately developed</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:14:17',NULL,NULL),(24667,3057,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:14:26',NULL,NULL),(24668,3057,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:14:33',NULL,NULL),(24669,3058,13,NULL,'<p>Lining of Pulmonary Capillaries in the Alveoli where Gas Exchange takes place; Respiratory Bronchioles and Alveolar ducts have same but limited capabilities</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:14:50',NULL,NULL),(24670,3058,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:14:58',NULL,NULL),(24671,3058,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:15:05',NULL,NULL),(24672,3059,13,NULL,'<p>Thickening of the Alveolar respiratory membrane, mainly caused by Pulmonary Edema, decreases the rate of gas exchange between blood and gas in the Alveoli; other causes: TB, Silicosis, Pneumonia, smoking</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:15:25',NULL,NULL),(24673,3059,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:15:35',NULL,NULL),(24674,3059,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:15:42',NULL,NULL),(24675,3060,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., Respiratory Frequency; Number of normal breathing per minute; Tidal Capacity, approx. 12 breaths)&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:16:01',NULL,NULL),(24676,3060,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:16:09',NULL,NULL),(24677,3060,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:16:16',NULL,NULL),(24678,3061,13,NULL,'<p>Gas exchange occur from the Terminal bronchioles to the Alveoli</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:16:33',NULL,NULL),(24679,3061,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Re-</em></strong> (L. prefix), again, repeatedly</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breath; </p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:16:40',NULL,NULL),(24680,3061,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Re- + Spirat- + -ory</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Re-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Spiratum</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-orium</em></strong> (suffix), denotes function/site; Eng., -ory</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:16:49',NULL,NULL),(24681,3064,13,NULL,'<p>Regular pattern of breathing with measurable regularity</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:17:18',NULL,NULL),(24682,3064,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Rhythmus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Rhythmi</em></strong>), symmetrical flowing motion; </p><p><em>\"measured movement”</em>;</p><p>Metaphor for regularly paced breathing</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:17:26',NULL,NULL),(24683,3065,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Rhythmic</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:17:49',NULL,NULL),(24684,3065,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pulse,</strong></p><p>Waves of blood flow from the aorta <em>“echoing”</em> in the arteries</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:17:56',NULL,NULL),(24685,3065,13,NULL,'<p>Regular beating of the heart palpable at several points in the body where the arterial pulse is palpable; </p><p>Radial pulse is the commonest.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:18:01',NULL,NULL),(24686,3065,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Rhythmus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Rhythmi</em></strong>), symmetrical flowing motion; </p><p><em>\"measured movement”</em>;</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>Metaphor for regularly paced heart beat</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:18:07',NULL,NULL),(24687,3066,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Rhythmic&nbsp;</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:18:29',NULL,NULL),(24688,3066,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Ventilation,</strong></p><p>Atmospheric air filling-emptying the Alveoli&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:18:35',NULL,NULL),(24689,3066,13,NULL,'<p>Rhythmic Ventilation is automatically controlled by neurons in the Medulla Oblongata that stimulate the muscles </p><p>of Respiration causing air to inflow and outflow in the Alveoli.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:18:41',NULL,NULL),(24690,3066,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Rhythmus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Rhythmi</em></strong>), symmetrical flowing motion; </p><p><em>\"measured movement”</em></p><p>Metaphor for regularly paced breathing</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:18:50',NULL,NULL),(24691,3067,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., <strong>Hilum</strong>; Primary bronchus, Blood Vessels, Nerves, and Lymphatic Vessels enter or exit through the lungs.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:19:09',NULL,NULL),(24692,3067,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Root</strong> (Eng. n.), a sense of anchor, source of sustenance<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:19:15',NULL,NULL),(24693,3072,13,NULL,'<p>Cavernous, “large empty space”, within a bone or an enlarged junction of blood vessels merging, or a large blood vessels branching into two</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:20:05',NULL,NULL),(24694,3072,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sinus </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Sini</em></strong>), an empty bowl, empty curved surface </p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:20:11',NULL,NULL),(24695,3074,13,NULL,'<p>Posterior portion of the Palate; connective tissue separation between the Nasopharynx and the Oropharynx</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:20:41',NULL,NULL),(24696,3075,13,NULL,'<p>Measurement by Spirometer of volumes of air Inspired and Expired&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:26:43',NULL,NULL),(24697,3075,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Spirare</em></strong> (v.), to breathe<strong><em> </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Metrum </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Metra</em></strong>), meter measurement&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:26:51',NULL,NULL),(24698,3075,9,NULL,'<p>comp., <strong><em><u>Spiro- + Metrum</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spirare</em></strong>, </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Metrum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:26:58',NULL,NULL),(24699,3076,13,NULL,'<p>Infection by Streptococcus Pyogenes, characterized by sore throat and high fever.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:27:16',NULL,NULL),(24700,3076,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Streptococcus Pyogenes</em></strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:27:22',NULL,NULL),(24701,3077,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Superficial</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:33:26',NULL,NULL),(24702,3077,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Lymphatic Vessels,</strong></p><p>Filter bacteria infection within the pleura</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:33:34',NULL,NULL),(24703,3077,13,NULL,'<p>Located deep in the Visceral Pleura; they filter and drain lymph from the surface of lungs and the Visceral Pleura.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:33:43',NULL,NULL),(24704,3077,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. prep), above, high </p><p><strong><em>Facies </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Faciei</em></strong>), face</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:33:49',NULL,NULL),(24705,3077,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SuperFacialis</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “above the face”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Super + Faci- + -al</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Super </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Facies</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-al</em> </strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:33:58',NULL,NULL),(24706,3078,13,NULL,'<p>The filmy fluid surface in the Alveolar respiratory surfaces (tension) is caused by the polar H2O molecules bonding to each other, preventing encroachment of air, to be broken down by surfactants to enable exchange of Oxygen-C02</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:34:21',NULL,NULL),(24707,3078,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. prep), above, high </p><p><strong><em>Facies </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Faciei</em></strong>), face</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:34:27',NULL,NULL),(24708,3078,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SuperFaciei</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “above the face”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Super + Faciei</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Super </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Facies</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:34:37',NULL,NULL),(24709,3079,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Surface</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:35:06',NULL,NULL),(24710,3079,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Area of Lungs,</strong></p><p>sum total of alveolar functional surface</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:35:14',NULL,NULL),(24711,3079,13,NULL,'<p>In healthy adults the total surface of Respiratory membrane is approximately 70 sq. m.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:35:21',NULL,NULL),(24712,3079,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. prep), above, high</p><p><strong><em>Facies </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Faciei</em></strong>), a face</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:35:27',NULL,NULL),(24713,3079,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SuperFaciei</em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “above the face”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sur- + Facies</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Super </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Facies&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:35:36',NULL,NULL),(24714,4186,13,NULL,'<p>Lipoprotein excreted by type II Pneumocytes of the Alveolar Epithelium cover the fluid surface; Monomolecular layer disrupt the polar bond of H2O, greatly reducing surface tension.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:36:25',NULL,NULL),(24715,4186,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(prep), above, high</p><p><strong><em>Facies </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Faciei</em></strong>), a face</p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>Agere</strong> (L. v.), to do, act, perform; &nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Actum </em></strong>(past part.), acted on, done&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:36:36',NULL,NULL),(24716,4186,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SurFactActum</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “acting on the surface”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em> <u>Sur- + Fact- + Actum</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Super </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Facies </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Actum&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:36:43',NULL,NULL),(24717,3082,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Terminal</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:37:16',NULL,NULL),(24718,3082,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Bronchioles,</strong></p><p>Smallest of the bronchial branches</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:37:23',NULL,NULL),(24719,3082,13,NULL,'<p>Originate from 7th to 8th generation of Bronchioles giving rise to Alveoli</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:37:28',NULL,NULL),(24720,3082,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Terminus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Termini</em></strong>), limit, end, boundary<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:37:34',NULL,NULL),(24721,3082,12,NULL,'<p><strong>TERMINALIS</strong>, CRISTA – CARDIOVASCULAR SYSTEM</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:37:43',NULL,NULL),(24722,3083,13,NULL,'<p>Originate from further division of the Secondary Bronchi giving rise to bronchioles, further subdividing (branch off) a few more layers to become Terminal Bronchioles</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:38:02',NULL,NULL),(24723,3083,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Tertius, -ia, -ium</em></strong>, one third, third</p><p>Third branching layer of finer bronchioes</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:38:08',NULL,NULL),(24724,3084,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Thoracic,</strong> adj.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:38:26',NULL,NULL),(24725,3084,13,NULL,'<p>The mid-upper back encompassing Vertebral levels T1 to T12; the chest region</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:38:31',NULL,NULL),(24726,3084,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thorax </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thoraces</em></strong>), classically, <em>“chest, breastplate”</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:38:39',NULL,NULL),(24727,3085,13,NULL,'<p>The upper Trunk: includes the Thoracic Vertebrae, Ribs, Costal Cartilages, Sternum, and their associated muscles are involved in inspiration and expiration.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:38:57',NULL,NULL),(24728,3085,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thorax </em></strong>(plu., <strong><em>Thoraces</em></strong>), classically, <em>“chest, breastplate”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:39:03',NULL,NULL),(24729,3086,13,NULL,'<p>Translation:<em> “of the Thorax”</em>; <em>“of the upper back”</em>, Vertebral levels T1 to T12</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:39:21',NULL,NULL),(24730,3086,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thoracis</em></strong>, </p><p>(possessive form of <strong><em>Thorax</em></strong>, classically, <em>“chest, breastplate”</em>)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:39:27',NULL,NULL),(24731,3087,13,NULL,'<p>Something takes effect at a level at which a process or action occurs.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:39:43',NULL,NULL),(24732,3087,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Threshold</strong> (Eng. n.), a level at which something come into effect</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:39:49',NULL,NULL),(24733,3088,13,NULL,'<p>Unpaired cartilage of the Larynx visible and palpable as the Adam’s Apple (other cartilages housing the Larynx and Trachea are paired)</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:40:08',NULL,NULL),(24734,3088,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thyrus</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Thyri</em></strong>), oblong shield<strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p>Metaphor for the shape of the thyroid gland</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 07:40:16',NULL,NULL),(24735,3088,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Thyroid,</em></strong></p><p><em>Simile: resembling “an oblong shield”</em></p><p><em>&n