enting&nbsp;</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:30:10',NULL,NULL),(24818,4193,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cords</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:30:45',NULL,NULL),(24819,4193,7,NULL,'<p><strong>False,</strong></p><p>Once mistaken for vibratory source of sound</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:30:54',NULL,NULL),(24820,4193,13,NULL,'<p>2 parallel cords that close to prevent food and liquid from going into the Larynx during swallowing and prevent air from leaving the lungs when holding breath</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:31:01',NULL,NULL),(24821,4193,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Corda</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cordae</em></strong>), strings of string instrument</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:31:06',NULL,NULL),(24822,4194,15,NULL,'<p><strong>Cords</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:31:41',NULL,NULL),(24823,4194,7,NULL,'<p><strong>True Vocal Folds</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:31:47',NULL,NULL),(24824,4194,13,NULL,'<p>Inferior ligaments of the Larynx lined with mucous membrane provide the main source of sound vibration (the tongue, lips, cheeks and teeth form the words).</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:31:53',NULL,NULL),(24825,4194,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Corda</em></strong> (plu., <strong><em>Cordae</em></strong>), strings of string instrument</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:31:59',NULL,NULL),(24826,4195,13,NULL,'<p><strong>Difference</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:32:56',NULL,NULL),(24827,4195,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pressure and Airflow,</strong></p><p>by force of pressure gradient</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:33:03',NULL,NULL),(24828,4195,13,NULL,'<p>Movement of gas occurs from the higher pressure to the lower pressure by the Physics of Partial Pressure of gases.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:33:10',NULL,NULL),(24829,4195,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Dis-</em></strong> (L. prep.), apart, separate from</p><p><strong><em>Ferre </em></strong>(L. v.), to carry</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:33:19',NULL,NULL),(24830,4195,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>DiFerrencia</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically, “carry apart”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp., </em><strong><em><u>Dis- + Ferre + -encia</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dis-</em></strong> </p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Ferre </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-encia </em></strong>(suffix), denotes process, action; Eng., -ence&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:33:33',NULL,NULL),(24831,4196,13,NULL,'<p>Continuous with the Proximal Tubule, composed of Descending tube, turns upward from a loop and becomes the Ascending tubule; within the kidney this apparatus spans between cortical and medullary osmotic differences for reabsorption of Plasma and formation of urine.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:34:21',NULL,NULL),(24832,4196,8,NULL,'<p><strong>Henle, </strong>Friedrich Gustav Jacob (1809-1885), </p><p>Discoverer (1880-1885); German anatomist, </p><p>Pathologist; pioneer of modern medicine</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:34:29',NULL,NULL),(24833,4197,13,NULL,'<p>The Diaphragm, External Intercostales Muscles, Pectorales Minor, and Scalenes, and Levator Scapulae; the Diaphragm contributes to 2<strong>/</strong>3 of the increase in Thoracic Volume during inspiration.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:35:09',NULL,NULL),(24834,4197,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>En </em></strong>(L. prep.), in, into</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Spirare </em></strong>(L. v.), to breathe;</p><p><strong><em>Spiratum </em></strong>(past part.), breathed&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-10 08:35:17',NULL,NULL),(24835,4197,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em><u>EnSpiration</u></em></strong></p><p><em>Literally, “breathing in”</em></p><p><em>&nbsp;</em></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong> <em><u>En + Spirat- + -ion</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;En</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs