), to turn;</p><p><strong><em>Versum </em></strong>(past part.), turned</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:11:26',NULL,NULL),(25021,2478,9,NULL,'<p><strong>EVersion,</strong> literally, “turning away”</p><p><br></p><p>Compound of:<strong> E- Vers- -ion</strong></p><p>•	<strong>E </strong>derived from <strong>Ex</strong></p><p>•	<strong>Versum</strong></p><p>•	<strong>-ion </strong>suffix: forms noun of action</p><p><br></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:12:09',NULL,NULL),(25022,2479,14,NULL,'<p>RETRACTION</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:12:31',NULL,NULL),(25023,2479,13,NULL,'<p>Lateral deviation of the jaw off mid-line (imagine receiving a left/right hook to the jaw)&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:12:42',NULL,NULL),(25024,2479,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Excurrere</em></strong><em> </em>(L. v.), to run off course;</p><p><strong><em>Excursum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), run off course</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:13:00',NULL,NULL),(25025,2479,9,NULL,'<p><strong>Excursion</strong>, metaphorically, <em>“running off course...”</em></p><p><br></p><p>Compound of: <strong>Excurs- -ion</strong></p><p>•	<strong>Excursum</strong></p><p>•	<strong>-ion</strong> suffix: forms noun of action</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:13:26',16,'2025-01-11 02:13:37'),(25026,2480,14,NULL,'<p>CONTRACTIBILITY</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:14:49',NULL,NULL),(25027,2480,13,NULL,'<p>Property of muscles to be stretchable.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:14:55',NULL,NULL),(25028,2480,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ex</em></strong><em> </em>(L. prep.), away, from, out of</p><p><strong><em>Tendere</em></strong><em> </em>(L. v.), to stretch;</p><p><strong><em>Tensum </em></strong>(past part.), stretched out</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 02:15:21',NULL,NULL),(25029,2480,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ExTensibility</em></strong>, literally, <em>“stretchability”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Ex Tens- -ability</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ex</em></strong></p><