13,NULL,'<p>Lying stomach and face down: In falling forward, what are you <em>“prone”</em> to do? Standing position, elbow flexed at 90-degrees, rotate palms/forearms to face.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:22:22',NULL,NULL),(25150,2521,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pronus, -a, -um</em></strong><em> </em>(L, adj.), stooping forward</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:22:31',NULL,NULL),(25151,2521,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pronation</em></strong><em> </em>figuratively, <em>“inclination, forward lean”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Prona -ation</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Prona</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ation </em></strong><em>suffix: forms noun of action</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:23:00',NULL,NULL),(25152,2522,14,NULL,'<p>SUPINATOR MUSCLE</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:23:17',NULL,NULL),(25153,2522,13,NULL,'<p>Muscle that rotates palm-forearm posteriorly; or inferiorly with flexed elbow. (When you fall forward on your face what happens to your palms/forearms.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:23:23',NULL,NULL),(25154,2522,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pronus, -a, -um </em></strong>tendency, stooping forward</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:23:37',NULL,NULL),(25155,2522,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pronator </em></strong>literally, muscle agent <em>“rotating palm-forearm posteriorly”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of:</em><strong><em> Prona -ator</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Prona</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ato</em></strong><em>r suffix: denotes agent of action</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:24:08',NULL,NULL),(25156,2523,13,NULL,'<p>(QUADRATUS, square)</p><p>Square shaped muscle on the anterior forearm that rotates forearm posteriorly; imagine: unscrewing with a screw driver.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:24:28',NULL,NULL),(25157,2523,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pronus, -a, -um</em></strong><em> </em>(L, adj.), stooping forward</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:24:36',NULL,NULL),(25158,2523,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Pronator</em></strong><em> </em>literally, muscle agent <em>“agent rotating palm-forearm posteriorly”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Prona -ator</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Prona</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ator </em></strong><em>suffix: denotes agent of action</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:25:04',NULL,NULL),(25159,2524,14,NULL,'<p>RETRACTION</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:25:25',NULL,NULL),(25160,2524,13,NULL,'<p>Jutting forward of the jaw.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:25:31',NULL,NULL),(25161,2524,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Protrahaere</em></strong><em> </em>(L. v.), to project forward;</p><p><strong><em>Protractum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), drawn forward</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:25:49',NULL,NULL),(25162,2524,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Protraction </em></strong>figuratively, <em>“jaw-jutting forward”</em></p><p><em> </em></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Protractum -ion</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Protractum </em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion </em></strong><em>suffix: forms noun of action</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:26:24',NULL,NULL),(25163,2525,13,NULL,'<p>Prominent and enlarged parts of bones (ex., Occipital Protuberance).</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:32:48',NULL,NULL),(25164,2525,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Protuberare</em></strong><em> </em>(v.), to protrude;</p><p><strong><em>Protuberans</em></strong><em> </em>(present part.), protruding</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:33:05',NULL,NULL),(25165,2526,14,NULL,'<p>DISTAL</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:33:25',NULL,NULL),(25166,2526,13,NULL,'<p>Closer to the mid-sagittal plane; a reference point is required for comparison (ex., elbow is proximal to the wrist).</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:33:31',NULL,NULL),(25167,2526,8,NULL,'<p