he transverse plane of a reference point.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:47:49',NULL,NULL),(25195,2534,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Superioris</em></strong><em> </em>higher (comparative form)</p><p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. adj.), above, high</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:48:05',NULL,NULL),(25196,2535,13,NULL,'<p>(prefix), above.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:48:21',NULL,NULL),(25197,2535,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Super </em></strong>(L. prep), above, high</p><p><strong><em>Supra-</em></strong><em> </em>(prefix), above</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:48:34',NULL,NULL),(25198,2536,13,NULL,'<p>(BURSA, pocket cushion for tendons)</p><p>Literally, <em>“above the Patella”</em>; “pocket” cushion and lubrication between tendon and bone, usually in large joints; ex., knees, shoulders. (see PATELLA)&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:48:58',NULL,NULL),(25199,2536,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Supra- </em></strong>(prefix), above</p><p><strong><em>Super</em></strong><em> </em>(L. prep), above, high</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:49:11',NULL,NULL),(25200,2537,14,NULL,'<p>PRONATION</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:49:45',NULL,NULL),(25201,2537,13,NULL,'<p><u>Extended Elbow</u>: Rotate of forearm-palm to face anteriorly; Flexed Elbow: rotate forearm-palm superiorly.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:49:51',NULL,NULL),(25202,2537,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Supinare</em></strong><em> </em><u>(L. v.), to lie on one’s back;</u></p><p><strong><em>Supinatum </em></strong><u>(past part.), laid on back</u></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:50:06',NULL,NULL),(25203,2537,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Supination</em></strong><em> “rotate forearm-hand anteriorly to receive... something”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Supinat- -ion</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Supinatum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion </em></strong><em>suffix: forms noun of action</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:50:31',NULL,NULL),(25204,2538,14,NULL,'<p>PRONE</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:50:48',NULL,NULL),(25205,2538,13,NULL,'<p><u>Whole bod</u>y: lying on ones back, palms-forearms facing upward and toes pointing downward; <u>Hand/forearm</u>: elbow flexed 90 degrees; rotate palms/forearms to face superiorly as in driving the screw in</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:50:59',NULL,NULL),(25206,2538,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Sub</em></strong><em> </em><u>(L. prep.), under</u></p><p><strong><em>Spina</em></strong><em> </em>(L. n.), spinal column</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:51:15',NULL,NULL),(25207,2538,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SubSpina </em></strong><em>Lay down on your back. figuratively, “the spine is under”</em> the body</p><p><br></p><p>Compound of:<strong> <em>Sub Spina</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sub</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Spina</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:51:44',NULL,NULL),(25208,2539,14,NULL,'<p>PRONATOR</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:52:05',NULL,NULL),(25209,2539,13,NULL,'<p>Muscles in the forearm that rotates the forearm-hand anteriorly; or superiorly when elbows are flexed at 90 degrees (Think.: driving a screw in with a screw driver.)&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:52:12',NULL,NULL),(25210,2539,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Supinare </em></strong>(L. v.), to lie on one’s back;</p><p><strong><em>Supinatum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), laid on back</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:52:23',NULL,NULL),(25211,2539,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Supinator</em></strong><em> </em>muscle that <em>“drives the screw in”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Supinat- -or</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Supinatum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-or </em></strong><em>suffix: denotes agent of action</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:52:47',NULL,NULL),(25212,2540,14,NULL,'<p>ANTAGONIST</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:53:07',NULL,NULL),(25213,2540,13,NULL,'<p>Muscles that are co-contracting with Agonist Muscle to add strength.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:53:16',NULL,NULL),(25214,2540,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Syn</em></strong><em> </em>(Gr. prep.), with</p><p><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong><em> </em>(L. n.), work</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:53:26',NULL,NULL),(25215,2540,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>SynErgist</em></strong><em> </em>metaphorically, <em>“co- worker”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of: </em><strong><em>Syn Erg- -ist</em></strong></p><p><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em><strong><em>Syn </em></strong><em>Ergderived from </em><strong><em>Ergon</em></strong></p><p><em>·&nbsp;</em><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ist </em></strong><em>suffix: proponent of a cause (ex., activ-ist)</em></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:54:13',NULL,NULL),(25216,2541,14,NULL,'<p>CORONAL PLANE, SAGITTAL PLANE</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:54:42',NULL,NULL),(25217,2541,13,NULL,'<p>Imaginary Anatomical Plane cutting across the longitude of body or limb.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:54:48',NULL,NULL),(25218,2541,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Trans</em></strong><em> </em>(L. prep.), across, cross-section</p><p><strong><em>Vertere</em></strong><em> </em>(L. v.), to twist, bend;</p><p><strong><em>Versum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), twisted, bent</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:55:05',NULL,NULL),(25219,2541,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>TransVerse</em></strong><em> literally, “across”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of:</em><strong><em> Trans Verse</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trans</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Versum</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:55:34',NULL,NULL),(25220,2542,14,NULL,'<p>VARUS</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:57:26',NULL,NULL),(25221,2542,13,NULL,'<p>Knock–kneed: exaggerated bend of the knee joint to mid-sagittal plane.&nbsp;</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:57:32',NULL,NULL),(25222,2542,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Valgus, -a, -um </em></strong>(L. adj.), knock–kneed</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:57:41',NULL,NULL),(25223,2543,14,NULL,'<p>VALGUS</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:58:20',NULL,NULL),(25224,2543,13,NULL,'<p>Bow-legged; angle of knee has exaggerated curve away from the mid-sagittal plane.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:58:26',NULL,NULL),(25225,2543,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Varus, -a, -um </em></strong><em>(L adj.), bow-legged, knee angle bent sideward</em></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:58:37',NULL,NULL),(25226,2544,14,NULL,'<p>DORSAL or POSTERIOR</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:59:47',NULL,NULL),(25227,2544,13,NULL,'<p>a.k.a., ANTERIOR; front aspect.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 03:59:54',NULL,NULL),(25228,2544,8,NULL,'<p>(plu., <em>Ventres</em>), classically, stomach, womb</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:00:00',NULL,NULL),(25229,2544,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ventral </em></strong>literally, front side, stomach</p><p><br></p><p>Compound of: <strong><em>Venter -al</em></strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<em>Venter </em></strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<strong><em>-al </em></strong>suffix: forms adj.</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:00:36',NULL,NULL),(25234,4215,14,NULL,'<p>RELAXATION</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:14:07',NULL,NULL),(25235,4215,13,NULL,'<p>Electrical Resting Membrane Potential is Depolarized by an Action Potential leading to shortening of muscle fibers, causing movement.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:14:15',NULL,NULL),(25236,4215,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Contrahaere</em></strong><em> </em>(L. v.), to draw together;</p><p><strong><em>Contractum</em></strong><em> </em>(past part.), drawn together</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:14:27',NULL,NULL),(25237,4215,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Contraction</em></strong>, literally, <em>“shortening”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>Compound of:</em><strong><em> Contract- -ion</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Contractum</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ion</em>, </strong>suffix: forms noun of action</p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:14:52',NULL,NULL),(25238,4216,13,NULL,'<p>Literally, flexor <em>“of the sole of the foot”</em>.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:16:15',NULL,NULL),(25239,4216,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Plantae</em></strong><em> </em>Translation,<em> “of the sole”</em> (possessive form) </p><p><strong><em>Planta </em></strong>(L. n.), sole</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-11 04:16:35',NULL,NULL),(25240,4217,13,NULL,'<p>(TENSOR FASCIAE LATAE), fascia-like muscle to stabilize knee flexion / extension. Membranous fascia-like muscle on the lateral thigh for stabilizing knee joint; literal translation: Tensor muscle&nbsp;of the Side Fascia.</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-14 23:58:15',NULL,NULL),(25241,4217,8,NULL,'<p><strong>  <em>Latus, -a, -um</em></strong><em> </em>(L. adj.) wide, side</p><p><strong><em>Latae</em></strong><em> “of the side”</em> (possessive form, <strong><em>Lata</em></strong>)</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-01-14 23:58:43',NULL,NULL),(25250,2446,18,NULL,NULL,5,0,'https://scontent.fcgy1-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/489819803_1338572164075791_4033147782344121708_n.jpg?_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=f727a1&_nc_eui2=AeHdhOavo87U9Oog2Od6l0WILHcazhLr8VQsdxrOEuvxVMBqtX6y1pdinQmhTMkAiM7SbGC3dSRU2fJ1qpECmq4e&_nc_ohc=7TCUlMl8XlsQ7kNvwEDqfvL&_nc_oc=Adk7pGdFLIVzeuW-B_nqNB2itsM3UymqHzuhEZve-ykU9HVdzYKhxQPp7k7r1JYFT60&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy1-1.fna&_nc_gid=ghNtLJJ-j9JMAM_CpueAsw&oh=00_AfECT0L5SjXuHrXj_n2uFf0WEzY9BpAM9dpLX2BD1AMYSw&oe=67FE586A',16,'2025-04-11 01:38:34',16,'2025-04-11 04:31:39'),(25251,2443,18,NULL,NULL,4,0,'https://scontent.fcgy1-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/489808744_1338572144075793_6275229580528876921_n.jpg?_nc_cat=111&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=f727a1&_nc_eui2=AeGk801o702hrZdTj1Il5jW2asjYvvxG0PhqyNi-_EbQ-Njv6AmQ--q0T1JzErKWnt0sBlvhPCbRnuWHEsErk4N0&_nc_ohc=8O0x-Rq2kpUQ7kNvwEhKUqS&_nc_oc=Adl9YZarXsqRtSDf8Y-r1ABvjm94dBWPxiXpwv2cWI90HY5xENedLux9zFtJuskvA6o&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy1-1.fna&_nc_gid=toJNX0