><em>muscle that wrinkles above the eyebrows</em></p><p>·&nbsp;<u>CORRUGATOR</u><em>, muscle that wrinkles</em></p><p>·&nbsp;<u>SUPER- + CILII</u><em>, above the eyebrows</em></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:02:24',NULL,NULL),(25463,4219,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Corrugare</em></strong>&nbsp;(L v.), to wrinkle up;</p><p><strong><em>Corrugatum</em></strong>&nbsp;(past part.), wrinkled up</p><p><strong><em>-or</em></strong>&nbsp;(suffix), denotes agent of action</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Super</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. adj.), above, high</p><p><strong><em>Cilium</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Cilia</em></strong>), hair</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:02:43',NULL,NULL),(25464,4220,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Attachment between cardiac muscles with strong adhesive glycoproteins that bind heart muscle cells to one another, equipped with intermediate filaments that extend into the cytoplasm of the cells; enhances intercellular communications.</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:05:57',NULL,NULL),(25465,4220,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Desmus&nbsp;</em></strong>(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Desmoses</em></strong>), fastening chain, binding tie</p><p><strong><em>Soma</em></strong>&nbsp;(Gr. n.), body</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:06:14',NULL,NULL),(25467,4220,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Desmosome,</em></strong></p><p><em>Metaphorically</em><strong><em>,&nbsp;</em></strong><em>“binding tie body”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,&nbsp;<u>Desmo- + -some</u></em></p><ul><li><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;Desmoses</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;-some&nbsp;</em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em>&nbsp;Soma</em></strong></li></ul><p><br></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:11:22',NULL,NULL),(25468,4221,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">a group of muscle or nerve fiber&nbsp;</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:12:31',NULL,NULL),(25469,4221,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Fasciculus</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. n.), literally,&nbsp;<em>“a small bundle”</em></p><p>Metaphor for bundled group of muscles or nerves</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:12:47',NULL,NULL),(25470,4222,15,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">&nbsp;Coracoid&nbsp;</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:13:28',NULL,NULL),(25471,4222,7,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Prominent bone projection</span></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:13:38',NULL,NULL),(25472,4222,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Anteriorly directed process of the Scapula; origination for short head Biceps Muscle.&nbsp;</span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:13:46',NULL,NULL),(25473,4222,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Corax</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Coraces</em></strong>), classically,&nbsp;<em>“raven or crow”</em>;</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">the beak of the bird is metaphor for Coracoid Process</p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:13:54',16,'2025-08-16 02:14:08'),(25474,4222,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Coracoid</em></strong>,</p><p>simile,&nbsp;<em>“like the beak of crow, or raven”</em></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><br></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>comp.,&nbsp;<u>Coraco- + -oid</u></em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>Coraco-&nbsp;</em></strong><em>derived from</em><strong><em>&nbsp;Coraces</em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-oid</em></strong>&nbsp;(suffix), forms simile,&nbsp;<em>“like . . .”</em></p><p><br></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:14:30',NULL,NULL),(25475,4223,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Enzyme that neutralizes the action of Acetylcholine terminating Action Potential.&nbsp;</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:16:14',NULL,NULL),(25476,4223,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Acetum&nbsp;</em></strong>(L. n.), classically: vinegar, acid,<em>&nbsp;“wine turned sour”</em></p><p><strong><em>Choline</em></strong>, Quaternary Ammonium Cation; Vit. B complex, Lecithin</p><p><strong><em>-ester</em></strong>, denotes action of acid + alcohol, removing H2O&nbsp;</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:16:23',NULL,NULL),(25477,4223,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AcetylCholinEsterase</em></strong>,</p><p>Enzyme, neutralizing&nbsp;<strong><em>Acetylcholine.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em>&nbsp;<u>Acet-</u></em></strong><u>&nbsp;</u><strong><u>+&nbsp;</u><em><u>-yl + Choline + -ase</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Acetum</em></strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em><strong><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>-yl</em></strong>&nbsp;(Biochemistry), suffix, denotes free radicals</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Choline</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>-ester</em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>-ase</em></strong>, suffix, denotes enzyme</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:16:37',NULL,NULL),(25478,4224,15,NULL,'<p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Afferent</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:17:24',NULL,NULL),(25479,4224,7,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong>Neurons,</strong></p><p>Nerve cell</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:17:30',NULL,NULL),(25480,4224,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">a.k.a., AFFERENT TRACT / COLUMN / SENSORY NEURONS; Nerve Fibers carrying impulses from the Peripheral Nervous System to the spinal cord and brain, the Central Nervous System.</span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:17:38',NULL,NULL),(25481,4224,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. prep.), to, at, towards</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ferre</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. v.), to carry;</p><p><strong><em>Ferrentes</em></strong>&nbsp;(pres. part.), carrying&nbsp;</p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:18:29',NULL,NULL),(25482,4224,9,NULL,'<p><strong>AfFerrent</strong></p><p>literally, neurons “carrying to” the brain</p><p><br></p><p>comp.<strong>,&nbsp;<u>Af- + Ferrent</u></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Af</em>-</strong>&nbsp;derived.from<strong>&nbsp;Ad</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Ferrentes</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:18:39',NULL,NULL),(25483,4225,15,NULL,'<p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Afferent</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:19:16',NULL,NULL),(25484,4225,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Arteriole,</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">smallest diameter artery, larger than Capillary</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:19:26',NULL,NULL),(25485,4225,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Arteriole that enters the Renal Corpuscle, the Bowman’s Capsule, for filtering the blood through the Glomerular network</span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:19:34',NULL,NULL),(25486,4225,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Ad</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. prep.), to, at, towards</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 176, 240);\"><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Ferre</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. v.), to carry;</p><p><strong><em>Ferrentes</em></strong>&nbsp;(pres. part.), carrying&nbsp;</p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:19:44',NULL,NULL),(25487,4225,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>AfFerrent</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically,</em><strong><em>&nbsp;“</em></strong><em>carrying towards…</em>”</p><p><br></p><p>comp.,<strong><em>&nbsp;<u>Af-&nbsp;</u></em></strong><u>+&nbsp;</u><strong><em><u>Ferrent</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Af-</em></strong><em>&nbsp;derived from&nbsp;</em><strong><em>Ad</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ferrentes</em></strong></p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:19:54',NULL,NULL),(25488,4225,12,NULL,'<p><strong>AFFERENT</strong>&nbsp;COLUMN – NERVOUS SYSTEM</p><p><strong>AFFERENT</strong>&nbsp;FIBERS – NERVOUS SYSTEM</p><p><strong>AFFERENT</strong>&nbsp;TRACT – NERVOUS SYSTEM</p>',7,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:20:05',NULL,NULL),(25489,4226,15,NULL,'<p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Capillary&nbsp;</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:21:30',NULL,NULL),(25490,4226,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Action</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Observe how water behave in wet hair</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:21:38',NULL,NULL),(25491,4226,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">The O2, CO2, H2O, and nutrient gradient difference between the interstice and the bed of Arterioles and Venioles drives Capillary Action between the 2 compartments.</span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:21:46',NULL,NULL),(25492,4226,8,NULL,'<p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>Capillum</em></strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\"><em>Capilla</em></strong><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">), classically, “</span><em style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">strand of hair”</em></p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:21:58',NULL,NULL),(25493,4226,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Capillary,</em></strong></p><p><em>figuratively, functions like</em><strong><em>&nbsp;“</em></strong><em>hair-thin</em>” blood vessels</p><p><br></p><p>comp.,&nbsp;<strong><em><u>Capill- + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Capilla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ary</em></strong>&nbsp;(suffix), denotes function/location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:22:07',NULL,NULL),(25494,4227,13,NULL,'<p>The Force Pressure within the Glomerular Capillaries is 45mm which is higher than</p><p>most Capillaries.&nbsp;</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:22:37',NULL,NULL),(25495,4227,8,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>Glomerulus</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Glomeruli</em></strong>), small ball of yarn</p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\">diminutive of&nbsp;<strong><em>Glomus&nbsp;</em></strong>(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Glomeres</em></strong>), ball of yarn</p><p>Figurative for&nbsp;<em>“rolled up ball of capillary network”</em></p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:22:46',16,'2025-08-16 02:22:56'),(25496,4227,9,NULL,'<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">comp.,&nbsp;<strong><em><u>Glomerul- + -ar</u></em></strong></p><p class=\"ql-align-justify\"><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Glomerulus</em></strong></p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><em>-ar</em>&nbsp;</strong>(suffix), forms adj.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:24:24',NULL,NULL),(25497,4228,15,NULL,'<p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Medullary</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:24:51',NULL,NULL),(25498,4228,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Concentration Gradient,</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">differences of amount of Solute between 2 compartment</strong><strong>s</strong></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:24:58',NULL,NULL),(25499,4228,13,NULL,'<p>Concentrating urine (achieved by re-absorption of H2O from renal filtrate) occurs deeper into the Renal Medulla Interstitial Capillaries where Concentration of Solutes increases from 300 mOsm/kg in the Cortex to 1200 mOsm/kg Osmotic Pressure at the Apex of the Renal Pyramids. FYI:&nbsp;GRADIENT, difference in concentration of solutes between compartments separated by semi-permeable membrane; H2O gravitates to higher concentration.</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:25:08',16,'2025-08-16 02:25:41'),(25500,4228,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullus, -a, -um&nbsp;</em></strong>(L. adj.), small central part</p><p>Diminutive form of&nbsp;<strong><em>Medius</em></strong>&nbsp;(L. adj.), center</p><p>The&nbsp;<em>“small middle”</em>&nbsp;portion</p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:25:24',NULL,NULL),(25501,4228,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Medullary,</em></strong></p><p><em>Figuratively, “function of the small middle.”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,&nbsp;</em><strong><em><u>Medulla + -ary</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Medulla</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-ary</em></strong>&nbsp;(suffix), denotes function/location</p>',5,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:25:33',NULL,NULL),(25502,4229,15,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Apocrine</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:26:07',NULL,NULL),(25503,4229,13,NULL,'<p>Apocrine sweat glands are compound coiled tubular glands that drain into the hair Follicularopening of the Sebaceous Glands found in the axilla, genitalia and around the anus; secretions is influenced by the sex hormones.</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:26:25',NULL,NULL),(25504,4229,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Apos&nbsp;</em></strong>(Gr. n.), change, separation; ex., Apogee, Apology</p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong>&nbsp;(Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',3,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:27:17',NULL,NULL),(25505,4229,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>ApoCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>literally, “secretion of cell fragments breaking away”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em>&nbsp;<u>Apos&nbsp;</u></em></strong><u>+&nbsp;</u><strong><em><u>Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Apos</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Crinos</em></strong></p>',4,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:27:25',NULL,NULL),(25506,4230,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Sebaceous Glands of the skin is a Holocrine Gland because it sheds entire epithelial cells after accumulating secretory products in their cytoplasm, they rupture, and are secreted.</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:27:58',NULL,NULL),(25507,4230,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Holo</em></strong>&nbsp;(Gr. adj.), whole, entire, complete</p><p><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong>&nbsp;(Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:28:05',16,'2025-08-16 02:28:22'),(25508,4230,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>HoloCrinos</em></strong></p><p><em>metaphorically, “secretions of whole cell”</em></p><p><br></p><p><em>comp.,</em><strong><em>&nbsp;<u>Holo + Crinos</u></em></strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Holo</em></strong>&nbsp;(Gr. adj.), whole, entire, complete</p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em>·&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em>Crinos</em></strong>&nbsp;(Gr. n.), separation, secretion</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:28:13',NULL,NULL),(25509,4231,15,NULL,'<p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Mons</strong></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:28:50',NULL,NULL),(25510,4231,7,NULL,'<p><strong>Pubis</strong></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Of maturity</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Veneris</strong></p><p><em>“Of Venus”</em></p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:28:56',NULL,NULL),(25511,4231,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Poetically,&nbsp;</span><em style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">“Mountain of Puberty,”</em><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">&nbsp;</span><em style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">“Mountain of Venus”</em><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">; prominent mound over the Symphysis Pubis created by the union of Labia Majora.</span></p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:29:03',NULL,NULL),(25512,4231,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Mons</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Montes</em></strong>), mountain</p><p>Metaphor for the&nbsp;<em>“delta”</em>&nbsp;factor</p>',4,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:29:12',NULL,NULL),(25513,4232,13,NULL,'<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(239, 246, 255); color: rgb(51, 65, 85);\">Two entrance chambers into the heart: blood enters the right Atrium from Vena Cavas, superior and inferior; blood enters left Atrium from the lungs via the Pulmonary Veins.</span></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:30:04',NULL,NULL),(25514,4232,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Atrium</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Atria</em></strong>), classically, open air part of roof</p><p>of Roman villa, for rainwater collection</p><p>metaphor for blood pouring into the Atria</p><p>from Vena Cava and Pulmonary Veins</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:30:13',NULL,NULL),(25515,4233,13,NULL,'<p>ENGLISH TRANSLATION:</p><p><em>trumpeter muscle</em></p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:30:44',NULL,NULL),(25516,4233,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Buccinator</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Buccinatores</em></strong>), trumpeter</p><p><strong><em>Buccina</em></strong>&nbsp;(plu.,&nbsp;<strong><em>Buccinae</em></strong>), shepherd’s horn,<strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong>trumpet;</p><p>Think: blowing air into a ballon. blowing a horn</p><p><strong><em>-or</em></strong>&nbsp;(suffix), denotes agent of action</p>',2,1,NULL,16,'2025-08-16 02:30:55',NULL,NULL),(25518,4235,15,NULL,'<p>Barometric</p>',1,0,NULL,16,'2026-08-31 02:34:57',NULL,NULL),(25519,4235,13,NULL,'<p>Function for sensing high pressure within the circulatory system</p>',2,0,NULL,16,'2026-08-31 02:37:33',NULL,NULL),(25520,4235,8,NULL,'<p><strong><em>Baros </em></strong>(Gr. n.), weight, pressure</p><p><strong><em>Metrum</em></strong> (L. n.), measurement</p>',3,0,NULL,16,'2026-08-31 02:40:48',NULL,NULL),(25521,4235,9,NULL,'<p><strong><em>BaroMetric</em></strong></p><p>Literally, \'\'measurement of pressure\'\'</p><p><br></p><p>comp., <strong><em>Baro</em></strong> + <strong><em>Metr-</em></strong> + <strong><em>-ic</em></strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Baros</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Metrum</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>-ic</em></strong> (suffix), forms adj.; ability</li></ul>',4,0,NULL,16,'2026-08-31 02:45:25',16,'2026-08-31 02:47:05'),(25522,4236,13,'Chemoreceptor ',